Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:38:08-07:00","id":945206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945196#post945196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, another Kickstarter I'll end up spending $1000 on.<br /> <br /> Well, Mummy expansions weren't that much but still</div> </div> </div> </div>At least you have the luxury of spending a grand on a book. Some of us would kill to pull that off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:21:44-07:00","id":945251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945203#post945203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speak for yourself lol. The Canadian dollar had just tanked right before Dark Eras after being at parity with the USD. Exchange rate killed me. Worth every penny though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know your pain. I wish I weren't a completest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T23:27:35-07:00","id":945315,"title":"","content":"I'm reserving judgment on a crossover book, at least until we get some open development spoilers, which I assume will not be for quite a while.<br /> <br /> I'm unfortunately quite dubious that the subject can be satisfactorily handled in one book for around eleven major splats, even more minor supernaturals, and the myriad of other beings and dimensions that litter the CofD. I would sooner have no book than one that was bad or woefully incomplete and would likely generate more arguments that it would solve.<br /> <br /> I do hope, however, that the crossover section writers from the Demon Storyteller's Guide will be part of this project. The DSG crossover was some of the most creative and informative material I've read on the subject in all the recent nWOD/CofD WW books (and I'm not even a Demon fan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:11:01-07:00","id":945330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=944952#post944952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what questions is everyone hoping to see answered?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some things I'm hoping are covered or clarified:<br /> 1) Simple one, I wanna know if Mages can use other Supernaturals as sleepwalkers since they technically count as them (with regards to keeping Spell Control for them).<br /> 2) New rules for other supers in the Hedge, if the Hedge book doesn't cover that. I'd also love to see an example of a spirit/ghost halfway into the process of essence being replaced by glamour...<br /> 3) Some clarification about how Predatory Aura and Hunter's Aspect interact. Vampire implies they can sense werewolves' aura almost as easily as another vampire's, but then Werewolf utterly ignores how Hunter's Aspect interacts with other auras, or if werewolves can detect vampires.<br /> 4) Like someone else mentioned about Packs, I'm similarly curious if there might be similar benefits to those joining other supernatural 'circles'.<br /> <br /> Though while you can easily cover a chapter with mechanics questions, I hope that more of the book is focused on setting, story ideas, and NEW mechanics (things like Z-splats or similar focused on other supernaturals, for instance, or perhaps even new systems for what happens when X and Y try to do Z to combine their abilities, and of course more typical powers aimed towards crossover).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:26:53-07:00","id":945338,"title":"","content":"The Crossover Chronicle is going to provide story context for the different monsters interacting. We'll be dealing with mechanics and answering rules interaction questions, but it's not exclusively a rulebook.<br /> <br /> No developer has been contracted yet. As CofD lead, I'll be heavily involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:28:33-07:00","id":945341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945338#post945338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crossover Chronicle is going to provide story context for the different monsters interacting. We'll be dealing with mechanics and answering rules interaction questions, but it's not exclusively a rulebook.<br /> <br /> No developer has been contracted yet. As CofD lead, I'll be heavily involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, that's what I was hoping to hear. About the first part, I mean, having rules interactions but focusing more on story and ideas.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the answer on the second bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:57:05-07:00","id":945350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945338#post945338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crossover Chronicle is going to provide story context for the different monsters interacting. We'll be dealing with mechanics and answering rules interaction questions, but it's not exclusively a rulebook.<br /> <br /> No developer has been contracted yet. As CofD lead, I'll be heavily involved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It sounds good, but I hope you're not underestimating the amount of new and expanded mechanics that will be necessary for so many different types of supernaturals, major and minor, to interact as you suggest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T02:05:49-07:00","id":945364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945350#post945350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It sounds good, but I hope you're not underestimating the amount of new and expanded mechanics that will be necessary for so many different types of supernaturals, major and minor, to interact as you suggest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills is at least a core rule now, so that significantly reduces the number of weird edge cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T04:44:45-07:00","id":945401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945315#post945315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope, however, that the crossover section writers from the Demon Storyteller's Guide will be part of this project. The DSG crossover was some of the most creative and informative material I've read on the subject in all the recent nWOD/CofD WW books (and I'm not even a Demon fan).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing against the people that worked on it (and indeed there was much content in the ST Guide that was enjoyable and worthy of praise), but on my part I hope that some of the writing in that book is not ever repeated or used as an example. Hence my wariness for this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-07-2016, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T06:24:17-07:00","id":945428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945401#post945401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing against the people that worked on it (and indeed there was much content in the ST Guide that was enjoyable and worthy of praise), but on my part I hope that some of the writing in that book is not ever repeated or used as an example. Hence my wariness for this project.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be the masterpiece that was the Demon Translation Guide. Seriously, it's such a no-nonsense but well put together product that it is a shame that it is stuck as something so relatively niche. The Storyteller's Guide had some good stuff and probably the best possible way I can interpret this project is if we get the DTG and DSG calibre stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:20:41-07:00","id":945590,"title":"","content":"Extremely excited for this project. While some mechanical guidance will be appreciated. I am particularly looking forward to writing on the crossroads where the themes of each splat meet and hopefully some oddball ideas as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:26:03-07:00","id":945595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945590#post945590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extremely excited for this project. While some mechanical guidance will be appreciated. I am particularly looking forward to writing on the crossroads where the themes of each splat meet and hopefully some oddball ideas as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a longtime staunch opponent of crossover on the grounds that the themes of each line often get muddled, I'm really excited to see some strong advice on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:32:33-07:00","id":945599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945595#post945595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a longtime staunch opponent of crossover on the grounds that the themes of each line often get muddled, I'm really excited to see some strong advice on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't like crossover in the WoD. Mostly on mechanical grounds, and a very close second to the gonzo moments in WoD being ruthlessly exploited by some of the most cringeworthy LARPers I've had the misfortune of playing with a long time ago. Thankfully ChroD hasn't engendered those responses in me so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:04:25-07:00","id":945611,"title":"","content":"Well. I hope it's good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T17:34:24-07:00","id":945765,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I'd love to see something more like Monte Cook's World of Darkness or Dresden Files, where things are simplified / standardized enough that you can have multiple splats interacting without having to sort through a massive pile of rules. Well, this is from the guy that can't even master one set of CoD rules so take this with a grain of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T17:45:15-07:00","id":945770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945765#post945765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I'd love to see something more like Monte Cook's World of Darkness or Dresden Files, where things are simplified / standardized enough that you can have multiple splats interacting without having to sort through a massive pile of rules. Well, this is from the guy that can't even master one set of CoD rules so take this with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want anything ever like Monte Cook's World of Darkness ever again. That book was genuinely awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:00:12-07:00","id":945776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945206#post945206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least you have the luxury of spending a grand on a book. Some of us would kill to pull that off.</div> </div> </div> </div>My partner doesn't know how much I've spent on any Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Uh...including the Conan board game and RPG, and both Cthulhu Wars runs. Not bragging, just...hoping she doesn't find out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:15:35-07:00","id":945779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945590#post945590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extremely excited for this project. While some mechanical guidance will be appreciated. I am particularly looking forward to writing on the crossroads where the themes of each splat meet and hopefully some oddball ideas as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Part of making cross-overs work, to me, is finding the middle ground between the various splats. Sure, you could potentially have your Mage cabal run into a pack of werewolves while investigating some spirit activity and have to adjust, but you are viewing them through the lens of a Mage as secondary characters in a Mage Chronicle. A Chronicle where Mages and Werewolves are looking at the world together through a shared Chronicle is going to be a different beast by necessity. Advice on how to do Chronicles that aren't merely, &quot;You play as Splat X, there are some members of Splat Y and Splat Z around, but they aren't really crucial to the plot&quot; but actually, &quot;You can choose between Splats X, Y, and Z, each of them is equally important to the Chronicle&quot; and where the thematic middle-ground between two (or three, or four, or...) game lines would be fantastic. <br /> <br /> Beast has an easier time with cross-overs because it has both crunch and fluff dedicated to explaining how to interact with other splats. The Pack for Werewolf did a nice job of discussing how a vampire or mage might join up with a werewolf pack, what their role might be within it, and what the potential problems of such arrangements are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:49:41-07:00","id":945845,"title":"","content":"Considering that this doesn't look to be an alt system reimagining of elements of Chronicles of Darkess I don't think you're going to see anything like the Monte Cook book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:34:52-07:00","id":946014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945770#post945770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want anything ever like Monte Cook's World of Darkness ever again. That book was genuinely awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I liked it as a cute re-interpretation of some of the core splats, but I would never want to play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:31:22-07:00","id":946152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945845#post945845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that this doesn't look to be an alt system reimagining of elements of Chronicles of Darkess I don't think you're going to see anything like the Monte Cook book.</div> </div> </div> </div> I imagine it might take its que from the God-Machine Chronicles, so that the basic framework is the same but it might add elements that might not be for every group much less every game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:13:33-07:00","id":946210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945765#post945765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I'd love to see something more like Monte Cook's World of Darkness or Dresden Files, where things are simplified / standardized enough that you can have multiple splats interacting without having to sort through a massive pile of rules. Well, this is from the guy that can't even master one set of CoD rules so take this with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started out gaming in D&amp;D &amp; d20 systems, so I enjoyed Monte Cook's World of Darkness. Even started working on a 5th edition d&amp;d setting &amp; homebrew rules for Chronicles of Darkness 2nd Edition stuff, just for fun lol. Given that this is to be a Chronicles of Darkness Crossover though, I think we're more likely to stay in the CoD rules &amp; general setting, but perhaps some advice on multi-splat group dynamic &amp; beat/experience gaining (seeing how a mixed group could be both a pack &amp; a throng, while also a motley &amp; cabal &amp; krewe in mechanical terms &amp; narrative terms). I for one am really interested in the possibility of narrative suggestions for how to describe different splats' auras to supernatural senses &amp; what happens if x-type blood is consumed by Kindred &amp; what pitfalls would happen if a Changeling entered x-type's dreams or harvested their emotions for Glamour (if possible). the common Clash of Wills &amp; allowing Supernatural Strength stats to be added to resist supernatural effects helps pave the way for a common rule set, as does the commonly held Merits across the books &amp; the anchors (either virtue/vice, dirge/mask, bone/blood, ellipsis/torment, mein/masque*, life/legend, and whatever Sin-Eaters &amp; Deviants will use lol), and the common experience costs of attributes, merits, &amp; skills/specialties. I have high hopes for a rollicking good time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:53:14-07:00","id":946334,"title":"","content":"11 splats?<br /> <br /> Changeling 1, Werewolf 2, Mages 3, Vampires 4, Prommie 5, Giest 6, Mummy 7, Hunter 8, Demon 9, Beast 10, Deviant 11.<br /> <br /> Okay I was miscounting I kept coming up with 10 for some reason.<br /> <br /> One problem I foresee is that Mummy is 1e, all the rest are either started at 2e, skipping 1e, or are on their second edition.<br /> <br /> Giest is getting a 2e, but Mummy 2e has not been announced yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:33:06-07:00","id":946373,"title":"","content":"I look forward to using this book to further develop my unified crossover history of the Chronicles of Darkness universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:24:31-07:00","id":946731,"title":"","content":"I'm desperately hoping that the words &quot;Monte&quot; and &quot;Dresden&quot; come up as infrequently as possible. Same with &quot;princess&quot; and &quot;dragon&quot;. And Mage, if we could dream, but such are but fancies. <br /> <br /> I'm curious, is this going to be an &quot;alternate universe&quot; book? The description in the brochure gave me that initial impression: that it describes an alternate way to play Chronicles of Darkness with setting and mechanic alterations that lead to different supernatural beings interacting with each other much more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:41:36-07:00","id":946736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=946731#post946731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm desperately hoping that the words &quot;Monte&quot; and &quot;Dresden&quot; come up as infrequently as possible. Same with &quot;princess&quot; and &quot;dragon&quot;. And Mage, if we could dream, but such are but fancies.<br /> <br /> I'm curious, is this going to be an &quot;alternate universe&quot; book? The description in the brochure gave me that initial impression: that it describes an alternate way to play Chronicles of Darkness with setting and mechanic alterations that lead to different supernatural beings interacting with each other much more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just that the default assumption for the average chronicle (and the view that most books take) is that whatever gameline being discussed is the only one with only rare subtle nods to others, like how Hunter makes sure to stress that your vampires aren't necessarily Kindred or how Werewolf doesn't take about specific Mage Orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:54:43-07:00","id":946739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945595#post945595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a longtime staunch opponent of crossover on the grounds that the themes of each line often get muddled, I'm really excited to see some strong advice on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience that's a problem with free-range crossovers, but you can do very strong thematic narratives where characters are limited to two or so splats with a game exploring some hook of their interaction/overlap.<br /> <br /> Also there are certain combos where a different supernatural type makes for a strong antagonist for a different game line. I'm particularly a fan of using Mages as antagonists for game lines where the hook is that theMage is more overtly powerful in a given domain but understands it less well than the domain's &quot;natives&quot; and is dangerously mucking with powers beyond their ken. The most obvious candidates for this dynamic are Werewolves vs Spirit-Mage, Changelings vs Fate-Mage, and Sin-Eaters vs Death-Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-09-2016, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:59:30-07:00","id":946740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=946736#post946736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's just that the default assumption for the average chronicle (and the view that most books take) is that whatever gameline being discussed is the only one with only rare subtle nods to others, like how Hunter makes sure to stress that your vampires aren't necessarily Kindred or how Werewolf doesn't take about specific Mage Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, exactly. Each game takes place in its own little universe to some degree. I'm wondering how much TCC is going to push that, if it's explicitly going to say &quot;this is an alternate way the ChroD world could be&quot; and not &quot;this is how it actually is&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T23:14:32-07:00","id":946763,"title":"","content":"I can't wait for the book to come out. I've been doing crossover games for some time now. I'm running a world of darkness world where every line exist and its been. If these rules help wit things I did not think of before that would be interesting. I've been finding it interesting having demons and Promethean's interact with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:55:11-07:00","id":946973,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there will be a kickstarter and if so what the stretch goals will be (perhaps city books like Mummy got DC and Rio).<br /> <br /> So here is what I think will be in the book. <br /> <br /> Interacting Cosmologies. How different cosmologies fit with each other, how splat interact with the inhabitants of other cosmologies and their enviroments.<br /> <br /> How powers of one splat effect another, including feeding off each other.<br /> <br /> Plothooks, perhaps divided by combinations of splats.<br /> <br /> Mixed Themes, example mixing the themes of Mage and Changelings.<br /> <br /> Mutual Antagonists, horror and such that fit a variety of campaigns.<br /> <br /> Crossover crunch like new merits.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a lesser template or templates that encourages Crossover Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Sample Cities, perhaps popular settings from other core books, like Toronto, Montreal, Toyko, Las Vegas, London, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:20:52-07:00","id":946992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=946973#post946973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there will be a kickstarter and if so what the stretch goals will be (perhaps city books like Mummy got DC and Rio).</div> </div> </div> </div>So far all the new games have had Kickstarters. Beast, Mummy, Demon. I'd be willing to back this for a lot, I like the concept and trust Dave to make it cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:26:52-07:00","id":947001,"title":"","content":"Here's my fringe hope: ChroD Kiasyd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:41:35-07:00","id":947019,"title":"","content":"Just the thought of this book has made me ponder starting another MUSH. I miss Crescent City. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:32:57-07:00","id":947527,"title":"","content":"So we're dealing with these Chronicles of Darkness where a diverse population of monsters are hiding in the shadows, conducting their affairs away from mortal eyes\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026and said supernatural entities cluster together, each into its own shadow society that exists in parallel to the others and largely ignorant of each others. <br /> <br /> Right. That seems rather unlikely. What seems more likely is that you'd end up with troupes and organizations with mixed populations but shared themes. I'd like to see advice on how to set up a unified \u201cshadow government\u201d in a city that polices <i>all</i> of the Night Folk living there, rather than assuming that vampires police vampires, werewolves police werewolves, mages police mages, etc. I'd like to see advice for putting together, say, a group of changelings and Sin-Eaters (a \u201cmotley krewe\u201d). I'd like to see advice for \u201cintertype y-splats\u201d that can be used to help fight the thematic muddying that crossovers tend to cause, by gathering in one place subgroups of all of the supernatural types who share common themes. <br /> <br /> I'd like to see more crossover-based elements for each supernatural type: Bloodlines and Disciplines that riff off of the animistic metaphysics of the Uratha or the cosmology of the Lost; Lodges and Rites that allow one to maintain the balance of the ghostly denizens in the Packs Territory; Legacies based on the Were-Hekau with Attainments aligning with the Arisen Pillars; Entitlements and Contracts by which changelings can contact the Moire and Anachronisms of the Arcadian Witches; and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:36:00-07:00","id":947529,"title":"","content":"When this comes out, I might make an appendix to it that deals with Transgression and The Lightning Chronicle, or a &quot;mod&quot; that swaps out parts related to Awakening. Those documents are already going to have substantial sections on crossovers (and making those viable was a conscious aspect of their development), so it shouldn't be too hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:52:17-07:00","id":947539,"title":"","content":"If anything, I'd like to focus crossover on a primarily thematic axis. Say you're looking at blending Promethean with Vampire and/or Mummy; the game becomes a reflection on what humanity means to those who covet it and to those who have left it behind, and that's the kind of thing you can build your chronicle out from. Demon and Changeling both share ideas of being hunted, living behind masks, and paranoia, so how can that inform a cohesive story as a structure. It's easy for obvious fits like those, but my mind kind of boggles when we try to do, say, Promethean and Beast, or Mummy and Demon. <br /> <br /> This might also be a lovely chance at some updates to 2e and some new content; the Dead Wolves bloodline or Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches entitlement have few better places to see conversion than in a dedicated book for it, and things like a fae-focused Lodge would be welcome additions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:13:12-07:00","id":947553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=947539#post947539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I'd like to focus crossover on a primarily thematic axis. Say you're looking at blending Promethean with Vampire and/or Mummy; the game becomes a reflection on what humanity means to those who covet it and to those who have left it behind, and that's the kind of thing you can build your chronicle out from. Demon and Changeling both share ideas of being hunted, living behind masks, and paranoia, so how can that inform a cohesive story as a structure. It's easy for obvious fits like those, but my mind kind of boggles when we try to do, say, Promethean and Beast, or Mummy and Demon. <br /> <br /> This might also be a lovely chance at some updates to 2e and some new content; the Dead Wolves bloodline or Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches entitlement have few better places to see conversion than in a dedicated book for it, and things like a fae-focused Lodge would be welcome additions.</div> </div> </div> </div>*cracks knuckles* Promethean and Beast would be about being caught between extremes, at least for the Promethean. Defy your nature or embrace it? The Beast outlook might make a Promethean consider whether or not their state might actually be &quot;natural&quot; in some way and not innately harmful to the world. Of course, the natural order espoused by Beasts is a fairly dark and brutal one, so there's another line of contention. I don't really think Mummies have left humanity behind as much as Beasts have, after all: Mummies don't tend to revel in their condition the way Beasts do, since theirs can't really be described as anything other than a curse. <br /> <br /> Mummy and Demon would be about discovery and mystery. Each side would have the experience of realizing that the world is much larger and much stranger than you ever imagined: an experience that's much more impactful when you're an ancient supernatural being. Mummy's theme of &quot;realizing that you're being dicked over by ancient malevolent forces&quot; has a fair bit of overlap with Demon's, and the techgnosticism of Demon can represent the future shock and time displacement that frequently comes up in Mummy: the Arisen dealing with an incredibly strange and confusing world that often seems to have left them behind. <br /> <br /> And yes on the crossover splats. I've already mentioned Kiasyd, but there's so much more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T04:32:54-07:00","id":947662,"title":"","content":"I've actually run a crossover &quot;chat&quot; before that was based around the typical organizations not being present, and instead a sort of 'council' of various supernaturals existed, mostly to make sure the Masquerade/equivalent was in place and that nobody fucked with each other too much. Then, to give people reasons to actually interact, there were two 'crossover splats'.<br /> <br /> The first was called 'Influence', and it was the realm or supernatural focus your character had. If you took Influence (Shadow) you had some bonuses dealing with spirits and their realm, AND you could recognize others with the same influence (It was a merit).<br /> <br /> You then had Guilds, which were more of an organizational type thing, obviously, and focused on the same sorts of things your typical y-splats deal with, like you had those that focused on mortal interactions, a guild of police-y types (obviously worked closely with the council), a mysterium-like organization, and a few others. Obviously, the typical y splats for those that had them based organizationally weren't much present, making it so if you wanted support, you joined a guild instead. (Vamps could also access blood magic more easily, but generally only a single type)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T06:02:14-07:00","id":947706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=947539#post947539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I'd like to focus crossover on a primarily thematic axis. Say you're looking at blending Promethean with Vampire and/or Mummy; the game becomes a reflection on what humanity means to those who covet it and to those who have left it behind, and that's the kind of thing you can build your chronicle out from. Demon and Changeling both share ideas of being hunted, living behind masks, and paranoia, so how can that inform a cohesive story as a structure. It's easy for obvious fits like those, but my mind kind of boggles when we try to do, say, Promethean and Beast, or Mummy and Demon. <br /> <br /> This might also be a lovely chance at some updates to 2e and some new content; the Dead Wolves bloodline or Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches entitlement have few better places to see conversion than in a dedicated book for it, and things like a fae-focused Lodge would be welcome additions.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Briar Wolves Lodge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:19:08-07:00","id":948950,"title":"","content":"What do you guys want to see in the Crossover Chronicles?<br /> <br /> And how big should book be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T18:56:47-07:00","id":949000,"title":"","content":"My Wishlist (as a Storyteller that doesn't really like Crossover because of the added complications).<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics</b><br /> <i><b>Cross-Template Powers:</b></i> I really like Disciplines, Gifts, Contracts and such lets A Template dabble in another templates domain. At least one example per template.<br /> <i><b>Cross - Over System Hacks:</b></i> Ways to modify the game mechanics that smooths over the rough edges when power collide. something a bit more in depth than just declaring a &quot;Clash of Wills&quot;.<br /> <i><b>Cross - Over Merits: </b></i>I could easily see an Ambassador merit that lets an outsider count as a member of that template socially. Beasts already have this to a degree, but have ways to extend it to the other Template would be excellent.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling</b><br /> <i><b>Shadow Society: </b></i>This was mentioned up thread, but a chronicle where all the supernaturals in a domain answer to the same authority would be very fun. Examples could show how different ruling parties could operate ( a council of representative from each Template all the way to a single powerful ruler). <br /> <b><i>The Band:</i> </b>Running a group comprised of multiple templates, with several example groups. Expanding on material in &quot;The Pack&quot; with more detail and from the perspective of the other supernaturals.<br /> <i><b>Common Enemies: </b></i>Explore how a supernatural would deal with the unique enemies of a different type of supernatural. What happens when Vampires encounter the Hosts, or a Changeling encounters one of the God Machines Angels, or when a Promethean gets tangles in a Seers plot.<br /> <i><b>Themes:</b></i> Unifying and combining the different (and occasionally conflicting) themes stressed by each line. Keep the focus on the CofD's genral philosophy to keep the interactions personal to the characters involved. Its all fine and good to think of the neat ways the assorted powers can interact, but why would these characters want to interact seems more important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T19:13:05-07:00","id":949011,"title":"","content":"A multi-splat shadow society would be fun, especially if it's set up either as a feudal deal or some sort of chaotic nightmare democracy. <br /> <br /> And part of me is kind of wondering if TCC is at least going to bring up the possibility of streamlining and paring down mechanics as much as possible and having all the splats use Dread Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T19:25:01-07:00","id":949023,"title":"","content":"It would be trivial to toss in a &quot;You count as Status 1 in another supernatural organization&quot; Merit somewhere, with the immortality-seeking Mage finding brotherhood among the Ordo Dracul and the Unfleshed unexpectedly welcome in the arms of the Spring Court. Maybe this comes at a cost - the Dragons want to many, many samples of Awakened blood, or the former slave finds themself entangled in chains of fae oaths - or maybe it's just a flat benefit gained form strange company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T07:39:49-07:00","id":949303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=949011#post949011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A multi-splat shadow society would be fun, especially if it's set up either as a feudal deal or some sort of chaotic nightmare democracy.<br /> <br /> And part of me is kind of wondering if TCC is at least going to bring up the possibility of streamlining and paring down mechanics as much as possible and having all the splats use Dread Powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> They'd have to come up with numbers for all the dread powers that aren't rated 1 to 5 though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:27:31-07:00","id":949389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=949023#post949023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be trivial to toss in a &quot;You count as Status 1 in another supernatural organization&quot; Merit somewhere, with the immortality-seeking Mage finding brotherhood among the Ordo Dracul and the Unfleshed unexpectedly welcome in the arms of the Spring Court. Maybe this comes at a cost - the Dragons want to many, many samples of Awakened blood, or the former slave finds themself entangled in chains of fae oaths - or maybe it's just a flat benefit gained form strange company.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a Hunter game featuring a full slate of supernatural NPCs I house ruled that the Court Goodwill merit from Changeling can be used by anyone for any supernaturally aware faction they aren't official member of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:27:54-07:00","id":949805,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, expanded variants of the primary Vampire covenants make pretty good ideas for universal supernatural social movements. If you lessen the Catholic paintjob on the Lance, you make a damn good umbrella for the Pure, some Guardians of the Veil, the Autumn and Winter Courts, a decent number of Arisen, and many Beasts, while boiling the Carthians down to &quot;cling to Humanity and destroy the Masquerade&quot; is applicable to every single gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:29:54-07:00","id":949808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=949805#post949805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, expanded variants of the primary Vampire covenants make pretty good ideas for universal supernatural social movements. If you lessen the Catholic paintjob on the Lance, you make a damn good umbrella for the Pure, some Guardians of the Veil, the Autumn and Winter Courts, a decent number of Arisen, and many Beasts, while boiling the Carthians down to &quot;cling to Humanity and destroy the Masquerade&quot; is applicable to every single gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would the Ordo fit into that, I wonder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:34:22-07:00","id":949810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=949808#post949808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would the Ordo fit into that, I wonder?</div> </div> </div> </div>As the posthumanist movement you seem to be agitating for; werewolves happily on the road to complete Spirit nature, potential and successful liches, some Created on the Refinement of Lead, Centimani, Alchemists, changelings who know what happens to Wyrd 10 and embrace it, Beasts well on the way to an Inheritance, suicidal Deviants on the road to Blowout...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:37:21-07:00","id":949813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=949810#post949810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As the posthumanist movement you seem to be agitating for; werewolves happily on the road to complete Spirit nature, potential and successful liches, some Created on the Refinement of Lead, Centimani, Alchemists, changelings who know what happens to Wyrd 10 and embrace it, Beasts well on the way to an Inheritance, suicidal Deviants on the road to Blowout...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see the Deviant connection. It'd be more likely to made up of Deviants who want a way to access blowout-level power without dying, or who want to better understand and control their conditions. From what's been said, a Deviant deliberately planning a Blowout is basically a suicide bomber.<br /> <br /> A cross-splat Ordo would probably do the &quot;help monsters be better monsters&quot; thing even better than Beasts, considering that the order has their whole network of laboratories and researchers looking for practical solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:41:07-07:00","id":949817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=949813#post949813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really see the Deviant connection. It'd be more likely to made up of Deviants who want a way to access blowout-level power without dying, or who want to better understand and control their conditions. From what's been said, a Deviant deliberately planning a Blowout is basically a suicide bomber.<br /> <br /> A cross-splat Ordo would probably do the &amp;quot;help monsters be better monsters&amp;quot; thing even better than Beasts, considering that the order has their whole network of laboratories and researchers looking for practical solutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a bad guess about a game that doesn't exist yet, so sorry for getting it wrong.<br /> <br /> An interesting line has to drawn between the Circle's &quot;revel in your monstrosity&quot; and the Ordo's &quot;surpass your capabilities.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:52:50-07:00","id":949825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=949817#post949817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a bad guess about a game that doesn't exist yet, so sorry for getting it wrong.<br /> <br /> An interesting line has to drawn between the Circle's &amp;quot;revel in your monstrosity&amp;quot; and the Ordo's &amp;quot;surpass your capabilities.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the line has always been that most of the Ordo use the &quot;better monster&quot; mostly as rhetoric and hyperbole, as a way to freak people out and sound badass. Most of them tend to see what they're doing in more practical terms: how can I be as immortal and as powerful and as not-terrible-drawback-having as possible? Sure, some of them might identify with the idea of the monster, and some of them put a &quot;we are the demons&quot; spin on the whole gnostic thing 2e gave them, but most of them don't really consider themselves monsters. The difference is, when the Circle talk about monsters they really tend to mean it, and the dominant philosophy there involves some degree of identification with monstrosity. Of course, you could draw another interesting parallel in that both of them tend to think, or try to think, in scientific terms detached from good and evil. The Circle teaches that vampires are natural, and are natural predators, while the order tends to approach things from a scientific, evolutionary viewpoint. Ironically, the order can be more mystical than the Circle: some Ordo members believe that their state is a curse from god and that what they do is an act of rebellion against him, while the Circle doesn't really believe in the abrahamic god at all and holds that vampirism is simply a natural feature of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T08:32:38-07:00","id":950049,"title":"","content":"I've been toying around with the idea of something like crossover-powers that are sort of like if a devotion or conjunctional spell required another supernatural ability to activate instead of just multiple of your own. It'd basically work how it sounds, allowing supernaturals who work together to find ways to combine their powers in various ways, and the exact effects could be anything from &quot;This happens if you use X immediate power and they use Y&quot; to something more like a Scale being combined with a Werewolf rite to produce some long term effect or experiment. Mages, who can already do just about anything, would benefit from things like a power that might normally need tons of reach having that be covered by the 'assistance', whereas most others benefit from doing something entirely new and probably more powerful than normal.<br /> <br /> So, basically would be nice to see some sort of system that covers different ways to combine supernatural powers, not as something anyone can do on their own, but to give crossover groups a little system to cover the inevitable &quot;What happens if he makes my skin wrap into a talen?&quot; and whatever else pops up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T12:29:16-07:00","id":950173,"title":"","content":"I think that Mage's Nameless Orders are the best possible cross splat originizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:59:48-07:00","id":950339,"title":"","content":"If there are sections for each splat, I might rewrite the Mage and Promethean sections when they come out to fit into the Pallid Data versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:47:54-07:00","id":950416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=947527#post947527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we're dealing with these Chronicles of Darkness where a diverse population of monsters are hiding in the shadows, conducting their affairs away from mortal eyes\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026and said supernatural entities cluster together, each into its own shadow society that exists in parallel to the others and largely ignorant of each others.<br /> <br /> Right. That seems rather unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your assumption is that the distribution of vectors for gregarious supernatural beings is both uniform and large enough for all of them to exist in every population center, sure.<br /> <br /> That's never actually been presented as the case, even before getting into how a variety of factors tend to prompt monsters who weren't made in a town to move there or conduct the bulk of their supernatural activity there (as with mages and vampires most commonly), or how some of those monsters interface with other dimensions in a fashion specifically designed to limit their influence (werewolves and Sin-Eaters, naturally), or how most of these monsters have a practical and/or metaphysical inclination towards secrecy as regards their magical nature (demons and changelings), or the matter of simple low numbers (Prometheans and Beasts and possibly mummies).<br /> <br /> The base state of a monster is solitude, and that doesn't shift readily to diving headfirst into the politics between four different societies messing with five different dimensions without the kind of specialized focus you go on to allude to, which itself constitutes both a dedication of precious inhuman resources and a potential liability with regards to secrecy and subversion.<br /> <br /> It doesn't take an egregious amount of effort for one group of monsters to discover a different group of monsters exists, yes. It also doesn't take even a significant amount of contemplation for one group of monsters to determine that, absent a collaboration or conflict of interests with that other group, they want as little involvement with that group as they can manage. Two or three groups of thirty or so people can manage pretty well in a decent-sized city without running afoul of each other in the course of pursuing their own agendas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:01:57-07:00","id":950422,"title":"","content":"Or to put it another way, not everyone is into anime conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:40:44-07:00","id":950451,"title":"","content":"I've always found the arguments for each type of supernatural sticking to its own kind to be less than compelling; but normally, they're just good enough for me to accept in order to facilitate an overall setting where each gameline <i>can</i> operate in isolation. That is, they strike me as rationalizations for a pre-ordained status quo rather than something from which the traditional status quo naturally derives. So if your goal is to avoid crossovers, the arguments that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> makes rationalize the \u201ceach unto its own\u201d conceit well enough. <br /> <br /> But this thread is about a recently announced book tentatively called <b>Crossover Chronicle</b>. The assumption here is that your goal is to <i>embrace</i> crossover; so the fig leaf excuses for why the city's vampires always seem to find each other but never seem to find the city's werewolves or mages? They're not needed here. Rather, the base assumption is that the city's supernatural community <i>is</i> aware of each other, and <i>doesn't</i> engage in willful blindness based on race (where the races are \u201cvampire\u201d, \u201cwerewolf\u201d, \u201cmage\u201d, etc.). Instead, divisions are more likely to be based on <i>interests</i>, with a vampiric practitioner of Cruac being more likely to hang with a Thyrsus shaman than with a vampire who's pursuing the Coils of the Dragon, or a Gangrel finding as much common ground with an Uratha pack than with a Ventrue and his political intrigue. Which, on a larger scale, implies sociopolitical structures where race is at most a secondary concern rather than being the dominant organizing principle: a mystical organization inclined to facilitate messy, carnal magics, for instance; or Pack-like gangs that are as likely to have Gangrel vampires and Beast changelings as Uratha in their hunting parties. <br /> <br /> In particular, mages and their addiction to mysteries run directly counter to the notion of each race existing in isolation from the others. The fact that the other supernaturals don't count as Sleepers where Supernal Magic is concerned means that the single most common reason for mages to maintain secrecy (the effects of the Sleeping Curse) doesn't apply to other supernaturals; and the fact that mages can earn arcane experience through encounters with other supernaturals means that they're not inclined to ignore them. <br /> <br /> In fact, they arguably rival Beasts for the position of most crossover-friendly type in the Chronicles of Darkness; and Beasts were <i>designed</i> with crossover-friendliness in mind. So much so that I think one of the main challenges for <b>Crossover Chronicle</b> will be to avoid the perception that it's a <b>Mage</b>-centric book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:56:51-07:00","id":950455,"title":"","content":"Flimsy barriers or not, the barriers must be understood before they can be broken to fully engage in the topic, in fairness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T23:01:15-07:00","id":950456,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting is that there's a certain amount of &quot;That's the point&quot; going on-the membrane between the games is supposed to be thick enough that not only can they be run in isolation of anything else, but sole existence(difference between werewolves existing but not being relevant in your vampire game vs there simply being no werewolves), but thin enough that you can break it down and make things messy as shit without much work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T00:57:17-07:00","id":950470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=950451#post950451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always found the arguments for each type of supernatural sticking to its own kind to be less than compelling; but normally, they're just good enough for me to accept in order to facilitate an overall setting where each gameline <i>can</i> operate in isolation. That is, they strike me as rationalizations for a pre-ordained status quo rather than something from which the traditional status quo naturally derives. So if your goal is to avoid crossovers, the arguments that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> makes rationalize the \u201ceach unto its own\u201d conceit well enough.<br /> <br /> But this thread is about a recently announced book tentatively called <b>Crossover Chronicle</b>. The assumption here is that your goal is to <i>embrace</i> crossover; so the fig leaf excuses for why the city's vampires always seem to find each other but never seem to find the city's werewolves or mages? They're not needed here. Rather, the base assumption is that the city's supernatural community <i>is</i> aware of each other, and <i>doesn't</i> engage in willful blindness based on race (where the races are \u201cvampire\u201d, \u201cwerewolf\u201d, \u201cmage\u201d, etc.). Instead, divisions are more likely to be based on <i>interests</i>, with a vampiric practitioner of Cruac being more likely to hang with a Thyrsus shaman than with a vampire who's pursuing the Coils of the Dragon, or a Gangrel finding as much common ground with an Uratha pack than with a Ventrue and his political intrigue. Which, on a larger scale, implies sociopolitical structures where race is at most a secondary concern rather than being the dominant organizing principle: a mystical organization inclined to facilitate messy, carnal magics, for instance; or Pack-like gangs that are as likely to have Gangrel vampires and Beast changelings as Uratha in their hunting parties.<br /> <br /> In particular, mages and their addiction to mysteries run directly counter to the notion of each race existing in isolation from the others. The fact that the other supernaturals don't count as Sleepers where Supernal Magic is concerned means that the single most common reason for mages to maintain secrecy (the effects of the Sleeping Curse) doesn't apply to other supernaturals; and the fact that mages can earn arcane experience through encounters with other supernaturals means that they're not inclined to ignore them.<br /> <br /> In fact, they arguably rival Beasts for the position of most crossover-friendly type in the Chronicles of Darkness; and Beasts were <i>designed</i> with crossover-friendliness in mind. So much so that I think one of the main challenges for <b>Crossover Chronicle</b> will be to avoid the perception that it's a <b>Mage</b>-centric book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed completely, especially on the Mage crossover point (though I think Deviant may rival them in crossover potential).<br /> <br /> One of the biggest hurdles running crossover is maintaining a sense of disconnect, explaining how different night denizens can remain blind to one another. Some are easy, like Demons* or Prometheans, while others are seriously hard, namely Mages and Werewolves (both being naturally talented at sniffing out the strange). I've added things to help, like all Diamond orders having a standing rule that Mages are <b>not</b> to let other supernaturals become aware of their existence, but that still leaves the Free Councils, Nameless Orders and random disparates to pal about. <br /> <br /> Even keeping the major supernatural splats low in numbers as I do, blurring of lines becomes inevitable. Some groups make this easy, the Ordo Dracul is a good example, being capable of embracing (no pun intended) many other splats in matched purpose. Others not so much, I found the Werewolf tribes especially difficult to manage (difficult enough to drop them entirely) what with their hunting focus and how certain supernaturals (cough Sin-Eaters cough) appear so much like prey. <br /> <br /> My solution to all of it is to keep things to their own story. Don't let anything get to global. But that's not something the book can do, so I'll be interested in seeing how it's all justified. Though, frankly I think people would be happiest with a branching option approach. Maybe four or five takes on the setting each with different core assumptions. That'd probably be the most agreeable handling of the material.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Demons are easy to keep hidden, what with Cover and all. And their espionage angle means its actually in theme for them to know more about other splats, and even infiltrate them.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T02:20:31-07:00","id":950482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=950470#post950470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others not so much, I found the Werewolf tribes especially difficult to manage (difficult enough to drop them entirely) what with their hunting focus and how certain supernaturals (cough Sin-Eaters cough) appear so much like prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Tribes of Moon are a bit more problem with their focus on Sacred Prey, but I think they can still easily join global factions. Let's see:<ul><li><b>Blood Talons </b>- 'Defenders' group. Probably the one with Adamantine Arrow, Ferrum Created and Summer Court.</li> <li><b>Bone Shadows</b> - 'Occult' groups. Joins Ordo Dracul, Circle of Crone, Mysterium, Argentum Created and Autumn Court.</li> <li><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - This Tribe will probably be hardest but I could see them as part of 'Secret' group and they will be there with Guardians of Veil and Winter Court. Maybe some Copprum Created will be added here.</li> <li><b>Iron Masters</b> - 'Modern Society' group members, with Carthain Movement, Free Council and Spring Court.</li> <li><b>Storm Lords</b> - 'Rulers' groups. With Invictus and Silver Ladder they lead supernatural to victory. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul>I think that first 5 games of <b>C</b><b>hronicles of Darkness </b>nicely mesh with each other, as they were written with basic concept of 5x5 model ( or rather division like I mentioned above ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T02:57:39-07:00","id":950488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=950482#post950482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Tribes of Moon are a bit more problem with their focus on Sacred Prey, but I think they can still easily join global factions. Let's see:<ul><li><b>Blood Talons </b>- 'Defenders' group. Probably the one with Adamantine Arrow, Ferrum Created and Summer Court.</li> <li><b>Bone Shadows</b> - 'Occult' groups. Joins Ordo Dracul, Circle of Crone, Mysterium, Argentum Created and Autumn Court.</li> <li><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - This Tribe will probably be hardest but I could see them as part of 'Secret' group and they will be there with Guardians of Veil and Winter Court. Maybe some Copprum Created will be added here.</li> <li><b>Iron Masters</b> - 'Modern Society' group members, with Carthain Movement, Free Council and Spring Court.</li> <li><b>Storm Lords</b> - 'Rulers' groups. With Invictus and Silver Ladder they lead supernatural to victory. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul>I think that first 5 games of <b>C</b><b>hronicles of Darkness </b>nicely mesh with each other, as they were written with basic concept of 5x5 model ( or rather division like I mentioned above ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but there in lies the problem. I don't want global alliances, and I doubt the devs do either. Global alliances means global expectations, global stereotyping, and at least passing global knowledge. Not to mention an inevitable watering down of factional themes. Just try reconciling the beliefs of the Adamant Arrow with those of the Blood Talons, on the surface they seem to mesh but once you get into the nitty gritty they depart severely. Frankly the Blood Talons share just as much in common with the Praetoreans. Start throwing other splats into the alliance and it gets exponentially messier.<br /> <br /> But more importantly it seems to clash with the current direction of ChroD. Just look at the city write-ups in the 2e books, they put great effort into differentiating the cities, defying standard assumptions, and establishing the sheer unknowable weirdness of the world. Some of the new books (notably Lost 2e) are moving in the same direction, putting emphasis on local customization. So I'd be kinda surprised if the book takes the League of Nations approach, surprised and frankly disappointed.<br /> <br /> At best I expect to see allied Lodges, Bloodlines and Legacies. Largely local or occasionally regional.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>None of that is to say that it can't be done, only that I think they can do better.<br /> <br /> <b>Double Edit: </b>What I <u>do</u> expect to see is a section discussing the themes of the different factions and where they match up. There a bit of &quot;Blood Talons and The Adamant Arrow might come together if...&quot; would be quite welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-14-2016, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T04:08:35-07:00","id":950498,"title":"","content":"Global alliances as an option? Sure. As a default? Not in my opinion.<br /> <br /> That said, the various tribes can work with others in slightly more nuanced ways than the groups above.<ul><li><b>Blood Talons </b>- Willing to work with others to bring down the most powerful, troublesome werewolves.</li> <li><b>Bone Shadows</b> - Realise that hunting <i>Hisil</i> is more than just killing spirits. You need to work bigger changes on both sides of the Gauntlet. Other groups can have a big impact on this.</li> <li><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - Territory is sacred. Some other creatures understand that, others can be educated. Still others need to be eradicated, and the more agreeable folks can help. Plus, supernatural residents of a territory can be considered part of that territory. The Hunters will defend them as vehemently as any other aspect.<br /> <b>Iron Masters</b> - Every other supernatural creature has an interest in humanity. So do the Iron Masters. Crossover ideas are plentiful.</li> <li><b>Storm Lords</b> - Whatever the game, the Storm Lords will have an opinion about it. With their need to hide away perceived weakness, once they're in something they'll represent the tribe to the best of their ability. And many other supernatural types will almost invariably (perhaps ignorantly) bring the Storm Lords into it.</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T06:42:14-07:00","id":950534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=950498#post950498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Global alliances as an option? Sure. As a default? Not in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really interested in ideas of 'normal crossovers' beyond 'use a Tribe in situation it would normally go for'. On plot side it just seems 'do what you have done with crossovers to this day'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T07:18:29-07:00","id":950544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=944789#post944789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for a long time now, I've been blowing off crossover mechanical queries like &quot;so what happens when vampires feed from mages&quot; or &quot;what does Infrastructure look like under Mage Sight&quot; or &quot;What's the Hedge in Mage cosmology&quot; because I wanted a writer to be paid for it.<br /> <br /> It's also because I knew this was coming.<br /> <br /> Chicago is for three of the gamelines. This will be for all eleven.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Eleven. Does that mean Deviant will be out before the Crossover chronicle and will be part of the chronicles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:32:51-07:00","id":950628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=950488#post950488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found the Werewolf tribes especially difficult to manage (difficult enough to drop them entirely) what with their hunting focus and how certain supernaturals (cough Sin-Eaters cough) appear so much like prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're hunters, they're not murderhobos. They can decide whether or not to hunt someone and just being someone's sacred prey doesn't mean they're automatically going to get a hunt. Otherwise the Iron Masters would have wiped out all of humanity and the Blood Talons would have been wiped out by all the other werewolves. A Storm Lord who knows a geist might be okay with them. In similar fashion, a vampire might not drink from everyone, or a hunter may not hunt everyone. The Mysterium is about preserving magic, but even they don't go on pogroms killing all other mages so no one can know magic but them.<br /> <br /> But Lodges seem like a better option for global organizations. Or Mots, actually, which could be more of a social thing than lodges and less of a territorial thing than protectorates.<br /> <br /> Or they could go the Danse Macabre way and offer 'gonzo' international versions of the tribes. This book seems to be offering a different play style, so it might pop up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-14-2016, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:13:22-07:00","id":952463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=950628#post950628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they could go the Danse Macabre way and offer 'gonzo' international versions of the tribes. This book seems to be offering a different play style, so it might pop up.</div> </div> </div> </div> The werewolf chroniclers guide way actually, they were called conclaves, or dominions for the pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:36:14-07:00","id":952468,"title":"","content":"The Pack also presents something along these lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:05:49-07:00","id":952486,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Crossover Chronicle is going to have a &quot;thing.&quot; I mean an analogy for the strix or idigam (ie a monster), the fallen world (ie a drive), or firestorms (ie a phenomenon) set up to be of approximately the same level of interest to everyone.<br /> <br /> I also wonder if it means Onyx Path intend Deviant to be their last monster type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:20:39-07:00","id":952495,"title":"","content":"I doubt it. That said, Onyx Path appears to be getting off of the \u201cmonster treadmill\u201d (where every year heralds a new gameline featuring a new monster type) just as they previously got off of the supplement treadmill. I have no doubt that well see new monster types in the future; but I expect them to be fewer and farther between, and driven more by \u201cthat's a really neat idea!\u201d than by \u201cwe need something to meet this year's quota\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T08:31:45-07:00","id":952543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=952495#post952495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt it. That said, Onyx Path appears to be getting off of the \u201cmonster treadmill\u201d (where every year heralds a new gameline featuring a new monster type) just as they previously got off of the supplement treadmill. I have no doubt that well see new monster types in the future; but I expect them to be fewer and farther between, and driven more by \u201cthat's a really neat idea!\u201d than by \u201cwe need something to meet this year's quota\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hm? I didn't hear that - is that your theory, or is it something someone said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T09:43:34-07:00","id":952571,"title":"","content":"It's my theory, based on the lack of a gameline this last year and their stated dislike for quota-based publishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:13:49-07:00","id":952591,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras was a replacement for a gameline, and I think that their goal is something more of a &quot;project&quot; every year instead of a &quot;monster&quot; every year- for example, I imagine that the Crossover Chronicles would take the place of a new gameline, considering it has to squeeze 11 different games in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:04:17-07:00","id":952764,"title":"","content":"Isn't Crossover Chronicle going to be concurrent with Deviant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_bla