> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=952956#post952956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This release eliminates the chances of another line to be launched in the coming years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is Deviant yet to come out (and Changeling and Hunter and Geist).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T21:07:33-07:00","id":952965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=952959#post952959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there is Deviant yet to come out (and Changeling and Hunter and Geist).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Changeling. Mummy, Hunter e Geist would review and Desviant They have appeared in this book.<br /> <br /> However thinking with depth is difficult to think of a subject that can not be embedded as a template minor in an existing line; as a Blue Book (although some supplements, but no more than five) or Mirrors (Mummies and different Demons could be thought of in a Mirrors second edition or the Mirrors own turn the secondary line to deal with Mara demons, gods created by a Destiny with conscious and servants, Angels and Demons given off of a Dead God Mummies Incas, Mumias Chinese, Faes Innocence hunters).<br /> <br /> With one exception. I would like a review of the Changing Breeds and not see them as a Minor Template or simply as an Antagonist (as Aliens and Lovecraftianos beings would be).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:29:09-07:00","id":953240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=952956#post952956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This release eliminates the chances of another line to be launched in the coming years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly doubtful, especially if it is more advice on how to blend the themes and run the chronicle rather than hard mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:30:20-07:00","id":953316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=952956#post952956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This release eliminates the chances of another line to be launched in the coming years?</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you familar with the Hunter supplement &quot;Mortal Remains?&quot; When it came out, it covered up to all existing game lines. Then, Onyx Path started releasing more games. And then, a promise of new Mortal Remains chapter for the new game.<br /> <br /> Crossover Chronicles could easily follow the same style.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:49:48-07:00","id":953410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=953316#post953316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are you familar with the Hunter supplement &amp;quot;Mortal Remains?&amp;quot; When it came out, it covered up to all existing game lines. Then, Onyx Path started releasing more games. And then, a promise of new Mortal Remains chapter for the new game.<br /> <br /> Crossover Chronicles could easily follow the same style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they promise? I thought that everyone just got on a Dark Eras/Mortal Remains wagon for Beast and OPP agreed it was a good idea. Still, excellent point. The same thing is likely to happen with Deviant, as with any future games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T03:37:27-07:00","id":953744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=953316#post953316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover Chronicles could easily follow the same style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. I certainly wouldn't <i>want</i> there to be no chance of new monster-lines (and I don't really buy into the &quot;no new room&quot; argument, given the last four lines - counting Deviant - have defied similar claims).<br /> <br /> What about my other question? Will it have a &quot;thing&quot; to make crossover happen? Or will crossover - expressed in character, perhaps, as the realisation that ignoring each other has ceased to be a viable option - be the thing in and of itself? I think I'd prefer the latter; it's a complex enough subject, but the former would make it more focussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T14:04:32-07:00","id":954033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=953744#post953744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about my other question? Will it have a &quot;thing&quot; to make crossover happen? Or will crossover - expressed in character, perhaps, as the realisation that ignoring each other has ceased to be a viable option - be the thing in and of itself? I think I'd prefer the latter; it's a complex enough subject, but the former would make it more focussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like it if there was a lot of small things that might create a crossover game, but I wouldn't want a Strix, Idigam or Huntsman <i>thing</i> as the default. On the other hand I don't want it to only be about the breaking of the splat walls, because that's quickly boring. Vamp VS Werewolf, Mage VS Demon, etc... I can already do this without a corebook to help me.<br /> <br /> In short: I want a chapter filled with lots of plot hooks, not a single \u00dbber-Antagonist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:16:28-07:00","id":954503,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, rather than an antagonist, it can be something more like Firestorms: a phenomena that affects all the splats and, thus, is a context for interaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:55:12-07:00","id":954523,"title":"","content":"or something like the Fallen World- that is, something which is just around, and draws the different splats to get out of their own little bubbles and give them a reason to actually talk with each other- not some of weird occult phenomena, but some kind of mystery or problem which gives them a motivation to work together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T06:18:21-07:00","id":954925,"title":"","content":"Well, there's several things that we need to think about for crossover games. First and foremost, we have to figure out the kind of crossover. Is it a true crossover, with a mixed troupe? Cameo appearances of other supernaturals as NPCs? Dedicated as antagonists in Vamp vs. Wolf style (or, like I mentioned in the Alchemist thread in the Prommie section) mages as alchemical antagonists there. <br /> <br /> What about hacks / houserules? There's a lot of changes if we start looking at merging ephemeral realms and fuel stats to make them more crossover friendly. How about benefits for vampires who seduce and feed from supernaturals? Werewolves already get bonuses for supernatural pack mates. There's Yantara bonuses from supernaturals we can talk about. There are lots of ways we can swap the game to make supernaturals actively WANT to hang out together.<br /> <br /> There's always official rules on interactions that can be listed, but frankly, I don't like those. I find those get in the way of different kinds of games by focusing on just one style of game, and you're out of luck if that doesn't fit your preferred game style. Or shows clear bias towards one supernatural over another- especially if the crossover rules are in a supernatural game line (ie there will be a changeling bias in CtL books). Its best to stick with ways to make your own personal rulings so as to customize your game, rather than make official rules that may get in the way of story. When it comes to details like this, rulings &gt; rules.<br /> <br /> The biggest hurdle to crossover games is the difficulty of making themes resonate. Chapters on how to make games with even clashing themes work together might be awesome. Also, works on different ways to resolve things like the five or so different versions of God would be cool - are they the same? Different but allied? Mutually opposed and at war? Just don't care? How do the different mega-corporations of different games work? Could they be combined? What does a joint project look like?<br /> <br /> Right now, with the exception of Beast and Hunter, every game effectively lives in its own sandbox. Almost exclusionary sandboxes to the point its best to compare different game lines to . Ways to merge, mingle, or just deal with these different worlds would be cool. I ran games where I literally shoved the Shadow, Hisil, Astral, Underworld and a custom digital world into a single spirit world, and it worked awesomely. Giving supernaturals like vamps and non-ulgan prommies ways to interact with spirit worlds and Twilight is pretty important when dealing with wolf and mage crossovers. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:50:52-07:00","id":954996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=954925#post954925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, with the exception of Beast and Hunter, every game effectively lives in its own sandbox. Almost exclusionary sandboxes to the point its best to compare different game lines to.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned earlier in this thread, Mage is arguably at least as crossover-friendly as Beast, both in terms of thematic reasons to cross over (mages are literally rewarded for sticking their noses into other supernaturals' concerns) and in terms of having the tools to deal with crossover concerns: for instance, Spirit as written is exclusively about interacting with Werewolf's playground; and Death likewise opens up Geist's personal playground to exploration. <br /> <br /> Promethean also has a whole Refinement dedicated to crossovers, complete with a Transmutation that's geared entirely toward interacting with other supernaturals. I wouldn't mind if other gamelines' z-splats get used to emulate this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:04:33-07:00","id":955004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=954996#post954996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned earlier in this thread, Mage is arguably at least as crossover-friendly as Beast, both in terms of thematic reasons to cross over (mages are literally rewarded for sticking their noses into other supernaturals' concerns) and in terms of having the tools to deal with crossover concerns: for instance, Spirit as written is exclusively about interacting with Werewolf's playground; and Death likewise opens up Geist's personal playground to exploration.<br /> <br /> Promethean also has a whole Refinement dedicated to crossovers, complete with a Transmutation that's geared entirely toward interacting with other supernaturals. I wouldn't mind if other gamelines' z-splats get used to emulate this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage's ease to steal another's game thunder hardly is what I'd call &quot;crossover friendly&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:24:07-07:00","id":955011,"title":"","content":"I imagine what was meant there is that the base game of Mage is crossover-friendly in that it's easy to add other gamelines' material to it, as they invariably tend to be interested in them, and have abilities that make it easier to do so, so you don't need to fight too hard to make it work on their end.<br /> <br /> Mechanics-wise, yeah, Mages aren't very easy to include because they're so comparatively powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:19:53-07:00","id":955073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=954996#post954996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned earlier in this thread, Mage is arguably at least as crossover-friendly as Beast, both in terms of thematic reasons to cross over (mages are literally rewarded for sticking their noses into other supernaturals' concerns) and in terms of having the tools to deal with crossover concerns: for instance, Spirit as written is exclusively about interacting with Werewolf's playground; and Death likewise opens up Geist's personal playground to exploration.<br /> <br /> Promethean also has a whole Refinement dedicated to crossovers, complete with a Transmutation that's geared entirely toward interacting with other supernaturals. I wouldn't mind if other gamelines' z-splats get used to emulate this.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree about Mage, I think its rather antagonistic towards crossover for a wide variety of reasons. There are entire threads dedicated to the difficulties contained in that very act as well as comments directly from Mage writers to indicate their stances towards crossover in Mage.<br /> <br /> And having a single Refinement is pretty worthless as a whole when you need to swap Refinements at least four times, at minimum, over the course of your Pilgrimage. Usually more. Its not very promising in the long term. That doesn't take into account the fact that non-ephemeral supernaturals are just as susceptable to Disquiet as mortals, making them as brief aquaintances, when they show up,<br /> <br /> Any game can potentially crossover with some effort and specific builds. Mage and Promethean are not exceptions to this. But that doesn't change that the games are designed fully to hang out in their own sandbox. Beast and Hunter are the only games where dealing with other supernaturals literally IS their focus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Crossover is not easy. The easiest way to do it is just to have cameos, because its always possible to just drop something in. But all other forms of crossover require levels of planning and comfort of rules beyond the casual. With Beast, its a different matter, because the Begotten are specifically built in a way that resonates with the common points of all supernaturals, and possess the ability to fully interact with anything a supernatural might need to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-21-2016, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:30:40-07:00","id":955083,"title":"","content":"I think that the best way to describe Mage at crossovers is as &quot;invasive species&quot;- that is, Mages has many reasons and means to enter the territory of other splats and play around, but that doesn't mean the other splats are happy about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:01:13-07:00","id":955511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=955083#post955083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the best way to describe Mage at crossovers is as &quot;invasive species&quot;- that is, Mages has many reasons and means to enter the territory of other splats and play around, but that doesn't mean the other splats are happy about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;So, since some Mages started snooping around the Domain, the Prince brought in some &quot;Abyssal&quot; monstrosities to keep their numbers down. Yeah... that didn't end well.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:00:05-07:00","id":955708,"title":"","content":"Eh. A mage who comes snooping around is no more of a problem than a werewolf who comes snooping around, or a changeling who comes snooping around, etc.; it's just more likely to happen. And when we're talking <b>Crossover Chronicle</b>, I'd expect the game to focus on aspects more interesting and constructive than \u201cthe Other is here! Drive it out so we don't have ideal with it!\u201d (Unless, of course, the Other is a Promethean.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:44:51-07:00","id":955861,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;addicted to mysteries&quot; thing does sort of support the idea that mages are more likely than others to end up snooping around in invasive ways. That appears in Transgression in a slightly different way. <br /> <br /> It's definitely truer for Mages than a lot of other supernaturals: for example, Demons do have some reason to poke around in the business of other entities, but the whole &quot;master spy&quot; thing means they're much likelier to be subtle about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:59:46-07:00","id":955947,"title":"","content":"\u201cInvasive\u201d is a loaded term, predicated on the notion that any involvement by the mage will be seen as unwelcome interference. <i>Especially</i> in a Crossover Chronicle, that ain't necessarily so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:29:33-07:00","id":955973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=955947#post955947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cInvasive\u201d is a loaded term, predicated on the notion that any involvement by the mage will be seen as unwelcome interference. <i>Especially</i> in a Crossover Chronicle, that ain't necessarily so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant &quot;invasive&quot; as for the canon outlook of the CofD setting, not under the idea of the Crossover Chronicles. Mages, in general, are not seem to be trusted or welcomed by the other splats, especially since they always seem to say they know better how things work. Mages always has more reasons to stick their nose in other monster's territory than the monster in question, usually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:00:44-07:00","id":955993,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's supported by the books. Rather, I suspect that that's a long-standing view of <b>Mage</b> <i>fans</i> by other gamelines' fans, which then get conflated with the game's protagonists. I doubt that any of the <i>writers</i> have presented mages as invasive.<br /> <br /> In particular, <b>Mage</b> tends to present its protagonists as nosy busybodies, not as arrogant know-it-alls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-22-2016, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:19:51-07:00","id":956108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=955993#post955993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, <b>Mage</b> tends to present its protagonists as nosy busybodies, not as arrogant know-it-alls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though some overlap is hardly surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:41:15-07:00","id":956120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=955993#post955993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, <b>Mage</b> tends to present its protagonists as nosy busybodies, not as arrogant know-it-alls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Fallen World Fiction Anthology? Really you get a mix of both. They just tend to be nosy busybodies or arrogant know-it-alls mostly in regards to other mages. But in the Beast Fiction Anthology which probably had a better name maybe, there's one who insists to knowing what the Beast is despite her insistence otherwise, and way, way back in the Silent Knife you get much more of the arrogance, and then in the Danse Macabre more along the lines of arrogant know-it-all who really gets their comeuppance at the hands of another character.<br /> <br /> Three Shades of Night probably portrayed them the most favorably, and even then they would fall to either side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-22-2016, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T05:11:43-07:00","id":956268,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, I'd imagine mages to be the second most knowledgeable about any given metaphysical sphere, and beasts to be the second most knowledgeable about any given social sphere, just because they take an interest in such things. The idea that needs to go isn't about whether mages are knowledgeable or ignorant, but that being more broadly knowledgeable means they win in some way - if it's a competition, it's a competition only mages are taking part in, because none of the other care that much.<br /> <br /> At any rate, I imagine that supernaturals being known - and approached - for particular skill sets will be something that's addressed. The uppermost example in my mind is that Geist ceremony that lets you change the apparent cause of death of a body, right down to the forensic level. A sineater who's known to be able to do that will be on every supernatural's speed-dial in the city, especially since sineaters are often willing to work for nothing more outre than cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:42:10-07:00","id":956294,"title":"","content":"Thing is, Hal isn't wrong about what a Beast is. He specifically says, when the beast says she's not possessed &quot;no, and neither is a Sin-Eater, but you are to Goetia as they are to ghosts&quot;.<br /> <br /> He just also mocks the Begotten &quot;lesson&quot; culture because he's a <i>Mastigos</i>, and ironically thinks Beasts would be a lot more fulfilled if they owned up to being monsters rather than paper a weak (to his mind) justification over it.<br /> <br /> But also, and this is the crucial part, because he's this particular Beast's ex-boyfriend and this is something like the seventh microaggressive line he's had in three pages. Because she has a Hunger for humbling the arrogant, and they broke up when she fed off him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:51:36-07:00","id":956300,"title":"","content":"People need not be factually wrong to miss on fundamental truths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:27:35-07:00","id":956334,"title":"","content":"I wasn't commenting on whether they were wrong or not, simply the attitude when pronouncing their belief, in Hal's case arrogance, particularly concerning the next line and the Beast's own beliefs. It puts him more firmly in the territory of arrogant know-it-all, and though I'll grant it probably has a lot to do with his relationship to the Beast, we don't exactly see him outside of that frame, and it still shows a writer depicting a Mage as invasive, which Dataweaver implied was only something fans of other gamelines believed.<br /> <br /> Basically, mages are still human and susceptible to human foibles. Just as the Embrace doesn't turn everyone into a Machiavellian mastermind, Awakening doesn't turn everyone into a humble hermit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-23-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:18:44-07:00","id":956370,"title":"","content":"As Mages gain power from knowing and codifying things, I think they are <i>more likely</i> to display know-it-all behavior, but as stated, they're human (mostly).<br /> <br /> I second that they are more likely/fitting for crossover, due to their broad reach, incentive for investigation, and ability to help others (while having their own problems mitigated). Beasts, despite being &quot;designed for crossover&quot; seem less fitting, mostly due to their limited ability to grant assistance (Mother's Kiss is nice and all, but nothing a Mage can't already simulate), pressing needs, and being, basically, the poisonous friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:35:39-07:00","id":956380,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to present a phenomena that each group could interpret in its own way and have there be no right answer. The werewolves think it is caused by a stirring idigam, demons think it is God-Machine infrastructure, mages approach it as supernal phenomena, etc. But do it in such a way that none are ever confirmed correct. Their approach works sometimes, other times it fails, such that it is certainly an unusual example of whatever they think it is and conceivably may be something else entirely, keeping with the Chronicles of Darkness tenet that weird, unexplained stuff exists and doesn't necessarily fit in any of the available boxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:22:53-07:00","id":956398,"title":"","content":"Who has had experience running crossover games with mages? And I mean more than just have a random supernatural show up in a Mage game - sure, mages are awesome at dealing with other supernaturals in a Mage-centric game. Lets talk about an actual a mixed party, or how about actual mages as full on antagonists in another game. Because I'm just hearing about a lot of theorycraft and guessing, and not a lot of personal experience on the matter. <br /> <br /> I have run such games, and I've personally experienced a number of issues stemming from a number of different sources - thematically, mechanically, overlapping abilities that render other PCs feeling redundant, and so on. Introducing the Awakened into other games causes multiple problems from a number of angles, and mixed groups have niche issues that a mage can easily overwhelm. <br /> <br /> I have talked with others who've done crossover games with mages, and the reports tend to be less than enthusiastic about mages being awesome in crossover games. In fact, the general consensus tends to lean towards disallowing mages more than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:37:09-07:00","id":956405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956398#post956398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who has had experience running crossover games with mages? And I mean more than just have a random supernatural show up in a Mage game - sure, mages are awesome at dealing with other supernaturals in a Mage-centric game. Lets talk about an actual a mixed party, or how about actual mages as full on antagonists in another game. Because I'm just hearing about a lot of theorycraft and guessing, and not a lot of personal experience on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played and STed a few mixed-troupe games in 1st edition and a single one in 2nd edition. I will sadly have to echo the existing reports that Mages are not fun in a crossover group. The only time where a Mage was fun to play with was when the player decided to be laid back and ride along rather than taking a true active role in the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:07:44-07:00","id":956610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956370#post956370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Mages gain power from knowing and codifying things, I think they are <i>more likely</i> to display know-it-all behavior, but as stated, they're human (mostly).<br /> <br /> I second that they are more likely/fitting for crossover, due to their broad reach, incentive for investigation, and ability to help others (while having their own problems mitigated). Beasts, despite being &quot;designed for crossover&quot; seem less fitting, mostly due to their limited ability to grant assistance (Mother's Kiss is nice and all, but nothing a Mage can't already simulate), pressing needs, and being, basically, the poisonous friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corollary that everyone seems to forget is that every Beast is equally adept at Crossover, while a Mage without a iota of Spirit simply doesn't has the tools to deal with say, massive outburst of elemental influenced destruction.<br /> <br /> Just because you happen to be a singular mage doesn't means you have every Arcana at, say, 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-23-2016, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:48:27-07:00","id":956626,"title":"","content":"In 1st edition, I've been able to get Mage to play nicely with other games with a bit of house ruling (not even that much) and in general opening up options for other character types (allowing Vampires to make gargoyles and keep devotion creation open, let changelings talecraft, etc). Sure, Mages could generally twink a little better and had a wider array of tools, but it didn't ruin the game for anyone else.<br /> <br /> With 2nd edition, well, I can't see that working anymore, I admit. They no longer have just better utility; their powers are now superior at similar levels too (if they're willing to risk paradox), to the point of completely overriding other splats in the same field. In 1e, a Mage needed 4 dots of Mind to do what a Vampire could do with Dominate 2, but now they have a 2 dot spell that's far better than Dominate is (again, if enough Reach is spent), for instance, in addition to the half dozen other spells they get at that level (plus CT and attainments). Paradox is more of a risk now, but not enough to override the complete advantage they have in both breadth and depth.<br /> <br /> As someone who always loved including Mage in crossover in 1e, it does sort of upset me how the 2e developer mindset is &quot;Fuck balance&quot; ( / &quot;balance is a myth&quot; / however else they actually put it) with regards to crossover (and sometimes in the same game).<br /> <br /> Now, that said, that's a mechanical issue. From a story standpoint, I don't think there's any support for saying Mages are harder to integrate; everyone has a healthy distrust as the default, but I've never seen any evidence of Mages being moreso than anyone else. Yes, they're seen as arrogant. And vampires are backstabbing, and werewolves violent, and changelings xenophobic/paranoid. It's a stereotype. And not one that's any more universally pervasive, I don't think.<br /> <br /> So, my overall point, I suppose, is that Mage is a great game for crossover, and fits it in thematically better than many other games, from a story standpoint. It's just terrible for any PC-level characters of other venues involved, as they'll very quickly be overshadowed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For what it's worth, I do like a large amount of the changes to the 'skeleton' of Mage's spellcasting, and a large number of other changes, it's just the actual balance and individual spells that I have issue with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-23-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T22:16:23-07:00","id":956787,"title":"","content":"I do hope that <b>Crossover Chronicle</b> will take a more thoughtful approach to the mechanical issues that crossovers raise than simply saying \u201cbalance is a myth\u201d and dumping everything on the Storyteller's shoulders. At the same time, that doesn't mean that I want \u201cwhite-room game balance\u201d; just an acknowledgement that it <i>is</i> possible to \u201cwizard the warrior\u201d (where what's supposed to be in theory a jack of all trades who is second-best at everything turns out in practice to be a master of all trades who is as good as or better than the specialists in their chosen fields) and some advice on how to prevent it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T02:43:16-07:00","id":956861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956294#post956294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, Hal isn't wrong about what a Beast is. He specifically says, when the beast says she's not possessed &quot;no, and neither is a Sin-Eater, but you are to Goetia as they are to ghosts&quot;.<br /> <br /> He just also mocks the Begotten &quot;lesson&quot; culture because he's a <i>Mastigos</i>, and ironically thinks Beasts would be a lot more fulfilled if they owned up to being monsters rather than paper a weak (to his mind) justification over it.<br /> <br /> But also, and this is the crucial part, because he's this particular Beast's ex-boyfriend and this is something like the seventh microaggressive line he's had in three pages. Because she has a Hunger for humbling the arrogant, and they broke up when she fed off him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I miss Hal <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(and his supporting cast</span>), and hope we see more of his mage-y attitude and shenanigans in future stories. It's a shame such an excellent representation of a mage was hidden in the Beast Anthology.<br /> <br /> Also, considering Hal would have been well justified in <i>ending</i> Sandhya after the feeding, a few arguably microagressive remarks when she wanted his help year later, are negligible in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T03:08:39-07:00","id":956866,"title":"","content":"Well, if Crossover gets an anthology and I get a story in it, he'll be back to insult new supernatural entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T05:33:52-07:00","id":956893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956861#post956861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, considering Hal would have been well justified in <i>ending</i> Sandhya after the feeding, a few arguably microagressive remarks when she wanted his help year later, are negligible in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that flat judgement not a bit unjust in consideration of his (seeming lack of) respect for personal boundaries, and her circumstances?<br /> <br /> I can see how he would have thought that, however. Or that not doing much worse in retaliation when he could have makes him magnanimous.<br /> <br /> But returning to the topic, I'd be all for more crossover fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-24-2016, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T06:21:56-07:00","id":956908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956861#post956861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, considering Hal would have been well justified in <i>ending</i> Sandhya after the feeding, a few arguably microagressive remarks when she wanted his help year later, are negligible in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? It was alarming for him, but it's not like he actually got hurt by it. Nothing but his pride, which isn't worth shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:16:11-07:00","id":956941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956908#post956908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? It was alarming for him, but it's not like he actually got hurt by it. Nothing but his pride, which isn't worth shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it torpedoed to relationship too, I'm guessing on account of him being treated as merely food.<br /> <br /> ADDENDUM: Which suggests a dangerous level of regard for people and boundaries. Trying to justify it as &quot;but she's hungry&quot; isn't really a defense against not taking action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:58:52-07:00","id":957003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956941#post956941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to justify it as &quot;but she's hungry&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The same story sees her Horror attack Hal as they're crossing from her Lair to their destination.<br /> <br /> There are limits to how high you can reasonably set your expectations for self-control when it comes to the activity of your subconscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:52:51-07:00","id":957042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957003#post957003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same story sees her Horror attack Hal as they're crossing from her Lair to their destination.<br /> <br /> There are limits to how high you can reasonably set your expectations for self-control when it comes to the activity of your subconscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when one's lack of self-control represents a clear and previously demonstrated danger to others?<br /> <br /> Separate issue: Isn't it established that the Beast (namely, the human identity) decides when to <i>actively</i> feed, as opposed to the Starving induced nightly feeding rampages of the Horror? If so, then she <i>choose</i> to target him, subconscious weighting or not.<br /> <br /> (Mostly we can conclude that at least some part of her <i>really</i> does not like Hal.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:17:26-07:00","id":957057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957042#post957042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And when one's lack of self-control represents a clear and previously demonstrated danger to others?<br /> <br /> Separate issue: Isn't it established that the Beast (namely, the human identity) decides when to <i>actively</i> feed, as opposed to the Starving induced nightly feeding rampages of the Horror? If so, then she <i>choose</i> to target him, subconscious weighting or not.<br /> <br /> (Mostly we can conclude that at least some part of her <i>really</i> does not like Hal.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, by the RAW it turns out that the Horror can'