m</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:14:08-07:00","id":957096,"title":"","content":"Killing over it may seem overboard for some but it is one of the first things he suggests doing when woken from his dream. '...I will <i>end </i>you.' Though having just been awakened from a Beast-induced nightmare from someone you trusted enough to sleep with might have had him unbalanced, so to speak, emotionally. It was a betrayal, of sorts.<br /> <br /> I can't say how my character would react, not knowing enough about the situation beyond the fact that he wouldn't have slept with her in the first place, but he's killed for less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:30:02-07:00","id":957107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957090#post957090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite the reverse!<br /> <br /> Najat's a Chronicles of Darkness-style Bastet, from Changing Breeds:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/51348.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\"> World of Darkness: Changing Breeds - White Wolf | World of Darkness (new) | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> World of Darkness: Changing Breeds - Nature is FED UP with us. In fact, she&rsquo;d like to have a chat With you. So lay right there And let&rsquo;s begin. I&rsquo;ll do </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changing Breeds is considered by a great many CofD fans to be a less than stellar addition to the setting and rules, and best forgotten or ignored. <br /> <br /> In your ample free time after your real life, developing Mage and Deviant and writing for almost everything else in the CofD, it would be great if you (and maybe Chris Allen) wrote a much needed 2e treatment for Changing Breeds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:51:41-07:00","id":957169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956626#post956626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With 2nd edition, well, I can't see that working anymore, I admit. They no longer have just better utility; their powers are now superior at similar levels too (if they're willing to risk paradox), to the point of completely overriding other splats in the same field. In 1e, a Mage needed 4 dots of Mind to do what a Vampire could do with Dominate 2, but now they have a 2 dot spell that's far better than Dominate is (again, if enough Reach is spent), for instance, in addition to the half dozen other spells they get at that level (plus CT and attainments). Paradox is more of a risk now, but not enough to override the complete advantage they have in both breadth and depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's true. Mind spells are fairly weak until your character is significantly advanced. Psychic Domination is, I assume, the spell you're talking about. It is Withstood by Resolve, has to last for sufficient duration for the action to be completed and has a primary factor of Potency. A starting mage with Gnosis 1, Mind 3, has one spell control slot, so having someone do anything that takes a while is going to eat it, has a base four dice and may have to spend 2-4 of them to even make the spell have an effect depending on the target's resolve, has to spend at least a reach for making the duration scene long if the action can't be completed in a few seconds, and may need to spend even more dice if a longer duration is required, and has to contend with paradox on those tiny dice pools if they just want to make the spell instant cast and sensory range. Iron Edict is a much surer much more powerful ability for a starting character. Once you've hit someone with the Mesmerized condition they're pretty much yours. The mage is constantly running risks to duplicate the base effect, and success is far from guaranteed. <br /> <br /> The thing with mage spells in 2e is that because effects are placed in the appropriate practice, lower level Arcana dots *seem* really strong, but it's because even their lower dot powers scale with the mage getting stronger, unlike the other splats, not because they're really powerful the second you get them. The system has balancers that keep power level in check. <br /> <br /> Mages are also slow to cast things now because of this; having to incorporate Yantras so that you have enough dice to boost spell factors to an effective enough level means the werewolves or celerity/vigor vampires are able to contribute far more relative combat effectiveness than a simple glimpse at Mage's spell list would suggest. They also get far fewer useful innate abilities; a vampire reflexively boosting strength or dex can cause a lot of damage with a mundane attack, and you're probably dead if they successfully get you in a grapple and start feeding, a werewolf can shrug off massive amounts of damage reflexively, etc. It's very easy to create situations where the mage is completely outclassed and functions best by providing support. <br /> <br /> 2e Mages aren't broken power level wise. They're maybe broken information gathering wise. They'll break PC groups where they're allowed to set the tempo because they're absurdly good at getting the upper hand with preparation. But that's an issue with the ST losing control of pacing, or failing to move the spotlight around so that individual character strengths and weaknesses are properly highlighted.<br /> <br /> That being said, mixed groups are headaches no matter what splat you're talking about. There are ways to work around any issue, but I've had situations where having a single Vampire in a mixed game caused me more logistical issues than almost anything else simply because of the sleeping during the day thing. You can run into difficult to deal with limitations caused by any splat in a mixed group. So much so that I'm generally of the opinion that they shouldn't be attempted unless the ST and the group are very good at improvisation, there's a really strong social contract, and they have a lot of system mastery, or if the game is intended to be ridiculous and rules light. They are messy and difficult to pull off well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 08-24-2016, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:55:56-07:00","id":957203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957169#post957169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's true. Mind spells are fairly weak until your character is significantly advanced. Psychic Domination is, I assume, the spell you're talking about. It is Withstood by Resolve, has to last for sufficient duration for the action to be completed and has a primary factor of Potency. A starting mage with Gnosis 1, Mind 3, has one spell control slot, so having someone do anything that takes a while is going to eat it, has a base four dice and may have to spend 2-4 of them to even make the spell have an effect depending on the target's resolve, has to spend at least a reach for making the duration scene long if the action can't be completed in a few seconds, and may need to spend even more dice if a longer duration is required, and has to contend with paradox on those tiny dice pools if they just want to make the spell instant cast and sensory range. Iron Edict is a much surer much more powerful ability for a starting character. Once you've hit someone with the Mesmerized condition they're pretty much yours. The mage is constantly running risks to duplicate the base effect, and success is far from guaranteed.<br /> <br /> The thing with mage spells in 2e is that because effects are placed in the appropriate practice, lower level Arcana dots *seem* really strong, but it's because even their lower dot powers scale with the mage getting stronger, unlike the other splats, not because they're really powerful the second you get them. The system has balancers that keep power level in check.<br /> <br /> Mages are also slow to cast things now because of this; having to incorporate Yantras so that you have enough dice to boost spell factors to an effective enough level means the werewolves or celerity/vigor vampires are able to contribute far more relative combat effectiveness than a simple glimpse at Mage's spell list would suggest. They also get far fewer useful innate abilities; a vampire reflexively boosting strength or dex can cause a lot of damage with a mundane attack, and you're probably dead if they successfully get you in a grapple and start feeding, a werewolf can shrug off massive amounts of damage reflexively, etc. It's very easy to create situations where the mage is completely outclassed and functions best by providing support.<br /> <br /> 2e Mages aren't broken power level wise. They're maybe broken information gathering wise. They'll break PC groups where they're allowed to set the tempo because they're absurdly good at getting the upper hand with preparation. But that's an issue with the ST losing control of pacing, or failing to move the spotlight around so that individual character strengths and weaknesses are properly highlighted.<br /> <br /> That being said, mixed groups are headaches no matter what splat you're talking about. There are ways to work around any issue, but I've had situations where having a single Vampire in a mixed game caused me more logistical issues than almost anything else simply because of the sleeping during the day thing. You can run into difficult to deal with limitations caused by any splat in a mixed group. So much so that I'm generally of the opinion that they shouldn't be attempted unless the ST and the group are very good at improvisation, there's a really strong social contract, and they have a lot of system mastery, or if the game is intended to be ridiculous and rules light. They are messy and difficult to pull off well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I disagree with your assessment there.<br /> <br /> With Gnosis 1 + Mind 2 (we'll go even lower than assumed), you have 3 dice, but to be honest, it's fairly easy to get +2 from some yantra or another on that, giving you a base of 5. Unlike a Vampire, you don't need to worry about the opposing dice pool possibly being lucky, you just need to account for the opponent's resolve. By default, with Mind 2, that does mean you probably need a -2 penalty to deal with an average opponent (mundane or otherwise), putting you back at 3, though you can spend willpower to bring it to 6, where it's no longer a concern. If you're dealing with someone above average, sure, you'll need to up it some more, maybe leaving you with 4 or even 2 dice (but still at least a 50% chance). This does mean when you first get it, people do have a shot of resisting (or rather, you have a chance of failing, if you overcompensate and thus dont have enough dice afterward).<br /> <br /> Even if the chosen yantra takes you an extra turn, from using, say, high speech, that's still combat-time, which as I recall dominate 2 still has trouble performing during. So, the whole 'time taken' thing still gives the Mage the advantage, and if we're assuming similar use circumstances, you aren't caring about combat time anyway as you have conversational time to work with, so can more easily incorporate yantras, and for that matter, can probably recast the spell a few times if it's withstood or the roll fails.<br /> <br /> As for paradox, just contain it and you dont need to deal with penalties to the casting. Might have a deleterious condition and some bashing damage, depending on how much 'dox you accumulate, but even assuming you need the reach for all of casting time, duration and range, and for the fun of it, we'll say you're causing suicide (Which Dominate can't even do) for +2 more, that's 4 dice for the gnosis 1 mage, which means their Wisdom of 7 probably can handle the containing roll. And if they want to be more careful, they can probably rely on an aimed spell instead and depending on the end goal, maybe even use basic duration.<br /> <br /> This of course is all assuming you have NONE of the following: A praxis (likely able to beat the Withstand just by exceptional-ing and ignoring it, plus you'll have less paradox to deal with), a rote (mudra bonus AND you have 3 more reach, meaning your paradox pool is now only 1 die), or the sympathetic range attainment (if you can cast sympathetically, 90% of non-mage opponents are f'd as you can take all the time you need to add in yantras and work ritually for less paradox risk). Any of those means even that starting Mage with 2 dots of Mind will have a much larger chance of performing much more competently (admittedly the space 2 scenario isn't always available, if dealing with a threat you weren't expecting).<br /> <br /> So, yes, that Gnosis 1 Mind 2 Mage does have some difficulties, but overall, there's a varied number of ways they'd still be able to make easy use of that powerful spell, just not as easily as an adept would. Plus, there's the rest of Mind 2 that they get with that same dot, including a mental shield to prevent the vampire from dominating them to start with (yes, I know, we dont have to assume it's a direct conflict, but still).<br /> <br /> As for innate abilities, Mages have attainments, and that means Mage Sight and Mage Armor, as well as a Utility attainment or 2, no matter what. Mage armor is very useful in a lot of cases, mage sight you admittedly already mentioned, and the utility attainments vary, but definitely provide heavy advantages (one possibility, again, being sympathetic casting).<br /> <br /> So, overall, while I'm not saying a starter mage doesn't need to account for things a bit better than an adept or master, I still think they have the advantage over a similar 'level' of opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-24-2016, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:59:41-07:00","id":957207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956908#post956908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? It was alarming for him, but it's not like he actually got hurt by it. Nothing but his pride, which isn't worth shit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mage, hubris, pride. Combine that with the natural instinct of Beasts to push people towards low Integrity equivalents? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:05:24-07:00","id":957212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957203#post957203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I disagree with your assessment there.<br /> <br /> With Gnosis 1 + Mind 2 (we'll go even lower than assumed), you have 3 dice, but to be honest, it's fairly easy to get +2 from some yantra or another on that, giving you a base of 5. Unlike a Vampire, you don't need to worry about the opposing dice pool possibly being lucky, you just need to account for the opponent's resolve. By default, with Mind 2, that does mean you probably need a -2 penalty to deal with an average opponent (mundane or otherwise), putting you back at 3, though you can spend willpower to bring it to 6, where it's no longer a concern. If you're dealing with someone above average, sure, you'll need to up it some more, maybe leaving you with 4 or even 2 dice (but still at least a 50% chance). This does mean when you first get it, people do have a shot of resisting (or rather, you have a chance of failing, if you overcompensate and thus dont have enough dice afterward).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The targets Resolve doesn't subtract from the die pool, it has to be overcome by Potency. And you ignored the Duration point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:06:31-07:00","id":957213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957212#post957212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The targets Resolve doesn't subtract from the die pool, it has to be overcome by Potency. And you ignored the Duration point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it doesn't. The -2 was to bump Potency up to 3 (and you can see I accounted for further Potency raises for higher Resolve by lowering the pool by 2 more at a time). And I didn't ignore a duration point, I assumed a scene was enough for most purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:13:27-07:00","id":957219,"title":"","content":"The comparison of difficulties might be negated out by Dominate being resisted by Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance, and complete immunity being achieved by closing your eyes or looking away. Plus it can be broken by taking Bashing damage, or Lethal.<br /> <br /> But even if it wasn't we're veering into nitpicking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-24-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:24:07-07:00","id":957224,"title":"","content":"Also good points, but yeah, I'm mildly upset at myself for breaking down several paragraphs of math that includes a bunch of &quot;ifs&quot; and &quot;maybe&quot; type things, which I get drawn into doing too easily.<br /> <br /> To be more concise, my overall point is that the spell itself is more powerful than the second level of dominate, assuming the mage either can naturally take advantage of it one way or another, or can prep a bit. And it's just one of many similar examples of Mages starting high and growing exponentially while everyone else (out of 2e splats) grows more linearly. Yes, there are circumstances where others have the advantage, and yes, they might not always be best able to use the ability, but more often than not they're better off now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-24-2016, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:49:04-07:00","id":957269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957224#post957224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also good points, but yeah, I'm mildly upset at myself for breaking down several paragraphs of math that includes a bunch of &quot;ifs&quot; and &quot;maybe&quot; type things, which I get drawn into doing too easily.<br /> <br /> To be more concise, my overall point is that the spell itself is more powerful than the second level of dominate, assuming the mage either can naturally take advantage of it one way or another, or can prep a bit. And it's just one of many similar examples of Mages starting high and growing exponentially while everyone else (out of 2e splats) grows more linearly. Yes, there are circumstances where others have the advantage, and yes, they might not always be best able to use the ability, but more often than not they're better off now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooner or Later,the devs will have to tackle the whole &quot;Mages can do everything the others can do better&quot; issue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:03:36-07:00","id":957354,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u2669Anything you can do, Mage can do better;\u2669<br /> \u2669Mage can do anything better than you!\u2669<br /> \u2669No, it can't! Yes, it can! No, it can't! Yes it can, yes it can, yes it can!\u2669<br /> \u2014 with apologies to <i>Annie Get Your Gun</i></div>Agreed about <i>Mage</i> getting exponential growth: raising an Arcanum by one gives immediate access to multiple new spells and a stronger showing (i.e., more free Reach) with all existing spells in that Arcanum. If it's a Ruling Arcanum, the mage <i>also</i> gets a stronger showing (i.e., more free levels in the primary spell factor) with all spells in the Arcanum, both new and established. That's not counting Attainments and Praxes. <br /> <br /> By contrast, in <i>Vampire</i> you need to buy or improve each power you have individually; and you don't get supplemental experiences to speed things up, either, the way mages do. (Exception for when you use the Mage-inspired blood magic system in, I think, Blood and Treachery?, in place of the normal Cruac and/or Theban Sorcery rules.)<br /> <br /> Mage's exponential growth strikes me as the reverse of the issue that 1e <i>Werewolf</i> had, where the mechanics made it difficult for werewolves to advance power-wise. Fortunately, 2e has fixed that problem; but 2e's power development is still mostly linear, with each Facet being acquired individually.<br /> <br /> <i>Promethean</i> powers are weird: every Promethean gets eight powers (i.e., one Alembic from each of two Transmutations, each with an escalating* set of four powers) automatically, and those free powers shift around as the Created changes Refinements. Mastering Roles gives you an additional pair of Alembics (again, one from each Transmutation; eight more powers) whenever you're in that Refinement. Basically, it's a try-before-you-buy setup, with a potentially massive swing in how many and which powers you have access to at any given time. When it comes to actually buying the powers, you never buy them individually; you always buy them in sets of four (i.e., as Alembics) in the form of keeping one of the Alembics you had been trying out when you change things up. (There's also a \u201cmagic item\u201d \u2014 an Athanor \u2014 you can try to make when you master a Refinement that lets you retain access to <i>all of its powers</i> and sundry benefits after you've moved on to your next Refinement.) When actual, irreversible <i>growth</i> occurs, it's linear; but it's a <i>fast</i> linear, four powers at a time. I can actually see a Promethean \u201ckeeping up with the mages\u201d in a power escalation race by cycling through the Roles as quickly as possible and locking in new powers as soon as they're acquired. Not that I'm encouraging power escalation races, mind you. <br /> <br /> We've got spoilers on <i>Changeling</i> 2e's Contracts; but I'm not recalling specifics. I <i>think</i> 2e's Contracts would experience linear growth like Disciplines and Gifts, with power buildup occurring one power at a time. <br /> <br /> There are no specifics known about the 2e powers of <i>Hunter</i> or <i>Geist</i>, as those games are too early in the development cycle; and <i>Mummy</i> 2e hasn't even been announced (yet?). But barring radical reenvisioning of their power structures (such as what happened with Promethean), Hunter Endowments will mostly be one-power-at-a-time growth while Geist's Keys and Manifestations will provide multiplicative growth: each Key you acquire unlocks one power per Manifestation that you know, and each Manifestation that you attain grants one power per Key that you have. And Mummy's Descent mechanic means that they deal with an overall power <i>drop</i> over time. <br /> <br /> <i>Demon</i>, <i>Beast</i>, and <i>Deviant</i>: I think all three are one-power-at-a-time growth, with Deviant making it easy to escalate how much a power can do \u2014 but due to the link between powers and Scars, that's not a good thing: it's been suggested that such Blowouts tend to end in the Deviant's death. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Summarizing</u></b> <br /> Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling\u2020, Hunter\u2020, Demon, and Beast operate off of \u201cpower creep\u201d paradigms, where it's assumed that how much and what your powers can do increases slowly but surely. Mage, Geist\u2020, and Deviant\u2020 operate off of various \u201cescalating power\u201d paradigms, where your power level never decreases, and <i>can</i> increase very quickly. Promethean and Mummy\u2020 operate off of \u201cfluctuating power\u201d paradigms, where your power level sometimes increases and sometimes decreases. <br /> <br /> I think that tackling the \u201cMages can do everything others can do better\u201d issue needs to be done, but in the context of these various power development paradigms. Sure, mages escalate quickly; but what does that mean in a Mage/Mummy game where one protagonist's powers are on the rise while another's are in decline? The solution may not be as straightforward as \u201cnerf the Mages!\u201d or \u201cbuff everyone else!\u201d<br /> <br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* That is, how many of these powers you have access to depends on how much Pyros you're willing to invest in the Alembic, from zero to three.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2020 Speculative, as the ChroD-compatible editions aren't out yet.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:54:06-07:00","id":957380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957269#post957269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooner or Later,the devs will have to tackle the whole &quot;Mages can do everything the others can do better&quot; issue</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWake me when a Mage can <i>reflexively </i>hit you in the face with a literal truck like a Vigor/Celerity Vampire can.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe issue does not exist. In actual play, the Vampire with Dominate 2 is the go to character for mind control, not the Mage with Mind 2. He's much less likely to screw it up. The Mind Mage has access to a whole set of things his Vampire ally doesn't, but Psychic Domination is a poor substitute for Iron Edict, <i>for the types of effects Iron Edict can actually do</i>. You'd only use it if you absolutely need to do something that Iron Edict *can't* do. Similarly, it takes a three dot Mind effect to temporarily alter a memory, and a Dominate Vampire can do that *permanently* at one dot. Mage effects often exceed the limits of the other splats, but they're far more complicated, fragile, prone to blowing up in the Mage's face, slower, and generally more limited in duration or have higher requirements to accomplish the same thing. Duplicating the effect of Oubliette is, for example, next to if not completely impossible, and would require multiple spells to even attempt; spell control slots are very limited in 2e, and running out of them greatly increases paradox risk, other splat's powers generally don't have to worry about that kind of thing and have no issue stacking multiple longer duration effects.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust looking at the spell effects without the context of the rest of Mage's rules paints a very incomplete picture (f'rex, Gnosis requirements for increasing Arcana has a number of important implications in terms of power growth pacing in a mixed group, and they aren't to the Mage's benefit). There is more than sufficient niche protection mixing Mages and other Splats. Hell, Mages work best in mixed groups as utility and support.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: in light of Dataweaver's post, I'll expand on the Gnosis requirement thing a tiny bit, only looking at Vampires for simplicity: it costs a Mage that starts with a Ruling Arcanum at 3 and Gnosis at 1 48 experiences to take that Ruling Arcanum to 5. To contrast, it costs a Vampire with a starting in clan Discipline at 3, 6 experiences to get it to 5. Mages are also capped in terms of how high they can take their other Arcana without upping Gnosis, Vampires are not; it only costs 40 experiences to increase 2 out of clan disciplines from zero to 5, so our example Vampire can have 3 disciplines at 5 and still be 2 experiences shy of what it cost the Mage to become a Master in one Arcana (or 12 experiences shy if they're in clan instead), it will cost the Mage an additional 17 experiences to get their second ruling Arcana to 5, assuming they started it at 2. Additionally, Mages are the only group that uses a combination of 2 traits for their dice pools, rather than three. Vampires do not use Blood Potency as part of their dice pools to activate powers, so that starting Vampire that threw those first 6 experiences into a Discipline is not significantly impaired by the low BP. Yantras and Arcane Experiences are necessary to mitigate what would otherwise be crippling disadvantages. The effectiveness of increasing a dot of Arcana vs increasing a dot in a Discipline isn't just a matter of what you get, it also matters how much it costs. And Vampire powers are dramatically cheaper; you *should* be getting less for them. (Sidenote: the power increase for Arcana isn't exponential. That means something very specific dammit! It's more arguably logarithmic; going from 1-2 definitely feels like a bigger increase than 4-5, but putting aside the narrative effectiveness of the practices, the increase in mechanical 'stuff' is linear, you get one extra die, one extra reach, etc, every dot you go up. That you get more than you get from other power systems is baked into the higher costs and has nothing to do with the growth curve)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 08-25-2016, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:00:14-07:00","id":957382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957042#post957042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And when one's lack of self-control represents a clear and previously demonstrated danger to others?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a dream-monster that feeds itself when it's hungry by giving other people bad dreams. What your subconscious does in the realms of the subconscious while you are unconscious is both beyond any reasonable application of &quot;self-control&quot; and well below most sensible thresholds of &quot;danger.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Separate issue: Isn't it established that the Beast (namely, the human identity) decides when to <i>actively</i> feed, as opposed to the Starving induced nightly feeding rampages of the Horror? If so, then she <i>choose</i> to target him, subconscious weighting or not. </div> </div> </div>The story makes it quite explicit that that instance <i>was</i> the Horror's midnight snacking and that after that altercation she started making an effort to maintain her Satiety at a higher level, unless you somehow feel that Sandhya being <i>asleep</i> at the time of this incident constitutes an active decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Mostly we can conclude that at least some part of her <i>really</i> does not like Hal.) </div> </div> </div>It's her subconscious. &quot;Like&quot;/&quot;don't like&quot; is seldom so clean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Sentence derailment. 08-25-2016, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:04:51-07:00","id":957385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957354#post957354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've got spoilers on <i>Changeling</i> 2e's Contracts; but I'm not recalling specifics. I <i>think</i> 2e's Contracts would experience linear growth like Disciplines and Gifts, with power buildup occurring one power at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contracts have dot ratings but are no longer linked lists and instead &quot;grow&quot; by adding affinity powers that individual seemings get for free; they all run on an Attribute + Skill + Wyrd dicepool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T23:37:59-07:00","id":957431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957380#post957380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bEdit: in light of Dataweaver's post, I'll expand on the Gnosis requirement thing a tiny bit, only looking at Vampires for simplicity: it costs a Mage that starts with a Ruling Arcanum at 3 and Gnosis at 1 48 experiences to take that Ruling Arcanum to 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? 4 dots of gnosis = 20xp, 2 Arcana Dots = 8. Where's the extra 20 coming from here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:57:45-07:00","id":957474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957107#post957107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing Breeds is considered by a great many CofD fans to be a less than stellar addition to the setting and rules, and best forgotten or ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little known fact: Most of that book writers/developers used pseudonyms in the work's credits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:27:01-07:00","id":957512,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"614\" data-vbnamecard=\"614\">Eolirin</a> I still think you're very much overstating Mage's weaknesses and the advantages others have, even ignoring the XP costs being incorrect. Nobody's saying Mages lack weaknesses and others lack strengths, but the main point is the number of advantages Mages have so overwhelms that when it comes to mixed games and balance.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to go into a multi-paragraph tirade like last time, since I doubt you'll be swayed, so I'll just condense it down to you're understating Mage costs and the growth purchasing extra dots gets you. Whether exponentially is the mathematically correct term or not, Mages do NOT grow linearly AT ALL. It's linear for a singular spell, but then you get a new level of even more powerful spells, increasing the power of everything beneath at the same time. Maybe polynomial growth is the more correct term, but you can't exactly plot power to math anyway in a system like this. But still, you're growing faster than you're paying XP (I don't agree with the Gnosis argument, since Gnosis is powerful and important anyway, and already helped along by the mentioned arcane beats, and other Power Stats are actually worth buying now).<br /> <br /> Also, you're NOT always going to default to iron edict if you have a choice between the two, even at two dots. There are definitely circumstances where the spell is better, even for someone with just mind 2, especially if you're willing to risk paradox and/or with certain attainments added in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-25-2016, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:10:15-07:00","id":957531,"title":"","content":"As we said at GenCon (I think it was the CofD panel) the games are designed for interoperability (they have the same skill list, we have things like Supernatural Tolerance and Clash of Wills, unified spirit systems, etc) but not parity (so, yes, your mages, mummies, and demons are noticeably more powerful than vampires, who would be tough fights for hunters and deviants)<br /> <br /> How that relates to the Crossover Chronicle... Who knows!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:15:11-07:00","id":957534,"title":"","content":"Math while half asleep is bad idea. Apologies. <br /> <br /> And I said you'd use Iron Edict whenever Iron Edict's effect was what you were after, which is, in my experience, most of the time. It is better at doing what it does than Psychic Domination is at replicating it. You will obviously use Psychic Domination when you need to do something Iron Edict can't do. The same hold true for much of the other powers in the other lines. I'm not arguing that mages aren't extremely flexible in what they can do and that that isn't an advantage, just that speaking as an ST, mages can only overshadow other splats if you don't structure your scenes to make sure their limitations come into play. Magic generally doesn't replace or invalidate the other splats' powers. It does create a tension between the narrower thematic and role focus of the other lines and the broader generalist focus of Mage, but dealing with that isn't a mechanical issue with power levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:57:37-07:00","id":957581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957531#post957531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we said at GenCon (I think it was the CofD panel) the games are designed for interoperability (they have the same skill list, we have things like Supernatural Tolerance and Clash of Wills, unified spirit systems, etc) but not parity (so, yes, your mages, mummies, and demons are noticeably more powerful than vampires, who would be tough fights for hunters and deviants)<br /> <br /> How that relates to the Crossover Chronicle... Who knows!</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows? Hopefully the Crossover Chronicle developer and writing team!<br /> <br /> Given the very contentious nature of crossover and issues like &quot;game balance, when the book finally drops, these people will either be conquering heroes or the hated lepers to the CofD fanbase. I really hope they don't screw things up.<br /> <br /> BTW, Dave, are you assigned any of the writing in the book, and who's the developer?<br /> <br /> In any event, I'll likely buy the book for no other reason than it'll likely finally answer my Mage / Changeling crossover questions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:58:15-07:00","id":957583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957474#post957474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Little known fact: Most of that book writers/developers used pseudonyms in the work's credits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot say I'm surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:19:21-07:00","id":957603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957354#post957354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u2669Anything you can do, Mage can do better;\u2669<br /> \u2669Mage can do anything better than you!\u2669<br /> \u2669No, it can't! Yes, it can! No, it can't! Yes it can, yes it can, yes it can!\u2669<br /> \u2014 with apologies to <i>Annie Get Your Gun</i></div></div> </div> </div> </div> Hahahahah! Awesome! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood and Treachery?, </div> </div> </div> <i>Blood Sorcery: Blasphemies and Sacraments</i>. Most people either refer to the book by the first or last part, rarely the whole.<br /> <br /> Yep, Changeling powers are still linear. Here's the thing - every Contract has a basic ability you get with a success on the roll. Exceptional successes tend to be on the level of an entirely new power altogether. And Seeming variations are third way to cheaply get entirely new abilities. Its all linear, but there's a lot of punch in each ability, and they're dirt cheap. The drawback is that the dice pools are entirely based on Wyrd and other skills / attributes, requiring one to build on those to get reliable dice pools or the exceptional successes, encouraging growth outside of direct Contract purchases in a wide variety of areas. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, unless you have a rote skill you're very keen on, a mage never needs to purchase a mundane Skill or Attribute for the full breadth of their abilities. Its always Gnosis + Arcana + Yantra. That's something no other supernatural can say - everyone else relies on mundane talent to some extent. Mages can totally ignore Fallen World talents. It says something about the game that's completely off topic here (and not in a bad way, so lets not start flaming).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957380#post957380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWake me when a Mage can <i>reflexively </i>hit you in the face with a literal truck like a Vigor/Celerity Vampire can.</div> </div> </div> </div> Consider yourself woke. Or, dare I say, Awakened?<br /> <br /> Vampires' can't hit you in the face reflexively, they still need to spend a turn actually performing the physical act. The only reflexive part here is boosting the power of the hit. Also? No vampire can pick up an actual truck with their bare hands - physics does not work that way, the truck would break off whatever you were picking it up by first. So, literally is not quite literal in this case.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, mages can use the Fate 2 Atttainment, Conditional Duration, and Matter 5 to cause a truck to be created and smack you in the face (well, entire body) without even using a reflexive action. Fate 2 and Forces 3 if you just want to smack someone in the face with the power of a speeding truck. Fate / Time could probably arrange you being hit by a runaway truck, or something like that. Lots of ways to hit people with trucks through the Arcana.<br /> <br /> You exaggerate the vampire's abilities while missing the mage's abilities. You want to say a power discrepency is not an issue, fine. But your examples are heavily based on misrepresentation and false information. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIn actual play, the vampire with Dominate 2 is the go to character for mind control, not the Mage with Mind 2. He's much less likely to screw it up. The Mind Mage has access to a whole set of things his Vampire ally doesn't, but Psychic Domination is a poor substitute for Iron Edict, <i>for the types of effects Iron Edict can actually do</i>. You'd only use it if you absolutely need to do something that Iron Edict *can't* do. Similarly, it takes a three dot Mind effect to temporarily alter a memory, and a Dominate Vampire can do that *permanently* at one dot. Mage effects often exceed the limits of the other splats, but they're far more complicated, fragile, prone to blowing up in the Mage's face, slower, and generally more limited in duration or have higher requirements to accomplish the same thing. Duplicating the effect of Oubliette is, for example, next to if not completely impossible, and would require multiple spells to even attempt; spell control slots are very limited in 2e, and running out of them greatly increases paradox risk, other splat's powers generally don't have to worry about that kind of thing and have no issue stacking multiple longer duration effects. </div> </div> </div> Okay, first of all, a Mage only needs Mind 2 to make someone forget (Memory Hole), and that spell can be made Indefinite and either released from control or given to a Sleepwalker. The spell you're thinking of (Read the Depths) is actually the equivalent of Auspex 4 <i>combined with Dominate's memory wiping powers</i>. <br /> <br /> Oubliette is easily reproducable with sympathetic casting of the Imposter and Incognito Presence. That's Mind 3 and Space 2, a starting Mastigos character, who can reproduce full mastery of Obfuscate. And, unlike Obfuscate 5, the mage can set this up so that they can affect things outside of their established territory, making them far more effective at this little game. And that's assuming we don't Creative Thaum a custom spell with a large area that lets you affect things at whim - and it would still be a Mind 3/Space 2 spell, just with a large area. <br /> <br /> I also find the idea that mages are highly limited in Spell Control to be vastly overrated. All you need to do is either relinquish the spell or have a Sleepwalker hold on to the magic. Or, to be frank, be willing to court Paradox. I personally haven't felt restrained by Spell Control in the little bit of Mage I've played. <br /> <br /> Yes, mage powers are far more complex, and there is a limit to using them in rapid fire in terms of Spell Control, Paradox, available mana and Yantra. But here's the thing where your argument falls apart. You're trying to directly compete against another supernatural to directly reproduce exact powers. We don't need to do that. There are a ton of other angles we can attempt to solve an issue without needing to directly reproduce an exact power from another splat. A vampire would need to mind control a guard to wipe the security footage and make them forget. A mage could simply borrow an imbued item from his Order and remotely destroy everything. Or rouse a technology spirit / ghost to do it. Or use space magic. Or be obvious and just use an EMP to destroy everything electronic. White room comparisons are generally going to be innately pointless, and this is not one of the exceptions. Without context, you can't say that one supernatural's powers are better than another's. <br /> <br /> Hell, the desires of the two supernaturals are vastly different. If a mundane sees a vampire doing their thing and remembers, its a Masquerade breach that needs to be fixed. If a mundane sees a mage casting magic and remembers, you grab her ass and drag her to safety, she's a bloody Sleepwalker. That's a cause of celebration.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> The problem with mages in a crossover troupe is the threat of overshadowing other PCs. Direct power levels don't really matter so long as every member of the game settles into their own unique niche. An Myst/Acanthus occult investigator, a Rahu/Blood Talon combat monkey, an Invictus/Ventrue social butterfly and a Winter Darkling spy/thief can all get along in the same group and have fun together, so long as we avoid personality clashes and everyone stays in their niche. The problem with mages is that the flexibility of their magic lets them easily enter into combat as an equal to the werewolf, engage in social manipulation on par with the vampire, and can engage in rogue operations equal to the changeling. The mage ends up dominating the group as a result in such a case. Our theoretical diviner, once they have enough experience, can effectively shut down any combat, manipulate people effectively with Blessings and Curses, and use magic to supplement any covert operations. With Eregore, our witch can even just rent magical items instead of learning the appropriate Arcana themselves!<br /> <br /> When one PC has the answer to everything, it makes everyone else in the group feel redundant and overshadowed. And that's a huge problem here. All social groups, from ants to human workforces to wolves in a hunt, to animals. We are drawn to establish niches that can contribute to the group as a whole. Mages, by virtue of their flexible powers, tend to break from the standard niches, which is the heart of the problem in this case. Others have stated that, when the mage tend to step back and get less involved in the games, everyone has fun in the games. This isn't because mages are less involved, but rather that the mage player is helping to reinforce the niches instead of breaking them. And that's not an easy player skill to cultivate.<br /> <br /> Now, crossover troupes aren't the only kind of kind of crossover. I tend to create four levels:<ul><li>Crossover troupes, where everyone is a different supernatural</li> <li>Antagonism between splats (ie Hunters versus anyone else, vamps v. wolves, etc)</li> <li>Casual interaction (ie Beasts making friends with everyone)</li> <li>Cameos (other supernaturals show up for a brief plot in some role, then vanish)</li> </ul>We already talked about the full crossover troupes. Now, lets look at the other three. In a cameo, its not really an issue, because the ST has enough control over the NPCs in either case that it won't affect anything long term. Casual interaction and antagonism is where the issues lie.<br /> <br /> Mages in casual interaction can be problematic because they have the insatisfiable desire to <i>know</i>. For non-mage PCs, this can be upsetting, because they generally have no way of blocking a mage's abilities to learn stuff, even private matters, without some rather extreme responces (which ups the interaction to antagonism). This is why I agree with the earlier statement about mages being considered <i>invasive</i>. Because with a mage, your expectations of privacy are only as good as the mage's morals, or maybe a good Social Maneuvering build. Meanwhile, from the other side? Mage PCs get to be all invasive to their heart's content, which I personally think should be a Wisdom breaking point. Its actually a good source of Arcane beats, which encourages you to go deeper and deeper into the issue. The problem I have is that I think gathering the info is too easily done, and needs rather creative STs to come up with appropriate measures to engage the plot without devolving into an antagonistic relationship.<br /> <br /> An antagnoistic relationship is where things go to hell in a handbasket. The Arcana is simply designed to ignore the basic defensive abilities of supernaturals. This is a design decision for how mages think about other mages as antagonists. Which is more important for a game, but it completely messes with any and all crossover assumptions and challenges. Other supernaturals need to try to attack mages from the holes in their considerable defenses with clever results, while a mage can use direct attacks if they so wish. Victory may not be a given, but there's definitely a major bias towards mages as a result of the game's design. I believe it was DaveB even said that mages are inappropriate enemies for the Vigil, and you should use Witches instead. I think the same logic applies to other supernaturals. There are entire threads out there about addressing this discrepency, including using blood magic/goblin vows/wolf rites to create Shielding effects, to how to apply Supernatural Tolerance, to how to make mages into better antagonists for others, etc. I'm not going to reproduce them here, but only note that, given the massive amount of conversations, it clearly is a problem at a large number of tables. If your specific table doesn't have a problem, great. That doesn't help that there are a notable number of tables that do, and that will need to be addressed in any crossover book. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, is Mage the only game with issues in crossover? No, not at all. <br /> <br /> Promethean and Vampire both have notable issues. Prometheans, with Disquiet and Wastelands, tend towards short lived interactions before they have to move on. Even Silver Refeinement isn't meant to be a long term crossover game, and that's if the Refinement comes up, and if the Refinement targets something other than spirits and ghosts as valid targets instead of something more crossover-y. And it should be noted that Silver's signature Transmutation tends towards magic to face off against other supernaturals antagonistically, or hide/run away from them, rather than encourage interaction. With Vampire? The issue here is daylight restrictions, which is actually a very significant hurdle back in 1e to the point of inplayability in many games. I haven't tried it in 2e yet, so I can't comment about the new daylight rules. Both of these are hurdles that need to be overcome for a crossover game to be successful. <br /> <br /> With werewolves and chagnelings, a heavy issue is the presence of the Hisil and Hedge, respectively. The heavy influence of these other worlds practically requires any crossover to be able to deal with them as well to an extent if there's any significant interaction. There's nothing more anticlimatic than a werewolf dealing with a vampire infestation problem simply by making a deal with Helios spirits to do everything for them and the vamps having no recourse. Or having a demon exposed by asking spirits who happen to follow the spy. <br /> <br /> The Hunter problem is, generally speaking, the fact that hunters tend to have other supernaturals as enemies. Being allies means you're a cancer cult. Demons risk exposure and basically dying out from angels just from having a troupe and acting out of character.<br /> <br /> And so on. Mage is a complex game, and that means we get complex problems with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:23:10-07:00","id":957608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957382#post957382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a dream-monster that feeds itself when it's hungry by giving other people bad dreams. What your subconscious does in the realms of the subconscious while you are unconscious is both beyond any reasonable application of &quot;self-control&quot; and well below most sensible thresholds of &quot;danger.&quot;<br /> <br /> The story makes it quite explicit that that instance <i>was</i> the Horror's midnight snacking and that after that altercation she started making an effort to maintain her Satiety at a higher level, unless you somehow feel that Sandhya being <i>asleep</i> at the time of this incident constitutes an active decision.<br /> <br /> It's her subconscious. &quot;Like&quot;/&quot;don't like&quot; is seldom so clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Summary: Operating on information others have commented on. Statements implied it was a deliberate (not automatic at Starving) feeding. I wasn't sure, and <i>did</i> make sure to establish the situation is different if the original assumptions change (as included in your quotation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:54:42-07:00","id":957621,"title":"","content":"Well MCN covered any response I mightve had for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"614\" data-vbnamecard=\"614\">Eolirin</a> about Mages so Ill leave that be as it was starting to get into agree to disagree territory anyway.<br /> <br /> I do have more to add overall but Im now on my phone which makes typing difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:55:38-07:00","id":957677,"title":"","content":"I would add to MCN's discussion that the Adamantine Arrows have a Merit that lets them cast a spell concurrently with punching you in the face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:17:02-07:00","id":957689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957677#post957677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add to MCN's discussion that the Adamantine Arrows have a Merit that lets them cast a spell concurrently with punching you in the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick - <i>Adamant Hand</i> Merit give you ability to cast right<b> after </b>punching you in the face. Still, Arrows can do this:<br /> <br /> Turn 1: Attack you<br /> Turn 2: Cast spell on you using attack from Turn 1 as Mudra roll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-26-2016, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:19:59-07:00","id":958002,"title":"","content":"One point I want to make is that with 'linear' characters, fixes for crossover are easier, even with large discrepancies. Yes, Demons are more powerful than Vampires, but Demons still use (mostly) linear power advancement. So, you can give Vampires extra Experience to cover the innate power gap, and then if dealing with power discrepancy in the realm of &quot;Y Power gives you +X benefit over the same XP amount for a vamp buying a power&quot;, increase the XP cost of Demon's abilities, or lower vampire's (probably the former).<br /> <br /> Admittedly, you do need to figure out a good amount for both that doesn't tip vampire over the edge or end up not being enough. The same goes with any other 'linear' discrepancies. The lack of parity doesn't matter because it's easier to fix, though still takes some effort. I imagine that's one of the easier fixes they can put into the book for certain crossovers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T23:00:49-07:00","id":958074,"title":"","content":"Of course, if power levels are an issue, one could always hack the rules- mage chroniclers guide, danse macabre, vampire chroniclers guide, armory reloaded, werewolf chroniclers guide, equinox road (I think, I can never remember which stuff is in which changeling book for some reason), and even other books have options to increase or decrease the power levels to taste. <br /> <br /> While of course one might be reluctant to play with the rules in an existing campaign, in a game specifically designed for a crossover is a perfect opportunity to play with things to get the esult one wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T00:35:08-07:00","id":958091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958002#post958002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One point I want to make is that with 'linear' characters, fixes for crossover are easier, even with large discrepancies. Yes, Demons are more powerful than Vampires, but Demons still use (mostly) linear power advancement. So, you can give Vampires extra Experience to cover the innate power gap, and then if dealing with power discrepancy in the realm of &quot;Y Power gives you +X benefit over the same XP amount for a vamp buying a power&quot;, increase the XP cost of Demon's abilities, or lower vampire's (probably the former).<br /> <br /> Admittedly, you do need to figure out a good amount for both that doesn't tip vampire over the edge or end up not being enough. The same goes with any other 'linear' discrepancies. The lack of parity doesn't matter because it's easier to fix, though still takes some effort. I imagine that's one of the easier fixes they can put into the book for certain crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Demons are really powerful, they are also heavily constrained by the very real fear of the GM noticing them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T04:22:48-07:00","id":958136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958074#post958074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if power levels are an issue, one could always hack the rules- mage chroniclers guide, danse macabre, vampire chroniclers guide, armory reloaded, werewolf chroniclers guide, equinox road (I think, I can never remember which stuff is in which changeling book for some reason), and even other books have options to increase or decrease the power levels to taste.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, here's where we go back to the whole &quot;power balance is a myth&quot; stance. That stance is not quite true, since power does have a direct effect on niches within parties, providing challenges and conflict in stories, etc. But its also not entirely false either. Its not the amount of power that a PC has that's the main issue here (ie the character's &quot;level&quot;). Its the breadth of abilities. Variety of abilities tends to be more game breaking that directly boosted dice pools or the like.<br /> <br /> Most of the hacks you're talking about directly boost supernatural's current abilities to make them stronger, or weaker, or whatever. But they don't increase the variety of abilities - it doesn't matter how much in the way of a power boost vampires and changelings get, if the opponent can simply hang out on the other side of the Guantlet and avoid everything. Those power boosts do nothing to address that issue in a crossover game.<br /> <br /> Its worth keeping in mind that games with elder vampires (more xp than the rest of the party), neonates, and a ghoul servant that ignores supernatural abilities is easily playable and everyone have fun. Same with werewolves and wolf bloods, changelings and their allies, and so on. Power isn't everything - its the ability to engage with the plot and challenges that are key. If you don't have that? Then the game is broken. And, yes, some amount of abilities are required for engaging with the plot and challenges in a lot of ways. If characters are being overshadowed, by either PCs or NPCs, then there's issues at play. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958091#post958091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Demons are really powerful, they are also heavily constrained by the very real fear of the GM noticing them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ish? There's a number of Embeds that are powerful as hell (no pun intended), and they don't exactly cause notice most of the time. Remember when the game was first released, and the healing-power Embed was actually better than the Exploit before talking about breaking things or risking Cover?<br /> <br /> That said, I'm honestly of the opinion that the big thing with Demons being considered so powerful is Going Loud, and all the free powers they get all the time. Demons start with 4 Embeds/Exploits, about 7 or so demon form abilities (a large number of which can be used subtly), and their innate abilities tied to spycraft, including Legend. When the Unchained unlock a Cypher, they get another free power and a free dot of Primum. That's more free stuff than almost anyone else. Of course, that &quot;free stuff&quot; is easily offset by just XP. So, by getting rid of Going Loud, can we really say that a demon is more powerful than, say, a changeling or werewolf with some extra powers under their belt?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-26-2016, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T04:31:21-07:00","id":958138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958091#post958091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Demons are really powerful, they are also heavily constrained by the very real fear of the GM noticing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but they were just an example. It does make a good point that there's no &quot;perfect&quot; Experience offset, because in a game where the GM is more prevalent, their powers aren't as universally usable, and thus are &quot;worth' less, but in a game where they're tagging along for something else and the GM is only a minimal concern, you may want a higher offset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:15:44-07:00","id":958153,"title":"","content":"Wow, only just stumbled on this thread; this is amazing news","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:27:38-07:00","id":958221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958136#post958136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm honestly of the opinion that the big thing with Demons being considered so powerful is Going Loud, and all the free powers they get all the time. Demons start with 4 Embeds/Exploits, about 7 or so demon form abilities (a large number of which can be used subtly), and their innate abilities tied to spycraft, including Legend. When the Unchained unlock a Cypher, they get another free power and a free dot of Primum. That's more free stuff than almost anyone else. Of course, that &quot;free stuff&quot; is easily offset by just XP. So, by getting rid of Going Loud, can we really say that a demon is more powerful than, say, a changeling or werewolf with some extra powers under their belt?</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes back to variety-of-powers. Depending on if you include the supplemental books (and why not?), Demons are crazy flexible with their selection of Form Abilities, Embeds, Exploits, and Interlocks/Lambdas derived from the former. And that's not even getting into the seriously open ended effects like Play On Words and Show Of Power (which outright copies most other abilities, albeit at reduced effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:38:06-07:00","id":958225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=956866#post956866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if Crossover gets an anthology and I get a story in it, he'll be back to insult new supernatural entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Hal the type to leave his Disquiet build just so it's easier for him to insult a Promethean? Or would he cleanse himself first in order for the insults to be pure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T09:18:38-07:00","id":958261,"title":"","content":"Demons do have <i>potential </i>access to wide variety of abilities, but so do changelings and werewolves for that matter (vampires kinda get screwed on that matter, which is why bloodlines with their unique abilities are so important). Its not a question of having access, but of practice. That's why Going Loud is so powerful - because it gets you not only full aether and Primum 10, but every Exploit and affinity Embed. That's a huge explosion of abilities at once, including social, investigative, combat, crafting, even stealth abilities that you can use to hide from angels who come hunting. That's why the Arcana are so powerful - because you have access to a wide variety of abilities for various situations with each level, even if you just want to focus on a certain style. All mages automatically learn shields, veils and attack spells, even if they don't want to. No one else has that particular issue.<br /> <br /> I mean, I haven't tried the game in a crossover situation with Going Loud banned and some tweaks. So I could be wrong. The point I'm making is just that its not something we can theorycraft, but will have to try out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-26-2016, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:21:42-07:00","id":958339,"title":"","content":"There's very little that you can't do with the right Gathra to the right spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:27:58-07:00","id":958386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958339#post958339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's very little that you can't do with the right Gathra to the right spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetishes shouldn't be overlooked for Werewolves. The ones that modify how Facets work can do some amazing things, and access to Influences is nothing to sneeze at.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:55:39-07:00","id":958399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958261#post958261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons do have <i>potential </i>access to wide variety of abilities, but so do changelings and werewolves for that matter (vampires kinda get screwed on that matter, which is why bloodlines with their unique abilities are so important). Its not a question of having access, but of practice. That's why Going Loud is so powerful - because it gets you not only full aether and Primum 10, but every Exploit and affinity Embed. That's a huge explosion of abilities at once, including social, investigative, combat, crafting, even stealth abilities that you can use to hide from angels who come hunting. That's why the Arcana are so powerful - because you have access to a wide variety of abilities for various situations with each level, even if you just want to focus on a certain style. All mages automatically learn shields, veils and attack spells, even if they don't want to. No one else has that particular issue.<br /> <br /> I mean, I haven't tried the game in a crossover situation with Going Loud banned and some tweaks. So I could be wrong. The point I'm making is just that its not something we can theorycraft, but will have to try out.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO what makes Demons so powerful isn't necessarily their breadth of powers (which helps, between Embeds, Exploits and Forms a 0xp demon can still have a dozen unique powers, not including template traits) or Going Loud (which, while potent, is rather costly). It's their ability to stay hidden and affect the world tangentially. Like Mages, Demons can solve problems without ever going near them, they can puppet circumstance and manipulate others so thoroughly that they rarely have to be on site. That ability to remain comparatively safe and hidden while manipulating the world in discreet ways, that's where Demon's strength comes from.<br /> <br /> Then there is the matter of flexibility. With the right Form, Embed and Exploit choices demons can be nearly as flexible as Mages. They can shuffle around skills so their always looking at 6+ dice on a roll, they can bend circumstance, be in two places at once, mimic any supernatural power, cause things to happen with a single word and (if they have the right Embeds/Exploits) do it without too much risk to Cover. I recall, shortly after Demon released, writing up a character who could basically just cause advantageous things to happen, and rewrite anything disadvantageous after the fact. That's something only Mages can match.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:10:06-07:00","id":958408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958399#post958399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something only Mages can match.</div> </div> </div> </div>To echo Malus and Xenorath, when it comes to the manipulation, you're overlooking werewolves, who can influence things from another world entirely without even having to be in the world of flesh. Vampires, for that matter. Possibly Changelings, with their dream influence and Talecrafting but I'm unsure how that works in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-26-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:23:41-07:00","id":958414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958408#post958408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To echo Malus and Xenorath, you're overlooking werewolves, who can influence things from another world entirely without even having to be in the world of flesh</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no. I just didn't touch on them. Werewolves can also be stupendous in power, all the splats can really when they play to their themes, but they do have to be slightly more hands on. But what I was referring to specifically in the &quot;something only Mages can match&quot; is the ability to screw with time and probability. Mages and Demons are, to my knowledge, the only splats that can screw with the past. No one else can say &quot;You know what? You didn't shoot me three turns ago, you shot your partner&quot;, or &quot;Actually, I wasn't here, none of this happened, I made a different choice four minutes ago&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mind you this evaluation is white-room-tacular. In actual play player, plot, and character variance throw all this theory craft out the window. Though this does make me want to run a game of shadowy manipulators, where everyone plays two characters, a standard character and a mastermind who secretly influences the plot. That'd be fun, and something all the splats could get in on in different ways (save perhaps Prommies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:27:28-07:00","id":958416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958408#post958408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To echo Malus and Xenorath, when it comes to the manipulation, you're overlooking werewolves, who can influence things from another world entirely without even having to be in the world of flesh. Vampires, for that matter. Possibly Changelings, with their dream influence and Talecrafting but I'm unsure how that works in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly seems like a great advantage werewolves have... until you realize Mages, Demons, and Beasts can enter that same world, and Changelings and Sin-Eaters have their own worlds with which to operate out of. Basically, Vampires, Prometheans, and possibly Mummies are the odd supernatural out when it comes to playing with an Otherworld.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not saying Werewolves <i>aren't</i> capable of subtle influence across dimension divides. I'm just saying it isn't exactly unique to them either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:38:49-07:00","id":958426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958414#post958414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no. I just didn't touch on them. Werewolves can also be stupendous in power, all the splats can really when they play to their themes, but they do have to be slightly more hands on. But what I was referring to specifically in the &quot;something only Mages can match&quot; is the ability to screw with time and probability. Mages and Demons are, to my knowledge, the only splats that can screw with the past. No one else can say &quot;You know what? You didn't shoot me three turns ago, you shot your partner&quot;, or &quot;Actually, I wasn't here, none of this happened, I made a different choice four minutes ago&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>We may be getting a time Gift soon but yes, that is a place where mages have a great advantage over basically everyone else. I'd include Demons. As versatile as a Demon can be, they're limited in ways a single mage isn't. White room, of course, a mage can have a very, very broad toolbox. But even outside of the white room, in a more realistic situation, a cabal is going to likely cover a good amount of the arcana between its members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958416#post958416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That certainly seems like a great advantage werewolves have... until you realize Mages, Demons, and Beasts can enter that same world, and Changelings and Sin-Eaters have their own worlds with which to operate out of. Basically, Vampires, Prometheans, and possibly Mummies are the odd supernatural out when it comes to playing with an Otherworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge and Underworld doesn't have the intimate connection to the real world that the Shadow does. Or at least didn't in first edition. And simple access to the world wasn't what I was talking about. The Shadow is full of spirits, which can be used to influence the real world, either through negotiation or force, or trapping them into an object and using their powers for your own. The 'essence' of a place can be sucked dry, a rite in another place can fill it full of activity, and these things can influence the real world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: I'm not saying Werewolves <i>aren't</i> capable of subtle influence across dimension divides. I'm just saying it isn't exactly unique to them either. </div> </div> </div>I specifically called it out because it allowed them to do something Demons and Mages were capable of doing, I did not say it was unique to them.<br /> <br /> All that said, from what little we know about the game it looks as if it will be light on the mechanics and heavy on storytelling advice. So I wouldn't hold my breath for any sort of 'universal balancer,' but I could definitely see advice for Pendragon's manipulating shadowmasters game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-26-2016, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:40:30-07:00","id":958428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958339#post958339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's very little that you can't do with the right Gathra to the right spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, however dealing with ephemerals is something anyone in the cofd can do, even muggles. <br /> <br /> Ghosts are valid subjects for social merits according to Book of the Dead.<br /> <br /> Anyone with unseen sense- god machine can potentially find, capture, and even hack infrastructure according to the God Machine Chronicles, so there can be muggles who can summon angels to do their bidding.<br /> <br /> And there are merits to communicate with spirits, from there it's just some social maneuvering to get this for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:45:20-07:00","id":958431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958414#post958414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no. I just didn't touch on them. Werewolves can also be stupendous in power, all the splats can really when they play to their themes, but they do have to be slightly more hands on. But what I was referring to specifically in the &quot;something only Mages can match&quot; is the ability to screw with time and probability. Mages and Demons are, to my knowledge, the only splats that can screw with the past. No one else can say &quot;You know what? You didn't shoot me three turns ago, you shot your partner&quot;, or &quot;Actually, I wasn't here, none of this happened, I made a different choice four minutes ago&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mind you this evaluation is white-room-tacular. In actual play player, plot, and character variance throw all this theory craft out the window. Though this does make me want to run a game of shadowy manipulators, where everyone plays two characters, a standard character and a mastermind who secretly influences the plot. That'd be fun, and something all the splats could get in on in different ways (save perhaps Prommies).</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XYXXhn9fMYs\" data-code=\"XYXXhn9fMYs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XYXXhn9fMYs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:31:05-07:00","id":958456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958431#post958431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XYXXhn9fMYs\" data-code=\"XYXXhn9fMYs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XYXXhn9fMYs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that movie is fine Demon fodder.<br /> <hr /><br /> Also, adding to my last post, I should explain where I'm coming from with the power evaluations. I tend to look on things through the eyes of the storyteller (as I primarily am), and thus look on 'balance' through the eye of what makes a good story. For instance, the Werewolves attacking from the shadow argument is fantastic plot fodder, and I can already think of interesting plots and challenges such a character could inspire. As a result what I tend to view as 'most powerful' has most to do with how hard it is to interact with. Allow me an example: Werewolves in the Shadow are tough to deal with, but may provide great opportunities to employ Loci and Abjuration rules, telling an exciting story about fighting unseen forces. Compare that to something like a Demon using Four Minutes Ago or a Mage with Shifting Sands, unless you are yourself a Mage (with two dots of time) it is functionally impossible to interact with these powers. The Demon pops sideways in time and the last four minutes didn't happen, nothing can be done about this.<br /> <br /> Mages and Demons have a lot of powers that can't easily be responded to. Take the Embed Lucky Break for example, no matter how hard you hide, no matter how many layers of obfuscation you put forward a Demon with Lucky Break can always find a lead, in a matter of minutes. And it can do more, it can help a Demon get out of jail, win a fight, take down doors, and so much more. Demons and Mages are loaded with effects like this, which make them fun to play, but potentially unpleasant to play alongside or against. Of course much of that comes down to the player, a disruptive player will be disruptive regardless of the splat, but it can still be a hurdle for crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T16:29:03-07:00","id":958481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958428#post958428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, however dealing with ephemerals is something anyone in the cofd can do, even muggles.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are valid subjects for social merits according to Book of the Dead.<br /> <br /> Anyone with unseen sense- god machine can potentially find, capture, and even hack infrastructure according to the God Machine Chronicles, so there can be muggles who can summon angels to do their bidding.<br /> <br /> And there are merits to communicate with spirits, from there it's just some social maneuvering to get this for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sherpa and tourists. Sherpa and tourists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T16:59:58-07:00","id":958490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957603#post957603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Promethean and Vampire both have notable issues. Prometheans, with Disquiet and Wastelands, tend towards short lived interactions before they have to move on. Even Silver Refeinement isn't meant to be a long term crossover game, and that's if the Refinement comes up, and if the Refinement targets something other than spirits and ghosts as valid targets instead of something more crossover-y. And it should be noted that Silver's signature Transmutation tends towards magic to face off against other supernaturals antagonistically, or hide/run away from them, rather than encourage interaction. With Vampire? The issue here is daylight restrictions, which is actually a very significant hurdle back in 1e to the point of inplayability in many games. I haven't tried it in 2e yet, so I can't comment about the new daylight rules. Both of these are hurdles that need to be overcome for a crossover game to be successful.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of sounding nitpicky (and I don't mean to slam anything, either), but two of the Spiritus Alembics aren't antagonistic at their core. One is for finding other supernatural creatures, and the other is useful to impersonate them, or at least fool them enough so the Mystic can get close enough to deal with them in a friendly manner. (Yes, okay, the 3 Pyros Distillation of that Alembic is for getting away if your ruse is discovered, but still.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:13:16-07:00","id":958498,"title":"","content":"This thread has convinced me that this book will likely have to deal with mechanical power differences some how.<br /> <br /> According to the Playtest Changeling have some tricks that other splats will find hard to deal with as well.<br /> <br /> Killing someone via dreams and the too solid tilt is hard for many splats to avoid.<br /> <br /> And the Contract of Abjuration will be a nightmare for many splats to deal with. There are others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T19:16:06-07:00","id":958560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957603#post957603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider yourself woke. Or, dare I say, Awakened?<br /> <br /> Vampires' can't hit you in the face reflexively, they still need to spend a turn actually performing the physical act. The only reflexive part here is boosting the power of the hit. Also? No vampire can pick up an actual truck with their bare hands - physics does not work that way, the truck would break off whatever you were picking it up by first. So, literally is not quite literal in this case</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMost of what you've said about Vampire disciplines is wrong:<br /> Celerity is activated reflexively. It lets you do this: &quot;Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of her own. This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by shifting out of reach. Or it could be any other instant action, like activating a Discipline or dodging.&quot; This means you can, in response to any action by any character, make an attack on them. This does not use your instant action for the turn, as you can activate it up to Celerity dots times in a turn.<br /> Vigor lets you do this: Lift and hurl objects normally far too unwieldy to use as weapons, such as boulders, cars, and other people. Any object she can lift, with Size no greater than her Strength, can be used as an improvised melee or throwing weapon\u200b.<br /> <br /> Picking up and throwing a nearby object is a single instant action as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo Celerity and Vigor very explicitly allow throwing of cars at people's face as a reflexive action, when used in conjunction. Physics saying you can't do this violates rule of cool, and gets ignored.<br /> <br /> Dominate One isn't a mind wipe a ability, it's a memory altering ability. You need Mind 3 to duplicate it, and going indefinite is a lot of dice penalties and leaves it open to dispellation, or if you don't spend a Willpower *dot* in relinquishing it, that the memory alteration will eventually start to change on you.<br /> <br /> Oubliette is a full sensory hallucination applied to a location that impacts everyone and everything inside of it, that can be updated at will. At minimum you're looking at needing Mind 4 and some amount of Space, and depending on how you read the rules on scale factors and what's actually being targeted, it may not be possible to apply the correct set of spells to impact everyone in the area in the same way that Oubliette does. Imposter and Incognito Presence are no where near sufficient. And even with properly scaled versions of Hallucinate, you'd have to recast the spell every single time you wanted to make a change. This is more or less impractical.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bBut I think I failed spectacularly at making something clear; I am not attempting to pit the splats in competition with each other, the context from which I'm operating is a mixed splat PC group. I am assuming<i> cooperation </i>between the splats. I was *trying* to say that in such a group the Dominate Vampire is not at all overshadowed by the Mind mage when it comes to using Dominate. In such a group the Mage is generally going to provide more utility by doing things like boosting the Vampire's Intelligence or lowering the target's Resolve than they are by trying to use Psychic Domination. Unless they really need to force a suicidal action or act outside the limits of Dominate, it's better to let the Vampire in the group do the mind control bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T20:44:32-07:00","id":958591,"title":"","content":"Celerity is limited to once per turn per effect, and Rating times per scene, not rating per turn. And explicitly DOES use your instant action up.<br /> <br /> And just to say it, both Werewolves and Mages have a far superior power for it (it's built in for Werewolves: urhan form).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-26-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T21:06:49-07:00","id":958596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958560#post958560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMost of what you've said about Vampire disciplines is wrong:<br /> Celerity is activated reflexively. It lets you do this: &amp;quot;Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of her own. This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by shifting out of reach. Or it could be any other instant action, like activating a Discipline or dodging.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I notice you conveniently left out the following two sentences, &quot;However, the vampire is still limited to one instant action. However, the vampire is still limited to one instant action. She cannot use Celerity to make two attacks, or an attack followed by another instant action.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958560#post958560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This means you can, in response to any action by any character, make an attack on them. This does not use your instant action for the turn,</div> </div> </div> </div>See above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958560#post958560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as you can activate it up to Celerity dots times in a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div> Scene. Celerity dots times in a scene. &quot;Finally, using Celerity in this way is exhausting; a vampire may only interrupt as many actions in a scene as she has dots in Celerity.&quot; Technically there's no reason you couldn't use up all your interrupts for the Scene in one turn if you wanted to (and had enough Blood Potency to spend that much Vitae in one turn, which is far from a given), but as per the above quote, only one of those actions could be something that's normally Instant, and you'd also be out of gas for the rest of the Scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:30:29-07:00","id":958684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=958560#post958560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMost of what you've said about Vampire disciplines is wrong:</div> </div> </div> </div> Others have covered where you are grossly mistaken about Celerity, so I'm just going to say this. Its a delieberate design decision by the developers and writers of Onyx Path that there will never be a power in 2e that lets you perform multiple Instant Actions in a turn. You will not be able to make multiple attacks on a person, or use two spells, or the like. The closest exception to this rule is hitting two or more people with a single attack, ala Two Weapon FS or long burst firearms. That's the extent. What you are suggesting goes against a design principle of the entire game. It will never happen. Not in the Arcana, not with Celerity, not with Fighting Styles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oubliette is a full sensory hallucination applied to a location that impacts everyone and everything inside of it, that can be updated at will. </div> </div> </div> Nooo..... Oubliette is creating an area of effect where you can activate the lower level abilities of Obfuscate at will. &quot;Once he has established an Oubliette, the vampire can use Touch of Shadow, Cloak of Night, and The Familiar Stranger at any distance, on anyone or anything within his haven.&quot; Nothing else. Touch of Shadow, Cloak of Night and Familiar Stranger are easily reproduced via the spells Imposter and Incognito Presence, Mind 3 and 2 respectively. Using said spells at sympathetic range just requires the Space 2 attainment. And that's assuming we don't just cast one of those two spells as a area of effect instead of individual targets.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, full sensory hallucinations are the domain of the Nightmare Discipline. Obfuscate isn't a hallucination power. That's two vampire abilities that you are grossly mistaken on the rules. I'm sorry, but you seem to have a giant misunderstanding of how Vampire powers actually work to the point we cannot have an honest comparison here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI was *trying* to say that in such a group the Dominate Vampire is not at all overshadowed by the Mind mage when it comes to using Dominate. In such a group the Mage is generally going to provide more utility by doing things like boosting the Vampire's Intelligence or lowering the target's Resolve than they are by trying to use Psychic Domination. Unless they really need to force a suicidal action or act outside the limits of Dominate, it's better to let the Vampire in the group do the mind control bits. </div> </div> </div> And I'm saying that we have people <i>with direct play experience</i> that disagree with you. Your white room theorcraft does not hold up in actual games, let alone inside of the white room itself.<br /> <br /> As well, your arguments are assuming that a mage will use Psychic Domination in all the same situations a vamp will use Dominate 1. They won't. Arcana let you pick different tools for the different jobs, whereas Disciplines don't have that flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-27-2016, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T11:59:30-07:00","id":958825,"title":"","content":"Relentless Assault 5: <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The Warpath (</span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">)</span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">: Your character kills, but does not stop her assault. Any time she fills a character\u2019s last health box with lethal or aggravated damage, she may immediately </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">make an additional attack against one other character within her reach. Doing so costs a point of Willpower, which does not add dice to the attack roll. </span><br /> <br /> Street Fighting 5 has a more situational second attack at 5 dots<br /> <br /> An exceptional success on a grapple roll allows for a damage move and one other maneuver. With the right merits Break Free or Drop Prone deal damage in addition to their normal effect.<br /> <br /> The circumstances are much more limited but multi attack powers absolutely do exist in 2e. And that's assuming Hurt Locker is pruned of all the other options it has before publication. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:04:28-07:00","id":959220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=957107#post957107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Changing Breeds is considered by a great many CofD fans to be a less than stellar addition to the setting and rules, and best forgotten or ignored. <br /> <br /> In your ample free time after your real life, developing Mage and Deviant and writing for almost everything else in the CofD, it would be great if you (and maybe Chris Allen) wrote a much needed 2e treatment for Changing Breeds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Breeds needs an overhaul . But beyond that he needs the treatment of major template , not a single Blue Book .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:49:18-07:00","id":959310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959220#post959220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing Breeds needs an overhaul . But beyond that he needs the treatment of major template , not a single Blue Book .</div> </div> </div> </div>Book didn't even had a sheet on it's back, for crying out loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:55:45-07:00","id":959535,"title":"","content":"The only issue of balance that is really important in games is between players and it isn't a matter of mechanics, it is a matter of focus. It is about how the Storyteller runs the game. For example, you have a group with two players. One has a character focused on social skills and powers and the other on combat skills and powers. The latter character can beat the crap out of the former one, but that ultimately doesn't matter in terms of game balance. What matters is that the game she runs has social stuff for the first character to do and combat stuff for the second character to do. This holds true whether all the characters are werewolves or if they are different sorts of creatures. The trick is running a campaign that makes sure that every character, regardless of the type or their abilities, has moments to do their thing and be in the limelight. If your two players are playing a vampire and a werewolf, you have to make sure that neither Machiavellian scheming nor spirit cop plots dominate (yes, I'm over-simplifying). Whether or not the vampire can beat up the werewolf or vice versa isn't really important.<br /> <br /> Power disparities will exist and these will inform conflicts and, hence, plots. Look at Hunter. Nobody thinks Hunters should be as powerful as vampires. The fact that they aren't is part of who they are and what makes the game interesting. Anyway, that's just my two cents but it is worth noting that I ran a World of Darkness MUSH back in the day with characters of pretty much every splat that existed at the time, so I know of what I speak. Two of my favorite plots during the life of the MUSH illustrate this. One involved a vampire hunter with no powers managing to assassinate several Kindred without getting caught and another involved a regular human stealing away with his Kinfolk daughter so she would be raised by the local Garou. In both cases, thorough and creative planning let them succeed. This is why the white room analysis that compares base powers isn't really useful, because it removes the role-playing element of the game and treats it like a war game or board game.<br /> <br /> Okay, going to stop talking now. Rambling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:20:13-07:00","id":959556,"title":"","content":"I don't like this approach, because it's based on idea that players are <br /> a) working as a team that delegates character roles (party face, party muscle, etc) [I'm biased here; we play a lot of games in a fantasy samurai setting where characters are often facing conflicting loyalties, and must handle discreet manners that you simply can't trust to someone outside of your family; you can't just go and ask your party face to negotiate a delicate deal that your father ordered you to oversee, for example; this means that characters can't &quot;cover&quot; for each other as much as in things like DnD; this type of play seems to be pretty popular in Chronicles, too)<br /> b) reduced to &quot;social guy&quot;, &quot;muscle guy&quot;, &quot;mental guy&quot;<br /> I dislike this design, because it basically means that when social encounter comes up, 3 out of 4 people are unable to engage with it competently; and so on. One of reasons why I really like CofD is that it's really easy and pretty encouraged to make characters that are competent in all 3 basic types of encounters (mental, social, physical) so unless you did so on purpose, you pretty much always can engage in given type of encounters. Which makes optimal use of our time.<br /> And while yeah, you &quot;physically focused character&quot; will get 11 points to spread around while someone else will only get 4, it doesn't mean that the last guy is drastically worse; usually it means that the first guy has more possible approaches, while second one has less possible roads to success; character with 11 in social skills can bribe, intimidate, persuade or trick their way out of an encounter; character with 4 points probably can only do one or two of these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:36:55-07:00","id":959564,"title":"","content":"Yeah I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>. Most of the time in Chronicles of Darkness, you make a character that fulfills a concept, not a party role like in other games. That concept will likely overlap several areas in small amounts, much of the time (A thuggish criminal probably can shoot and deal with the social workings of the criminal world, but likely sucks at doing acrobatics or maneuvering through high society, to give a very very simplified example). That unfortunately means there's plenty of room for, well, &quot;Everything you can do I can do better&quot;, in some cases, when powers and abilities are more wide-reaching. If a high society character's abilities also happen to make them an expert at maneuvering through street level issues, well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T01:06:40-07:00","id":959708,"title":"","content":"Here is an example of invasive special abilities clashing with concepts of other characters:<br /> In our current game, we have a person who decided that they want to be &quot;know it all&quot; type with massive scores of Occult and other mental knowledge skills. However, due to my character being a Fate Mage, I've discovered that I make him totally irrelevant and redundant - my magic can easily overcome the gap between our skills, and even without that, I'm simply better at &quot;knowing stuff&quot; because I can gain Informed Condition on demand using Exceptional Luck - which means that as long as I get 1 success on my Occult Roll, I actually get Exceptional Success guaranteed, which he - even with Occult of 5 - isn't producing in consistent manner. There is pretty much no point to his character theme, and choices he made at char gen are irrelevant, because my set of magic abilities overwrites it. In this case, it's a clear mechanical disbalance, not a Focus one. It's also pretty annoying to *me*, because I feel an obligation to self restrain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:13:52-07:00","id":959823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959708#post959708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is an example of invasive special abilities clashing with concepts of other characters:<br /> In our current game, we have a person who decided that they want to be &quot;know it all&quot; type with massive scores of Occult and other mental knowledge skills. However, due to my character being a Fate Mage, I've discovered that I make him totally irrelevant and redundant - my magic can easily overcome the gap between our skills, and even without that, I'm simply better at &quot;knowing stuff&quot; because I can gain Informed Condition on demand using Exceptional Luck - which means that as long as I get 1 success on my Occult Roll, I actually get Exceptional Success guaranteed, which he - even with Occult of 5 - isn't producing in consistent manner. There is pretty much no point to his character theme, and choices he made at char gen are irrelevant, because my set of magic abilities overwrites it. In this case, it's a clear mechanical disbalance, not a Focus one. It's also pretty annoying to *me*, because I feel an obligation to self restrain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually solved this same exact problem in one of my games:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, an exceptional success! You happen into book that happens to describe exactly what the phenomenon is...except then you start reading it, and it suddenly occurs to you it's invoking several obscure pieces of lore you have no freaking idea about. You simply don't have the expertise required to make sense of this, luck or no luck. Gained the Informed Condition in respect to indexing this particular library, but you're going to need help in decipher this thaumobabble.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, it relies on bending the rules a bit, but someone who doesn't have that high a Skill score is going to find truly impossible feats...impossible, because they don't have the background. Suggest the houserule 'It is forbidden to roll to decipher something I can't think of a reason I'd know how to decipher'. Even beyond that, someone with Occult 5 is going to be regarded as a prodigy-give the poor guy some free Contacts symbolizing students and would-be mystics who respect him (he doesn't have the Fame Merit because he doesn't have <i>popular </i>recognition). If he can't be the roll-monkey, then give him fluff buffs that come from other parts of the character concept.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's the Oberoni Fallacy (a broken rule you can houserule to fix is still broken), but the reason that fallacy exists is because it's what is meant to happen when the game group is adjusting a game to be more fun for the group.<br /> <br /> (It's also what Onyx Path has in mind when they say that fluff comes before rules, I think-because rules are built around fluff).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:12:38-07:00","id":959855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959220#post959220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing Breeds needs an overhaul . But beyond that he needs the treatment of major template , not a single Blue Book .</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem with changing breeds in part is that its not one splat, its a crap load of very different splats with some shared mechanics that generally have very different goals and intetests and histories with an over arching attempt to shoe horn them together via eco warrior hood.<br /> <br /> Some of the Changing Breeds individually had great fluff, like the various races of Bastet, with its hungry ghosts and Klinkerashes and so on, as well as the Land Titans and Medes (Goat Folk), but none of it meshed together all, none outside their over arching subgroups had any real meaningful commonality that drew all their really cool concepts togther.<br /> <br /> Why would the Bastets make common cause with Land Titans, beyond some basuc enviromental conversation, which is in everyones interest, human, vampire, ect... to.<br /> <br /> And the splats were very poorly balanced with each other.<br /> <br /> What Changing Breeds needs is either to have all of it tied together in a really tight way based on an original idea, or for all the subgroups of Changing Breed types to be completely seperate with their own themes.<br /> <br /> Example maybe the combined goal of the Changing Breeds is to restore Pangaea and the Pangaeans.<br /> <br /> Or break them up with the Bastets tracing their roots back to Bubastis, like how Mummies are tied to Irem, no matter where they are in the world or what form.<br /> <br /> Like maybe the Hungry Ghosts were the first Bastets and they were charged with protecting Basts heart, one of the last artifacts of Pangaea, but when the city fell, it got shatter in a particular and strange way, release energy into the world, that created the various types of other Bastets and the Hungry Ghosts became cursed because of thrir failure to defend her heart, do the goal of all the Bastets, but more so Hungry Ghosts, is rebuild her heart and restore the City of Bubastis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:27:55-07:00","id":959863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959823#post959823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually solved this same exact problem in one of my games:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, an exceptional success! You happen into book that happens to describe exactly what the phenomenon is...except then you start reading it, and it suddenly occurs to you it's invoking several obscure pieces of lore you have no freaking idea about. You simply don't have the expertise required to make sense of this, luck or no luck. Gained the Informed Condition in respect to indexing this particular library, but you're going to need help in decipher this thaumobabble.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, it relies on bending the rules a bit, but someone who doesn't have that high a Skill score is going to find truly impossible feats...impossible, because they don't have the background. Suggest the houserule 'It is forbidden to roll to decipher something I can't think of a reason I'd know how to decipher'. Even beyond that, someone with Occult 5 is going to be regarded as a prodigy-give the poor guy some free Contacts symbolizing students and would-be mystics who respect him (he doesn't have the Fame Merit because he doesn't have <i>popular </i>recognition). If he can't be the roll-monkey, then give him fluff buffs that come from other parts of the character concept.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's the Oberoni Fallacy (a broken rule you can houserule to fix is still broken), but the reason that fallacy exists is because it's what is meant to happen when the game group is adjusting a game to be more fun for the group.<br /> <br /> (It's also what Onyx Path has in mind when they say that fluff comes before rules, I think-because rules are built around fluff).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, make indexing it an extended task, thus the guy with 5 more rolls is obviously suitable to the task compared to the one with 4 at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:38:31-07:00","id":959867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959863#post959863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, make indexing it an extended task, thus the guy with 5 more rolls is obviously suitable to the task compared to the one with 4 at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Or, since the goal is &quot;find out a source of occult information in regards to X&quot;, your Mage gets a lead on a detailed source of information (due to their Informed Condition)... which is the occult character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:40:41-07:00","id":959869,"title":"","content":"Does anyone want Crossover information that doesn't involve mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T10:00:40-07:00","id":959877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959869#post959869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone want Crossover information that doesn't involve mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, plenty. How well do Unchained and Changeling interact, for one. Both use deals (albeit in different manners), both hide behind &quot;fake&quot; identities, both look over their shoulder for hunters. I could see fae Pledges being used to fortify Demon agreements (to the extent that they can), while Pacts make it easier for Changelings to reintegrate into society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T10:02:16-07:00","id":959878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959869#post959869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone want Crossover information that doesn't involve mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>-How to deal with a Promethean is a mixed group.<br /> -How to integrate a single X into a Y party<br /> -Vampires, or What do we do by Day?<br /> -How much should you keep from each game? (Courts? Covenants?)<br /> -Fixing what's not broken (Exorcising the Possessed/Bound, for example)<br /> -Antagonists, who's the villain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T12:23:59-07:00","id":959955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959869#post959869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone want Crossover information that doesn't involve mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's <b>Mage</b>-centric, but knowing what Arcana are related to what supernaturals and so which Active Mage Sight can 'detect'? Will Divine Fire of Promethean by Prime related? What about Matter looking over Created? Both vampires and Sin-Eaters or mummies are shown under Death? Are Unchained *pinging* in Prime?<br /> And most important - Are Beasts powers working as Mind related phenomena or Prime one? Like <i>Family Dinner </i>sounds as more second one, even if, in theory, their Horrors are giant Goetia beings.<br /> <br /> Because each decision like this make one Path more suitable to work this those beings, and more easier to find. You need to look for werewolves? You go to your known Thyrsus. You look for vampires? Your friendly Moros should help you. Acanthus are masters in uncovering changelings. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T14:45:52-07:00","id":960026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959878#post959878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -How to deal with a Promethean is a mixed group.<br /> -How to integrate a single X into a Y party<br /> -Vampires, or What do we do by Day?<br /> -How much should you keep from each game? (Courts? Covenants?)<br /> -Fixing what's not broken (Exorcising the Possessed/Bound, for example)<br /> -Antagonists, who's the villain?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind a list of effects attained from trying to drain Vitae from supernaturals either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:35:10-07:00","id":960052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959955#post959955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know it's <b>Mage</b>-centric, but knowing what Arcana are related to what supernaturals and so which Active Mage Sight can 'detect'? Will Divine Fire of Promethean by Prime related? What about Matter looking over Created? Both vampires and Sin-Eaters or mummies are shown under Death? Are Unchained *pinging* in Prime?<br /> And most important - Are Beasts powers working as Mind related phenomena or Prime one? Like <i>Family Dinner </i>sounds as more second one, even if, in theory, their Horrors are giant Goetia beings.<br /> <br /> Because each decision like this make one Path more suitable to work this those beings, and more easier to find. You need to look for werewolves? You go to your known Thyrsus. You look for vampires? Your friendly Moros should help you. Acanthus are masters in uncovering changelings. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flipping it, I'd like to see the book address 2e's position on the Mage/Promethean thing: in 1e, Pyros didn't fall under the purviews of <i>any</i> of the Arcana, despite superficial similarities with the Aether's imagery. Sure, there were a handful of spells for coping with various Pyros-related phenomena; but they were presented as the exception to the rule. Even as late as <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, where the book listed which Arcana would be needed to mess with various supernatural templates, it was oddly silent about Promethean-related stuff. I'm wondering whether 2e intends to keep this lack of relationship between Pyros and the Supernal, or if they're going to retcon it away. Likewise, I remember reading something about how the Hedge's Thorns affect various supernaturals, and Prometheans were given a pass on the usual deleterious effects, because the Wyrd doesn't recognize the existence of the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:39:57-07:00","id":960055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959878#post959878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -How to deal with a Promethean is a mixed group.<br /> -How to integrate a single X into a Y party<br /> -Vampires, or What do we do by Day?<br /> -How much should you keep from each game? (Courts? Covenants?)<br /> -Fixing what's not broken (Exorcising the Possessed/Bound, for example)<br /> -Antagonists, who's the villain?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope the book explores valid answers to these questions that keep to the features of each splat as written, but it also seems like a good place to introduce hacks that facilitate crossover or alleviate the lack of parity between splats in certain fields. The issue of Vampires in mixed games for one, could be the case to introduce alternate mechanics that allow them to regularly operate in daylight more easily at the cost of diminished or unavailable powers, \u00e0 la Dracula in Bram Stoker's book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:13:54-07:00","id":960111,"title":"","content":"Right; but every such rule has unintended consequences. For instance, letting vampires walk under the Sun diminishes the value of some Coils of the Dragon, whereby members of the Ordo Dracul get to do just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:30:45-07:00","id":960118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960111#post960111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right; but every such rule has unintended consequences. For instance, letting vampires walk under the Sun diminishes the value of some Coils of the Dragon, whereby members of the Ordo Dracul get to do just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, if it won't unbalance things, if your vampires are Ordo already, you could have them be established with that Coil, and thus give them a few dots. Or do something similar with blood sorcery rituals (though those would be custom).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:34:57-07:00","id":960122,"title":"","content":"Yes, that such rules can have notable ramifications must be a primary concern of those hacks. In this example, the presentation of the hack should at least acnowledge that it will make some Coils much less weighty or obsolete, and ideally introduce suggestions on how to make those powers still matter or alternate mechanics for those too as an extension of the basic hack.<br /> <br /> The possibility of unforseen edge-cases should also not be ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:47:27-07:00","id":960125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960055#post960055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the book explores valid answers to these questions that keep to the features of each splat as written, but it also seems like a good place to introduce hacks that facilitate crossover or alleviate the lack of parity between splats in certain fields. The issue of Vampires in mixed games for one, could be the case to introduce alternate mechanics that allow them to regularly operate in daylight more easily at the cost of diminished or unavailable powers, \u00e0 la Dracula in Bram Stoker's book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somebody came up with a houserule which did a good job with this. They called it &quot;Threshold&quot; (I can't remember who wrote this, but it's good).<br /> <br /> Essentially, Threshold measures the sense of home a structure holds and inhibits supernatural prowess accordingly. For instance, a home might have a Threshold of 2, reducing supernatural prowess by two within its walls. A Vampire within with Blood Potency 3 and Vigor 2 would have effective Blood Potency 1 and Vigor 0 (I'm paraphrasing; I don't remember all of the details).<br /> <br /> When I used that houserule, I gave sunlight the same effect (It was a <b>EDIT:</b>5 Threshold for Vampires) and had the Coil of the Ascendant reduce that Threshold. It'd be cool to see something like that.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Just checked my old notes. I didn't scale the sunlight Threshold with blood potency; it was a flat 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 08-29-2016, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:59:43-07:00","id":960136,"title":"","content":"I don't know if someone already already mentioned it but i really think that they should have a chapter on how the alternate dimensions and ephemeral entities interact with all of the splats. my brain gets headaches just thinking about mages inside the hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:23:43-07:00","id":960151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960055#post960055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope the book explores valid answers to these questions that keep to the features of each splat as written, but it also seems like a good place to introduce hacks that facilitate crossover or alleviate the lack of parity between splats in certain fields. The issue of Vampires in mixed games for one, could be the case to introduce alternate mechanics that allow them to regularly operate in daylight more easily at the cost of diminished or unavailable powers, \u00e0 la Dracula in Bram Stoker's book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depending on the splats involved, do you need such rules? Given the existence of Mages, Werewolves, etc. Might a Vampire be able to pick up a Fetish or Imbued Item to keep the sun off them? That's beyond the scope of <i>vampiric</i> power, but other forces don't treat the sun as so special.<br /> <br /> They'd still need to fight the urge to go to sleep, but that's in theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:29:42-07:00","id":960196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960151#post960151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the splats involved, do you need such rules? Given the existence of Mages, Werewolves, etc. Might a Vampire be able to pick up a Fetish or Imbued Item to keep the sun off them? That's beyond the scope of <i>vampiric</i> power, but other forces don't treat the sun as so special.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, use ghouls, because that's how they deal with the problem of not being able to go out in the daytime in the setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, though, those playing vampires should have a ghoul character to run during daylight hours. They aren't going to have access to the same kind of supernatural juju that their boss does, but they could easily have access to a lot of their mundane resources. That's part of playing a vampire. If you find a work-around for the daylight thing, are you going to find a way for werewolves to avoid rage? Or Disquiet for a Promethean? I mean, you could, to make it easier to play the multi-splat group, but I feel like it removes a large part of playing them. Of course, if that's okay with you, more power to you. For me, playing the downsides of the &quot;monsters&quot; in the CofD is half the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:42:25-07:00","id":960206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959564#post959564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>. Most of the time in Chronicles of Darkness, you make a character that fulfills a concept, not a party role like in other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to imply otherwise. Sorry if you got that impression. Character &quot;niches&quot; are complicated: a combination of themes, arenas, concept, and skills. My examples were, as noted, simplified in order to illustrate a particular point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a high society character's abilities also happen to make them an expert at maneuvering through street level issues, well... </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is handled more easily by the Storyteller running the game than mechanics or rules. Rulings not rules, and all that. Common sense should provide a number of obstacles to the high society character when they are trying to operate on the street level that I don't think need explicit rules. These are the sorts of things we have Storytellers for, after all. The same applies to the example someone gave of their Acanthus being able to outperform the Occult expert using only luck. It isn't hard to think of reasons why this shouldn't work (at least not consistently) and several folks have already noted ways the Storyteller could handle it. That's why I feel the Crossover book is better off giving advice on how to deal with these sorts of situations rather than trying to provide tons of new rules to try and mechanic them out of existence. For me, it is the same sort of futile effort as trying to make rules to thwart bad players. And, on that note, part of a player's responsibility is to make sure everyone at the table is having fun, not just them. If you are using your powers to stomp on someone else's character concept, the problem isn't the rules, it is you. I've had players before who made a habit of getting the same feats, gifts, whatever as other members of the party and &quot;stealing their schtick&quot; and it is a player problem, not a rule problem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T21:24:00-07:00","id":960220,"title":"","content":"I think part of the issue that was being pointed out is that due to their sheer versatility, mages have a tendency to \u201csteal their schtick\u201d <i>without meaning to</i>. With effort, this can be avoided; but it <i>takes</i> effort, more than usual, to avoid the mage's sheer array of options from rendering redundant most non-mages in similar fields. <br /> <br /> That is, it isn't always a player issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T23:02:15-07:00","id":960253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959855#post959855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with changing breeds in part is that its not one splat, its a crap load of very different splats with some shared mechanics that generally have very different goals and intetests and histories with an over arching attempt to shoe horn them together via eco warrior hood.<br /> <br /> Some of the Changing Breeds individually had great fluff, like the various races of Bastet, with its hungry ghosts and Klinkerashes and so on, as well as the Land Titans and Medes (Goat Folk), but none of it meshed together all, none outside their over arching subgroups had any real meaningful commonality that drew all their really cool concepts togther.<br /> <br /> Why would the Bastets make common cause with Land Titans, beyond some basuc enviromental conversation, which is in everyones interest, human, vampire, ect... to.<br /> <br /> And the splats were very poorly balanced with each other.<br /> <br /> What Changing Breeds needs is either to have all of it tied together in a really tight way based on an original idea, or for all the subgroups of Changing Breed types to be completely seperate with their own themes.<br /> <br /> Example maybe the combined goal of the Changing Breeds is to restore Pangaea and the Pangaeans.<br /> <br /> Or break them up with the Bastets tracing their roots back to Bubastis, like how Mummies are tied to Irem, no matter where they are in the world or what form.<br /> <br /> Like maybe the Hungry Ghosts were the first Bastets and they were charged with protecting Basts heart, one of the last artifacts of Pangaea, but when the city fell, it got shatter in a particular and strange way, release energy into the world, that created the various types of other Bastets and the Hungry Ghosts became cursed because of thrir failure to defend her heart, do the goal of all the Bastets, but more so Hungry Ghosts, is rebuild her heart and restore the City of Bubastis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It is true. But when I speak here of a review it would be a radical overhaul to the point of ignoring the earlier book. Something as radical as the difference of the Mummy - Resurrection for the WoD: Mummy or Kuei Jins for Gaki.<br /> <br /> Something that just caught the creature himself, the Changing Breeds and make a cohesive game with him. How they tried to make in-game fan Changing Breeds - The Elder Gods.<br /> <br /> Only taking advantage of the good ideas of Pure War and the Changing Breeds (first edition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T23:14:14-07:00","id":960261,"title":"","content":"Thematically I believe a kind of suggested story can be shared territory.<br /> <br /> Various creatures live in a nearby ignorant area from each other (and remain so during the game), and with its own problems, but how to share a place so close to have to interact, but to the player's character he would not have science that the other characters other players would be anything but human. And something unknown that disturbs the order of this small territory, with all perniciono and harmful (to harm humanity that place so that any supernatural being who lives there, finish severely disturbed in their relationship with humans place). And each would interact your way.<br /> <br /> _____________________________________<br /> <br /> On the rules they need to be rebalanced like a coterie game even, in the balance, with each creature highlighting a particular niche (something that existed in the first edition), including in relation to the powers.<br /> <br /> But the scenario of recommendations I think I should be concerned to give media players play for indirect interactions without trivializing the supernatural.<br /> <br /> ______________________________________<br /> <br /> Submit an antagonist that can be worked later would be interesting, more powerful than this common antagonist to be strange and incomprehensible to everyone. In addition to bringing some horrors. It would be the time to bring the Mythos and Aliens for the game. And cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T05:10:46-07:00","id":960362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959556#post959556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like this approach, because it's based on idea that players are<br /> a) working as a team that delegates character roles (party face, party muscle, etc)<br /> b) reduced to &quot;social guy&quot;, &quot;muscle guy&quot;, &quot;mental guy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=959564#post959564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>. Most of the time in Chronicles of Darkness, you make a character that fulfills a concept, not a party role like in other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Shrugs* Niches dont' have to be the whole fighter/rogue/cleric/wizard division. Its an easy one to use, especially given that the design of the CofD games tend to actually use those same roles in a lot of their games - hells, those roles are the defining features of the Auspices and Orders, as well as being a huge influence the four Seasonal Courts! You can't just handwave these four roles and their influence away because you don't like them. Their influence definitely exists in the CofD.<br /> <br /> But all that is immaterial, because its only an example we're using. Social animals of all ilks, from ants to rodents to dogs to humans, are biologically inclined towards establishing niches for the betterment of the whole. Its a tendacy in many gamers when making parties as well to avoid overlap. Those niches can be pretty much anything, as long as its an active area. Niches themselves are something that very much is central to gaming, as is spotlight sharing, but there's nothing to say what those niches have to be. If you have a heavy social game, for instance, you can have four kinds of social niches, and everything holds true. As well, there's nothing saying that you can't be competent in another role outside your specialty - the socialite knowing self defense, etc. But most games rely on having moments where you individually shine and have an impact on the story. The problem comes when one person can effectively do everything the rest of the group can, and be just as good.<br /> <br /> No matter how you slice things, overshadowing others is a problem for player enjoyment.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anyone want Crossover information that doesn't involve mage? </div> </div> </div></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure. But the whole niche-argument actually has implications outside of Mage crossovers as well. Its actually a very important consideration in any crossover game on top of themes and cohesive plot - mixing similar characters can lead to problems in any game, and ensuring that everyone has their own niche actually boosts the effectiveness of any crossover game that I've seen and heard about.<br /> <br /> &quot;How to successfully build a crossover troupe that works together&quot; is something that is actually important to the game, and well worth a section within a Crossover book. In my experience, everyone making their own characters and showing up to game is a recipe for disaster. Crossover games require greater cooperation between players than usual, especially since the usual meta-game support is not in place anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T06:31:31-07:00","id":960395,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> Personally, I wouldn't want to use a hack that works around the <i>rather important</i> vampiric inability to act effectively during the day and their weakness against sunlight, but I can see where it would work. I brought the topic up because it does not sound like an unfitting or implausible thing to see in a book dedicated to crossover, and I used vampires as an example because it was the simplest one that occurred to me.<br /> <br /> Depending on the splats involved, you're right such rules might not be necessary to overcome the bulk of related difficulties, and reliance on something like a Fetish or Imbued Item is something that creates story opportunities on its own.<br /> <br /> (But even if I handled something like my Dracula-inspired suggestion, Kindred would likewise still have to fight against daysleep. At least that contribution to thematics would have to be maintained.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2019_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2019\" data-vbnamecard=\"2019\">eberg</a><br /> I don't think Rage or Disquiet are very helpful examples of splat difficulties that could be hacked or ignored for this (even as just examples to object to the stance). First of all because they're not an impediment to crossover any more than they are an impediment to groups in solely Werewolf and Promethean games; unlike the inherent restriction of vampires to specific activity cycles, which doesn't hamper solely Vampire games because the player characters tend to all be vampires, but in multi-splat chronicles can interfere with the ability of the players to all be engaged at the same time unless the vampire player has a way to busy himself in the meanwhile (the Ghoul suggestion is a sensible one, but can also lead to the player having to pull double duty when both characters are in play unless something like Werewolf's approach to secondary cast is used).<br /> <br /> Second, I wouldn't feel comfortable removing Disquiet or Rage from the major factors that the respective splats have to deal with because I find them more vital to their games than the effective inability to operate during sunlight hours which can be worked around even within the boundaries of Requiem. The downsides of the monsters in the Chronicles of Darkess are very important things to the identity of those games the fun of playing them to me as well! So I would never want them to cease to matter at all.<br /> <br /> Even if Vampires could have limited ability to effectively operate during the day as a base assumption, the majority of the downsides of kindred, which constitute a vital part of playing them, remain. They are still not meant for the day, and labor to walk during its hours. They must still feed their thirst for blood for the express purpose of surviving. They must still deal with that dreadful beast inside which compels them to reactions of primal rage and fear and makes them monstruous predators among mortals. They are still deprived of many of the pleasures of the living and must go on with that, and they must watch themselves lest they grow too detached and coldly terrible. On the other hand, if Disquiet or Rage were made non-factors (mostly disquiet, but I think Rage permeates subtly into much of what being a werewolf is), it would harshly cut into ever-present downsides of being a Created or an Uratha. Without Disquiet to worry about and toil under, the backbone of the downsides to being a Promethean loses structural integrity where interaction with humans is concerned, where the backbone of Vampire disadvantages and existential pains can be maintained even without the need to worry about the day as much.<br /> <br /> (Not to say that the inability to look upon the sun ever again isn't a big deal in becoming a vampire, or that the loss it constitutes isn't significant. The Coil of the Ascendant is such an enticing pursuit precisely because of this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-30-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:05:20-07:00","id":960414,"title":"","content":"Quick note: Disquiet <i>does</i> hamper crossover play, because unlike other mind-warping aura effects (Lunacy, Sleeping Curse, etc.) it affects other supernaturals; only Beasts are exempt. So it is kind of like the vampire's nocturnal nature, in that it introduces difficulties in a mixed team that you don't have in an all-Promethean group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:13:28-07:00","id":960415,"title":"","content":"I had the mistaken impression it didn't affect them, at least to a degree that would always be relevant. That's what I get for not having read Promethean 2e yet. Thanks for correcting me.<br /> <br /> (Second point still holds: I wouldn't ever remove Disquiet from a crossover equation because I see it as too vital a pillar to the disadvantages of Prometheans, but if I was asked to come up with a hack maybe I would alleviate its effects where the supernatural as a whole is concerned.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:20:50-07:00","id":960421,"title":"","content":"It's not new to 2e; it's always been that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:27:34-07:00","id":960423,"title":"","content":"To be clear - there was a hack in a Priomethean book to make other supernaturals immune to Disquiet, but the default was always that only ephemeral creatures were immune to it. So, the option to play crossover that was was certainly on the table, but it wasn't the default, and there were other options as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:30:12-07:00","id":960428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960421#post960421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not new to 2e; it's always been that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't read much of 1e, and then not anything past the core. Was thinking of getting into it in earnest with the second edition after following open development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-30-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T08:22:11-07:00","id":960449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960414#post960414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick note: Disquiet <i>does</i> hamper crossover play, because unlike other mind-warping aura effects (Lunacy, Sleeping Curse, etc.) it affects other supernaturals; only Beasts are exempt. So it is kind of like the vampire's nocturnal nature, in that it introduces difficulties in a mixed team that you don't have in an all-Promethean group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, simple 'Mind protection' powers will solve the problem ( do not remember those for vampires and werewolves ). In 2E <b>Mage</b>, resisting Disquiet should be simple Mind 2 spell only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:16:07-07:00","id":960485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960449#post960449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, simple 'Mind protection' powers will solve the problem ( do not remember those for vampires and werewolves ). In 2E <b>Mage</b>, resisting Disquiet should be simple Mind 2 spell only.</div> </div> </div> </div> For vampires and werewolves, it was &quot;having Coils of the Beast&quot; and &quot;make anti-Rage fetishes.&quot; The former is no longer valid, given the transformation Coils underwent, and I don't think the latter are in the core book anymore, though I'm too lazy to check. So, I wouldn't count on non-mages having resistances to Disquiet anymore.<br /> <br /> As for mages? There were couple different levels of Mind required, depending on what you were trying to do. Shielding against Disquiet was one thing, curing it was another. Affect another person needed more. And so on. Curing Disquiet is probably still going to be Mind 3, since Perfecting is the level for curing or manipulating Conditions on targets. Shielding remains shielding at Mind 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-30-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:39:27-07:00","id":960501,"title":"","content":"Didn't there use to be some mention of Glamour being usable as a mana substitute for Fate and Time spells? Was that removed and if not what does that mean for other fuels. <br /> <br /> Also it might be nice to have a full list of what different supernatural auras look like in one place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:32:35-07:00","id":960532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960501#post960501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't there use to be some mention of Glamour being usable as a mana substitute for Fate and Time spells? Was that removed and if not what does that mean for other fuels.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that ever existed, it shouldn't.<br /> <br /> It's fairly trivial for a mage to make herself immune to Disquiet. The trick is knowing that you have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:36:16-07:00","id":960534,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I did think it odd at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:48:59-07:00","id":960542,"title":"","content":"IIRC, it was in Rites of Spring, and was part of the Arcadia Ambivalence Attitude: if it's possible that the Mage and Changeling Arcadias are the same, or could be mistaken for each other, then it follows that the supernatural energies emanating from each should at least bear a striking resemblance to the other.<br /> <br /> Of course, with a clear \u201cthey're not the same\u201d distinction between the two Arcadias in 2e, there's no point in making Glamour resemble Arcadia-flavored mana anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:38:08-07:00","id":960782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960532#post960532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's fairly trivial for a mage to make herself immune to Disquiet. The trick is knowing that you have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave,i think that's a bad idea . disquiet shouldnt be something easy to avoid even for a mage,because since disquiet is a by produt of the dvine fire inside prometheans a mage,even a powerful one, shouldn't be able to block it easily,even if said mage could understand what disquiet and the divine fire is . The divine fire is after all Divine! a mage can't just bend Divinity to her will. it's also not a good idea from a storytelling point of view, i don't believe mages should be able to easily block something that it is a omnipresent and almost unavoidable part of promethean existence,that would muddle the themes of each gameline in a crossover instead of combining them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:41:56-07:00","id":960785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960782#post960782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dave,i think that's a bad idea . disquiet shouldnt be something easy to avoid even for a mage,because since disquiet is a by produt of the dvine fire inside prometheans a mage,even a powerful one, shouldn't be able to block it easily,even if said mage could understand what disquiet and the divine fire is . The divine fire is after all Divine! a mage can't just bend Divinity to her will. it's also not a good idea from a storytelling point of view, i don't believe mages should be able to easily block something that it is a omnipresent and almost unavoidable part of promethean existence,that would muddle the themes of each gameline in a crossover instead of combining them</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't think a Promethean should sell herself and become virtually a slave of a divine being bending the universe to its hubris simply to taste what it's like to be human?<br /> <br /> I mean... it's pretty thematic if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:45:42-07:00","id":960786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960785#post960785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you don't think a Promethean should sell herself and become virtually a slave of a divine being bending the universe to its hubris simply to taste what it's like to be human?<br /> <br /> I mean... it's pretty thematic if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no,a promethean seeling herself is totally in theme. the mage being able to manipulate pyros related thing without a huge amount of effort it's not,and it's a bit anticlimatic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:51:54-07:00","id":960788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960786#post960786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no,a promethean seeling herself is totally in theme. the mage being able to manipulate pyros related thing without a huge amount of effort it's not,and it's a bit anticlimatic</div> </div> </div> </div> But the Mage isn't manipulating a Pyros thing; they're messing with their own brain to ensure that they can ifnore the effects of Disquiet. Like how a Forces Mage could protect themselves from Electrification; it might be a Divine Fire thing, but it's also an electricity thing. Likewise, Disquiet is a Divine Fire thing, but it's also a Mind thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:53:46-07:00","id":960790,"title":"","content":"There are only a handful of things where it has been established that Supernal Magic can affect the Divine Fire. Shielding against Disquiet is one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:58:38-07:00","id":960792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960788#post960788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But the Mage isn't manipulating a Pyros thing; they're messing with their own brain to ensure that they can ifnore the effects of Disquiet. Like how a Forces Mage could protect themselves from Electrification; it might be a Divine Fire thing, but it's also an electricity thing. Likewise, Disquiet is a Divine Fire thing, but it's also a Mind thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm,maybe i'm being a bit too worried here it's just that promethean as a gameline means a lot to me and i don't really like seeing any of its themes being put aside. but i gotta accept that to make a good crossover i gotta compromise,i just hope mages need to really know what they're doing first,i'td be a bummer if one of the most important things about promethean could just be brushed away easily,i want it to take effort. because if disquiet is easily dismissed it kinda makes Promethean as a gameline less awesome to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 08-30-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:07:29-07:00","id":960798,"title":"","content":"Reach wasn't a thing in 1e. I wouldn't object to a ruling that says that the alienness of the Divine Fire with respect to Supernal Magic means that even when you <i>do</i> find the occasional spell that can influence or thwart the Divine Fire, it takes an extra Reach above and beyond the normal requirements in order do so.<br /> <br /> So detecting the Divine Fire would be an Unveiling spell that automatically requires one Reach to perform; shielding against Disquiet would be a Shielding spell that automatically requires one Reach to perform; eliminating Disquiet would be a Perfecting spell that requires one Reach to perform; and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-30-2016, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:18:10-07:00","id":960853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960792#post960792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm,maybe i'm being a bit too worried here it's just that promethean as a gameline means a lot to me and i don't really like seeing any of its themes being put aside. but i gotta accept that to make a good crossover i gotta compromise,i just hope mages need to really know what they're doing first,i'td be a bummer if one of the most important things about promethean could just be brushed away easily,i want it to take effort. because if disquiet is easily dismissed it kinda makes Promethean as a gameline less awesome to me</div> </div> </div> </div>Unchained and Begotten already have workarounds for Disquiet. Beasts are immune, and Demons can choose to ignore it.<br /> Does it matter if Mages can fix themselves as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:46:54-07:00","id":960872,"title":"","content":"I personally dont think its a very good Idea. It just feels a bit too heavy handed,a disquiet Shield create by magic? To me it doesnt sound good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T22:41:20-07:00","id":960891,"title":"","content":"It's not new; Promethean mentioned it in Magnum Opus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:53:11-07:00","id":960920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960792#post960792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm,maybe i'm being a bit too worried here it's just that promethean as a gameline means a lot to me and i don't really like seeing any of its themes being put aside. but i gotta accept that to make a good crossover i gotta compromise,i just hope mages need to really know what they're doing first,i'td be a bummer if one of the most important things about promethean could just be brushed away easily,i want it to take effort. because if disquiet is easily dismissed it kinda makes Promethean as a gameline less awesome to me</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you play it <i>too</i> safe here. I plan to run <b>Mage-Promethean</b> plot soon ( only need to find Promie player for my Mage chronicle ) and I <b>totally</b> want to make Disquiet the thing. PCs can have Mind mages in their group but first they need to come in contact with it ( so probably not 'getting it' ) before Shielding one self - lore on Created is <i>very</i> scarce, even for Mysterium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960798#post960798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reach wasn't a thing in 1e. I wouldn't object to a ruling that says that the alienness of the Divine Fire with respect to Supernal Magic means that even when you <i>do</i> find the occasional spell that can influence or thwart the Divine Fire, it takes an extra Reach above and beyond the normal requirements in order do so.<br /> <br /> So detecting the Divine Fire would be an Unveiling spell that automatically requires one Reach to perform; shielding against Disquiet would be a Shielding spell that automatically requires one Reach to perform; eliminating Disquiet would be a Perfecting spell that requires one Reach to perform; and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Automatic Reach needed on spell is <b>not</b> the thing in 2E <b>Mage</b> and <u>should not be</u>. Spells should work on their own - other way, it's not proper spell. What <i>can</i> be made is that Mind Shield spell get's extra Reach 1 option that Shield it before Disquite, <i>if mage know what to make with Imago</i>. You do not know Created? You do not know what to cast. Simple<br /> <br /> Other, Disquite topic related with Awakened - most of the time Disquite works as obsession on mortal mind, then in to murder cravings. But with mages, they could get Obsession on Created - I think it's more thematically fitting that Mysterium want to dissect living Promethean to grasp Divine Fire, than to 'call the mob with torches and pitchforks'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-31-2016, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T00:06:42-07:00","id":960927,"title":"","content":"The notion that \u201cthis phenomenon doesn't really fit within this Arcanum's purview despite a superficial resemblance, and so requires you to Reach to do something that would come naturally otherwise\u201d seems logical to me. Assuming that 2e keeps 1e's notion that mages don't know what to make of the Divine Fire, increasing the Reach needed to mess with it seems like it's being generous to mages; the most reasonable alternative would be \u201csorry, you can't even try\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T01:36:06-07:00","id":960943,"title":"","content":"The mage isn't doing anything to the divine fire - they're protecting their own emotions from outside interference. Same way a Mastigos can no-sell Obfuscate without having to know how the vampiric curse works.<br /> <br /> What they can't do, barring archmaster-level plot devicium, is stop a Promethean from causing Disquiet in the first place","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T05:10:20-07:00","id":960989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960943#post960943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage isn't doing anything to the divine fire - they're protecting their own emotions from outside interference. Same way a Mastigos can no-sell Obfuscate without having to know how the vampiric curse works.<br /> <br /> What they can't do, barring archmaster-level plot devicium, is stop a Promethean from causing Disquiet in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are there some plans how mages will interact with Divine Fire? I know rules are probably not even planned - but maybe some general idea? Like, can mages see Divine Fire with some Active Mage Sight? Prime perhaps? Should they be able to interact with Pyros ( outside of modifying Promethean patterns )?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T05:38:38-07:00","id":960994,"title":"","content":"No idea. We'll see when we get around to writing the book this thread's about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T05:51:49-07:00","id":961000,"title":"","content":"My thought: Mage Sight reveals the Supernal World. Pyros is not Supernal, and so should not be revealed by Mage Sight. However, Unveiling spells are still a thing; and a mage who knows what to look for could use an Unveiling Prime spell to spot the effects of the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T05:55:42-07:00","id":961002,"title":"","content":"Honest question - <b>Do Active Mage Sight see Vitea or Essence? </b>Because if yes, then Prime Mage Sight should see Divine Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:10:33-07:00","id":961009,"title":"","content":"My guess would be technically no; but they'd probably see the Supernal symbology associated with Vitae and Essence. Likewise with Glamour, Plasm, Aether, etc. But Pyros doesn't have Supernal symbols associated with it, assuming 1e's take on the Pyros/Supernal relationship holds; so Pyros would be a blindspot for Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:28:14-07:00","id":961012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961009#post961009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Pyros doesn't have Supernal symbols associated with it, assuming 1e's take on the Pyros/Supernal relationship holds; so Pyros would be a blindspot for Mage Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>But are not Alchemy, Creation and Change as Symbols connected to Divine Fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:42:52-07:00","id":961017,"title":"","content":"Not the Supernal symbols of Alchemy, Creation, and Change, no; at least, not according to 1e.<br /> <br /> Elaborating on this: it's a Mystery why the Divine Fire doesn't have any Supernal Symbology associated with it, a Mystery that tantalizes mages who know about it. The going theory is that there <i>are</i> Supernal symbols associated with it; but they're in a \u201cregion\u201d of the Supernal that's \u201cdistant\u201d from where the Watchtowers stand. There's a fan-made Legacy called the Sons of the Aether that's built on the theory that the missing symbology can be found hidden in an obscure corner of the Aether; it's exactly the sort of Legacy that I'd hope to find in <b>Crossover Chronicle</b>. Another theory is that the Divine Fire is a manifestation of the hypothetical trans-Supernal Realm known as the Empyrean. My own favorite theory, though, is that there aren't any Pyros-related Supernal symbols because the Divine Fire has long since consumed them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-31-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T07:46:49-07:00","id":961053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960943#post960943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage isn't doing anything to the divine fire - they're protecting their own emotions from outside interference. Same way a Mastigos can no-sell Obfuscate without having to know how the vampiric curse works.<br /> <br /> What they can't do, barring archmaster-level plot devicium, is stop a Promethean from causing Disquiet in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>But can they set up a spell to protect <i>others'</i> minds from Disquiet, then anchor that to the Promethean? So whoever the Promethean is near (up to the limits of the spell) is rendered immune to Disquiet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T08:48:00-07:00","id":961073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=960943#post960943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage isn't doing anything to the divine fire - they're protecting their own emotions from outside interference. Same way a Mastigos can no-sell Obfuscate without having to know how the vampiric curse works.<br /> <br /> What they can't do, barring archmaster-level plot devicium, is stop a Promethean from causing Disquiet in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah,for i second I thought I thought you were saying mages could stop indeed stop disquiet completely,my mistake sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:42:35-07:00","id":961174,"title":"","content":"Question: What happens if different supernatural energies are mixed? Say for instance a werewolf fetish is left in the Hedge to become a token. Does the latter superimpose over the former or does it mutate like what Aether does to other beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:32:00-07:00","id":961242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961174#post961174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: What happens if different supernatural energies are mixed? Say for instance a werewolf fetish is left in the Hedge to become a token. Does the latter superimpose over the former or does it mutate like what Aether does to other beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the default answer there is &quot;plot hook&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:38:54-07:00","id":961304,"title":"","content":"You know, I've never really understood why people associate Prometheans with Prime, they aren't exactly pillars of the supernal or truth.... Forces + Life or Forces + Matter seems to make more sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:57:04-07:00","id":961313,"title":"","content":"A Promethean 1e writer took two &quot;divine fires&quot; at face value without thinking about what they meant. Pyros is really much more to do with Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:41:20-07:00","id":961327,"title":"","content":"Fair enough -- though Elpis-related functions of Pyros have to do with creation, and Flux-related functions are related to destruction, which arguably are related to Prime and Death, respectively. Or rather, they <i>would</i> be, if Pyros was related to the Supernal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:52:33-07:00","id":961333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961242#post961242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the default answer there is &quot;plot hook&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't part of the point of the crossover chronicle to explain how to mechanically represent a bizarre hobgoblin-fetish? I might be wrong about that, I admit. But I would still like to hear someone else's ideas on what mixing powers does. For instance, what happens if a Promethean gets stuck in the Astral? Sure it's a plot hook but clarifying if the Disquiet affects the Goetia and/or humans connected to that part of the Astral would be nice.<br /> <br /> Of course, I am still new and inexperienced with the World of Darkness so feel free to ignore me. I probably sound like I'm whining anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:01:34-07:00","id":961338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961333#post961333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But isn't part of the point of the crossover chronicle to explain how to mechanically represent a bizarre hobgoblin-fetish? I might be wrong about that, I admit. But I would still like to hear someone else's ideas on what mixing powers does. For instance, what happens if a Promethean gets stuck in the Astral? Sure it's a plot hook but clarifying if the Disquiet affects the Goetia and/or humans connected to that part of the Astral would be nice.<br /> <br /> Of course, I am still new and inexperienced with the World of Darkness so feel free to ignore me. I probably sound like I'm whining anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't mean to come off dismissive or anything. What I meant was that there's so many possibilities that most of the time, you end up with something unique, likely with its own mechanics. That said, I could easily see the book giving advice on how to come up with those mechanics, and maybe give some examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:08:24-07:00","id":961343,"title":"","content":"In first edition, glamour, or at least Changelings, had a Resonance of Madness when eaten by werewolves. Presumably talens that would pop up would be similar.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see rites and abilities so werewolves could deal with, capture and cage the other ephemerals or more-magic-than-matter beings. Or the results when they act as patrons to lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-31-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:11:13-07:00","id":961344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961338#post961338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I didn't mean to come off dismissive or anything. What I meant was that there's so many possibilities that most of the time, you end up with something unique, likely with its own mechanics. That said, I could easily see the book giving advice on how to come up with those mechanics, and maybe give some examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that is exactly what I hope for. Also don't about sounding dismissive, it was a completely reasonable answer. Mind, it would be nice to have a comprehensive list of what different beings look like under aura sight but frankly that sort of thing is so minor as to be the first dumped for word count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:11:19-07:00","id":961345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961343#post961343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In first edition, glamour, or at least Changelings, had a Resonance of Madness when eaten by werewolves. Presumably talens that would pop up would be similar.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see rites and abilities so werewolves could deal with, capture and cage the other ephemerals or more-magic-than-matter beings. Or the results when they act as patrons to lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Heh I've actually been toying with the idea of a Lodge whose patron &quot;spirit&quot; is actually a supernal entity of the Primal Wilds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:25:22-07:00","id":961355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961345#post961345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh I've actually been toying with the idea of a Lodge whose patron &quot;spirit&quot; is actually a supernal entity of the Primal Wilds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers of the Hunt? I wouldn't complain, it would be interesting to see. Werewolf's been very much about embracing the awesome and not rejecting stuff out of hand. The books throw out possibilities like that all over. That said, I've asked before what supernal entities do and never really got a response. We know what the Exarchs want, because they're tyranny and tyranny tyrannizes, but what would a supernal entity of the Primal Wilds want with a lodge of werewolves hunting on its behalf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-31-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:17:00-07:00","id":961646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961355#post961355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Seers of the Hunt? I wouldn't complain, it would be interesting to see. Werewolf's been very much about embracing the awesome and not rejecting stuff out of hand. The books throw out possibilities like that all over. That said, I've asked before what supernal entities do and never really got a response. We know what the Exarchs want, because they're tyranny and tyranny tyrannizes, but what would a supernal entity of the Primal Wilds want with a lodge of werewolves hunting on its behalf?</div> </div> </div> </div>To represent or exemplify whatever Symbol it is? (Supernals Represent)<br /> <br /> Aren't the Spirit ones even called Totems? I mean, they're already begging to be included, it sounds like. (And a rude surprise for any opposing pack that tries their spirit magic/rites on this pack's totem - &quot;Sorry, it's not actually a spirit even though it is a representation of Spirit&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:57:56-07:00","id":961691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961646#post961646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To represent or exemplify whatever Symbol it is? (Supernals Represent)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but they don't seem to have any interest in the Fallen World. They can be summoned and act as advisors, but it doesn't look like they want to go out and 'do' anything, let alone gather a cult to do it for them.<br /> <br /> There are the Bound, though, who constantly hunger for mana. Having a pack of werewolves gobbling up mages and tass and dissembling artifacts would probably be useful for one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:13:59-07:00","id":961702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961691#post961691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but they don't seem to have any interest in the Fallen World. They can be summoned and act as advisors, but it doesn't look like they want to go out and 'do' anything, let alone gather a cult to do it for them.<br /> <br /> There are the Bound, though, who constantly hunger for mana. Having a pack of werewolves gobbling up mages and tass and dissembling artifacts would probably be useful for one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may not <i>have</i> to (at least, like Spirits do), but they still seem to follow some guidelines. They may act because that's just what they are. Daemons from Pandemonium might test others not because they get something out of it, but merely because that's just what they do. Same thing with any potential Supernal Entity. If it forms cults around itself, that may be because doing so it core to its Symbol.<br /> <br /> But yeah, having one of the Bound as a cult focus or totem would have a direct and obvious drive. That seems something very Bale Hound like, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:03:54-07:00","id":961736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961702#post961702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They may not <i>have</i> to (at least, like Spirits do), but they still seem to follow some guidelines. They may act because that's just what they are. Daemons from Pandemonium might test others not because they get something out of it, but merely because that's just what they do. Same thing with any potential Supernal Entity. If it forms cults around itself, that may be because doing so it core to its Symbol.<br /> <br /> But yeah, having one of the Bound as a cult focus or totem would have a direct and obvious drive. That seems something very Bale Hound like, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> We'll like likely know more when Signs of Sorcery is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:13:02-07:00","id":961746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961327#post961327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough -- though Elpis-related functions of Pyros have to do with creation, and Flux-related functions are related to destruction, which arguably are related to Prime and Death, respectively. Or rather, they <i>would</i> be, if Pyros was related to the Supernal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> The Supernal is just a collection of symbols (admittedly living symbols with power, but still symbols). Its kind of like using the language of math to describe physics in the real world. Bolts of lightning have nothing to do with calculus, but that doesn't mean we can't use math to figure out how to predict and control the lightning. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, you totally can describe pyros in terms of Supernal symbols and run occult calculations with it. Just got to know what kind of calculations to run!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:57:53-07:00","id":961806,"title":"","content":"And if we were talking about virtually any other subject, I'd agree with you*. But from day one, <b>Promethean</b>'s Divine Fire has been the exception when it comes to the Supernal. By all rights, it <i>ought</i> to be describable through (and thus subject to manipulation by) Supernal symbols, because <i>everything</i> in the Fallen World is<span style=\"font-size:8px\"><sup>\u2020</sup></span>. And yet, <i>it isn't</i>. At least, not by any Supernal symbols familiar to any of the ten Arcana. If there <i>are</i> any Supernal symbols describing Pyros phenomena, they exist entirely outside the scope of mage experience. Which, in practical terms, is equivalent to them not existing.<br /> <br /> Among that part of the mage community that knows about Pyros, theories abound concerning its nature. How could it be otherwise? After all, mages are addicted to Mystery, and what is Pyros if not a big Mystery? Some say that Pyros manifests from some part of the Supernal that's beyond the reach of the Watchtowers and the ten Arcana; others say that it's proof of the reality of the Empyrean, the trans-Supernal source of everything the existence and nature of which some archmasters hypothesize. Still others say that it's Abyssal, or that it emanates from the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> Yet all of these theories are either flawed or worthless \u2014 flawed because the Divine Fire doesn't conform to what <i>is</i> known about, say, the Abyss or the Lower Depths; or worthless because there are no practical benefits to identifying it as \u201cexotic Supernal\u201d or \u201ctrans-Supernal\u201d: it's just mages attaching a name to something they don't know, in the hopes that naming it will make it comprehensible. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* 2e may change this. But unless and until I see some indication that they <i>will</i>, I'm sticking to my guns on this one.<br /> <br /> \u2020 Except, of course, the Abyssal; but Pyros isn't Abyssal either \u2014 though that hasn't stopped some mages of categorizing it as such in a desperate attempt to get it to fit <i>somewhere</i> in their model of reality.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:59:00-07:00","id":962135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961806#post961806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if we were talking about virtually any other subject, I'd agree with you*. But from day one, <b>Promethean</b>'s Divine Fire has been the exception when it comes to the Supernal. By all rights, it <i>ought</i> to be describable through (and thus subject to manipulation by) Supernal symbols, because <i>everything</i> in the Fallen World is<span style=\"font-size:8px\"><sup>\u2020</sup></span>. And yet, <i>it isn't</i>. At least, not by any Supernal symbols familiar to any of the ten Arcana. If there <i>are</i> any Supernal symbols describing Pyros phenomena, they exist entirely outside the scope of mage experience. Which, in practical terms, is equivalent to them not existing.<br /> <br /> Among that part of the mage community that knows about Pyros, theories abound concerning its nature. How could it be otherwise? After all, mages are addicted to Mystery, and what is Pyros if not a big Mystery? Some say that Pyros manifests from some part of the Supernal that's beyond the reach of the Watchtowers and the ten Arcana; others say that it's proof of the reality of the Empyrean, the trans-Supernal source of everything the existence and nature of which some archmasters hypothesize. Still others say that it's Abyssal, or that it emanates from the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> Yet all of these theories are either flawed or worthless \u2014 flawed because the Divine Fire doesn't conform to what <i>is</i> known about, say, the Abyss or the Lower Depths; or worthless because there are no practical benefits to identifying it as \u201cexotic Supernal\u201d or \u201ctrans-Supernal\u201d: it's just mages attaching a name to something they don't know, in the hopes that naming it will make it comprehensible. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* 2e may change this. But unless and until I see some indication that they <i>will</i>, I'm sticking to my guns on this one.<br /> <br /> \u2020 Except, of course, the Abyssal; but Pyros isn't Abyssal either \u2014 though that hasn't stopped some mages of categorizing it as such in a desperate attempt to get it to fit <i>somewhere</i> in their model of reality.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't recall the supplements, but P1e did provide some tools to sense and control pyros and related matters with the Arcana. I believe it required a combination of Mind and Prime.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:18:25-07:00","id":962193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=961806#post961806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. And yet, <i>it isn't</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Quibble - its not described <i>yet</i>. Pyros isn't fundamentally unknowable, its just fundamentally difficult to explore. Its like the magical equivalent of the Uncertanty Principle - interacting with a particle changes it, which limits what you can know about it, since you just changed all other variables by confirming one. <br /> <br /> Pyros is a complicated mess, sure, and undestanding it is not simple as manipulating essence. But I see no reason for it to be completely unviable. <br /> <br /> And even if the argument is that there's no current symbol to describe things, we're just one archmage away from developing the necessary symbols.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* 2e may change this. But unless and until I see some indication that they </span></i><i>will</i><i><span style=\"font-size:10px\">, I'm sticking to my guns on this one.</span></i> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even in 1e, things weren't that unknowable. Unknown is one thing. Unknowable is not. Unless there's specific quotes to back you up (which I don't recall ever seeing, mind), I think your position is more of a personal take than cannon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:21:54-07:00","id":962219,"title":"","content":"Now that I'm thinking about it, what I would like to see in the book is the ability to share some of the splat-exclusive merits. It already has a precedent: Promethean Alchemists can get some relevant Created-specific merits. Beast also mentions that people dabbling in the Primordial can buy some Beast-specific merits - this has further justification in that many of those Beast-specific merits were originally supposed to be Supernatural merits for mortals (mentioned by a developer in the Alpha Predators: The Strongest Vampires thread).<br /> <br /> So, for example, a Mage exploring the Primordial part of the Astral Realms could have a justification to buy merits like the Advanced Eidetic Memory or Advanced Striking Looks. On the other hand, non-Mages, like a Changeling, could after tutoring from the Mage benefit from merits like Dream or Destiny (admit it, these merits are really fucking appropriate for a Changeling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-02-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]