 least, not by any Supernal symbols familiar to any of the ten Arcana. If there <i>are</i> any Supernal symbols describing Pyros phenomena, they exist entirely outside the scope of mage experience. Which, in practical terms, is equivalent to them not existing.<br /> <br /> Among that part of the mage community that knows about Pyros, theories abound concerning its nature. How could it be otherwise? After all, mages are addicted to Mystery, and what is Pyros if not a big Mystery? Some say that Pyros manifests from some part of the Supernal that's beyond the reach of the Watchtowers and the ten Arcana; others say that it's proof of the reality of the Empyrean, the trans-Supernal source of everything the existence and nature of which some archmasters hypothesize. Still others say that it's Abyssal, or that it emanates from the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> Yet all of these theories are either flawed or worthless \u2014 flawed because the Divine Fire doesn't conform to what <i>is</i> known about, say, the Abyss or the Lower Depths; or worthless because there are no practical benefits to identifying it as \u201cexotic Supernal\u201d or \u201ctrans-Supernal\u201d: it's just mages attaching a name to something they don't know, in the hopes that naming it will make it comprehensible. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* 2e may change this. But unless and until I see some indication that they <i>will</i>, I'm sticking to my guns on this one.<br /> <br /> \u2020 Except, of course, the Abyssal; but Pyros isn't Abyssal either \u2014 though that hasn't stopped some mages of categorizing it as such in a desperate attempt to get it to fit <i>somewhere</i> in their model of reality.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the theories about the Divine Fire is that it doesn't even belongs to this universe, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:26:23-07:00","id":962440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=962412#post962412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping the book at least touches on the fact that Vampires make for ideal Mummy cultists; they're immortal and (with the Fog of Ages gone) can remember what you've forgotten! One of the Bloodlines in Ancient Bloodlines was a bunch of Egyptian dead who aid the failing memories of the torpid, and they're just screaming for a 2e update focused on Mummy crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unchained make great &quot;cultists&quot; too. Perfect recall, handy &quot;anyone can use&quot; items, and the ability to bolster other cult members through Pacts. You just have to find one that is &quot;trustworthy&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T13:11:47-07:00","id":962456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=962219#post962219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I'm thinking about it, what I would like to see in the book is the ability to share some of the splat-exclusive merits. It already has a precedent: Promethean Alchemists can get some relevant Created-specific merits. Beast also mentions that people dabbling in the Primordial can buy some Beast-specific merits - this has further justification in that many of those Beast-specific merits were originally supposed to be Supernatural merits for mortals (mentioned by a developer in the Alpha Predators: The Strongest Vampires thread).<br /> <br /> So, for example, a Mage exploring the Primordial part of the Astral Realms could have a justification to buy merits like the Advanced Eidetic Memory or Advanced Striking Looks. On the other hand, non-Mages, like a Changeling, could after tutoring from the Mage benefit from merits like Dream or Destiny (admit it, these merits are really fucking appropriate for a Changeling).</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay I admit it, they're fucking appropriate for Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:43:23-07:00","id":962711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=962412#post962412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping the book at least touches on the fact that Vampires make for ideal Mummy cultists; they're immortal and (with the Fog of Ages gone) can remember what you've forgotten! One of the Bloodlines in Ancient Bloodlines was a bunch of Egyptian dead who aid the failing memories of the torpid, and they're just screaming for a 2e update focused on Mummy crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely hoping we get plenty on splats working together and multi-splat organizations. You made me remember one I came up with a while ago, mostly just for fun- my only fleshed out Mummy character was based a lot on Sir Crocodile from One Piece, but her cult stole the playing card gimmick from Doflamingo. It was this sort of shadowy corporation called Atlantic Entertainment Concepts, and there was an inner framework of &quot;in the know&quot; people known as the suits. Employees who didn't know the boss was magic were &quot;zeros&quot;, members of the suits were &quot;numbers&quot;, and the heads of the suits were &quot;faces&quot;. Spades handled security, protection and assassination. Clubs handled construction and infrastructure. Diamonds handled finances. Hearts handled social and political maneuvering. Most of the Faces were various kinds of supernaturals: the Ace of Spades was a Centimani Frankenstein, the Ace of Clubs was a Beast, the Ace of Diamonds was a Mage, and the Ace of Hearts was a vampire. Never got to do anything with the idea, but I liked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:22:28-07:00","id":963071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=962135#post962135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall the supplements, but P1e did provide some tools to sense and control pyros and related matters with the Arcana. I believe it required a combination of Mind and Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div> You misremember.<br /> <br /> A promethean book had rules for mages being able to sense pyros, and that was explicitly all they could do- sense it, no creating it, destroying it, or affecting it in anyway. <br /> <br /> Even in the mage book about archmasters who could create werewolves with vampire disciplines and changeling contracts, prometheans and transmutations are noticeable by their absence. <br /> <br /> Now of course in second edition they can change whatever they want, but in 1st edition it was pretty clear that as awesome as controlling the 10 arcana are, Pyros was classified as none of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T05:06:43-07:00","id":963170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=962193#post962193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Quibble - its not described <i>yet</i>. Pyros isn't fundamentally unknowable, its just fundamentally difficult to explore. Its like the magical equivalent of the Uncertanty Principle - interacting with a particle changes it, which limits what you can know about it, since you just changed all other variables by confirming one.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the maths model, Pyros might be an analogue of a transcendal number (eg pi or e) - numbers that can't be calculated by performing mathematical operations between any non-infinite combination of non-transcendental numbers. Put back into Mage terminology, there may be a Supernal symbol for the Divine Fire, but it can't be derived from analysing the symbols mages have access to - only vaguely approximated for a few limited circumstances.<br /> <br /> (In this model, the lower Arcana might be whole numbers, the subtle ones rational, the other supernatural purviews irrational, and the Abyss imaginary).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:46:42-07:00","id":963196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963170#post963170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the maths model, Pyros might be an analogue of a transcendal number (eg pi or e) - numbers that can't be calculated by performing mathematical operations between any non-infinite combination of non-transcendental numbers. Put back into Mage terminology, there may be a Supernal symbol for the Divine Fire, but it can't be derived from analysing the symbols mages have access to - only vaguely approximated for a few limited circumstances.<br /> <br /> (In this model, the lower Arcana might be whole numbers, the subtle ones rational, the other supernatural purviews irrational, and the Abyss imaginary).</div> </div> </div> </div> But is there any proof of this in the books? Forget the math comparison for a moment - is this whole &quot;can't understand&quot; thing actually cannon, or is it something fans came out with? Because, as far as I'm aware, its still just under the &quot;difficult to understand&quot; umbrella, rather than the idea of &quot;impossible to understand.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-04-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T07:26:02-07:00","id":963213,"title":"","content":"It's something fans came out with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T07:32:42-07:00","id":963215,"title":"","content":"We understand transcendental numbers just fine; we simply can't derive them from non-transcendental numbers. By this metaphor, mages could find supernal symbols for Pyros, but it would be a whole-cloth discovery, not a derivation from the Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T09:28:28-07:00","id":963249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963213#post963213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something fans came out with.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there is no canon-canon on Supernal magic with Divine Fire, yes? Only 'we do not know what to do with it', from Awakened perspective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T10:39:12-07:00","id":963266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=962711#post962711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely hoping we get plenty on splats working together and multi-splat organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can live without precious word count dedicated to multi-splat organizations. Not only would it be a wholesale revision to the entire CofD setting and require substantial space to do properly, I fear it would turn a relatively tight mature horror game into a young adult urban fantasy. Simply, while I very much enjoy settings like the Dresden Files and, like many others, use it for some inspiration in my games and characters, it's really not the primary milieu of the CofD.<br /> <br /> It's one thing for rules and chronicle advice for individual supernaturals to interact, but it's quite another to start engaging in alternative settings (which is something that OPP/WW has already done).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:15:49-07:00","id":963285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963266#post963266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can live without precious word count dedicated to multi-splat organizations. Not only would it be a wholesale revision to the entire CofD setting and require substantial space to do properly, I fear it would turn a relatively tight mature horror game into a young adult urban fantasy. Simply, while I very much enjoy settings like the Dresden Files and, like many others, use it for some inspiration in my games and characters, it's really not the primary milieu of the CofD.<br /> <br /> It's one thing for rules and chronicle advice for individual supernaturals to interact, but it's quite another to start engaging in alternative settings (which is something that OPP/WW has already done).</div> </div> </div> </div> So what would you put in the book then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:20:52-07:00","id":963288,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a Minor template, The Hierophants, that worship and gain powers from all the major templates, but different major templates given Hierophants different benifits.<br /> <br /> A Hierophants calling upon the name of a Changeling gets one benifit, yet calling upon a Sin Eater gets the Hierophant a different benifit, and calling upon a Promeathan a different one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:32:13-07:00","id":963298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963288#post963288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea for a Minor template, The Hierophants, that worship and gain powers from all the major templates, but different major templates given Hierophants different benifits.<br /> <br /> A Hierophants calling upon the name of a Changeling gets one benifit, yet calling upon a Sin Eater gets the Hierophant a different benifit, and calling upon a Promeathan a different one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be interesting, though I'd imagine it less like worship and more akin to forging a connection with them can grant you access to related abilities. Maybe they thus cultivate and do their best to protect those they're so connected to, lest they lose their benefits (and potent allies, for that matter). Some supernaturals might see it almost akin to worship because of that. But that's just my thoughts on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:36:09-07:00","id":963299,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's definitely going to be something about splat cooperation, and probably some intersplat organizations mentioned, even if they aren't fully written up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:36:21-07:00","id":963300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963285#post963285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what would you put in the book then?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I indicated in my original post, needed rules and mechanics, particularly concerning supernatural powers, for interaction among the multitude of splats, and chronicle advice for crossover play and mixed troupes, could easily fill multiple volumes. Not only has the CofD already published material concerning alternate settings, I would vastly prefer word count be dedicated to rules and advice concerning the current setting before yet more alternate material is even considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:37:56-07:00","id":963301,"title":"","content":"I think that will definitely be part of it, but I'd personally be disappointed if the book was just mechanical errata and chronicle advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:30:13-07:00","id":963329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963213#post963213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something fans came out with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which surprises me, because I clearly remember seeing something in one of the books about it. I don't remember it clearly enough to cite a page reference, mind you; but I <i>do</i> recall being surprised when I saw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:58:45-07:00","id":963346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963298#post963298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be interesting, though I'd imagine it less like worship and more akin to forging a connection with them can grant you access to related abilities. Maybe they thus cultivate and do their best to protect those they're so connected to, lest they lose their benefits (and potent allies, for that matter). Some supernaturals might see it almost akin to worship because of that. But that's just my thoughts on it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like they might be linked to the Primordial Dream. I like it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T15:49:23-07:00","id":963424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963329#post963329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which surprises me, because I clearly remember seeing something in one of the books about it. I don't remember it clearly enough to cite a page reference, mind you; but I <i>do</i> recall being surprised when I saw it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a full reread of 1e under my belt from within the last two years; the nearest the books get to &quot;the Divine Fire cannot be understood through the Supernal Arcana&quot; is &quot;qashmallim do not fall under the direct sway of the Forces Arcanum, mages attempting to create a Promethean risk burning out their Gnosis in the necessary realignment, and the Divine Fire definitely can't be manipulated through Awakened magic by anything short of an archmage.&quot;<br /> <br /> All of which roughly amounts to &quot;It is functionally impossible to dick around with a godlike being on a game-mechanical level without occupying a similar degree of abstraction from ground-level characters.&quot; The confusion of terms resulting from &quot;the Divine Fire&quot; being both a substance and an entity contributes some, but telephone takes things a lot farther.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:27:34-07:00","id":963435,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was in a Mage book? I clearly remember seeing something in print to the effect of \u201cthe Divine Fire is something that baffles mages, and can serve as a lesson in humility for the more hubristic ones\u201d, along with some speculation by mages that their difficulties with it might indicate that it's associated with the Lone Watchtower instead of the five that mages Awaken to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:39:48-07:00","id":963444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963435#post963435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it was in a Mage book? I clearly remember seeing something in print to the effect of \u201cthe Divine Fire is something that baffles mages, and can serve as a lesson in humility for the more hubristic ones\u201d, along with some speculation by mages that their difficulties with it might indicate that it's associated with the Lone Watchtower instead of the five that mages Awaken to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tome of Mysteries does go into Azoth being untouchable, but it all seems to be in the same vein of &quot;no you can't affect other supernatural templates&quot; that that book covered in general. It also calls Pyros mysterious and not able to be &quot;fully&quot; perceived or manipulated, and avoids scrutiny. Though I can't see anything about the divine fire being beyond the supernal's grasp entirely; it really all just seemed to be the same level of crossover rules you got with 1e in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:43:36-07:00","id":963445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of the Mysteries p48-49, &quot;Magic Versus Prometheans&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Created are alive \u2014 sort of. It\u2019s an artificial life sustained by a mysterious type of energy that defies even the Prime Arcanum\u2019s ability to fully perceive and manipulate.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Being able to identify a Promethean by the strange fire burning within him is not the same thing as understanding that fire. Pyros eludes the scant scrutiny most mages have been able to apply to it, and so remains a curious exception to the array of forces, Essence or Mana-based energies cataloged by mages.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> The Promethean\u2019s Azoth, the inner fire that animates him, cannot be targeted by Supernal magic, and so cannot be directly manipulated or altered by mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Lone Watchtower&quot; shows up as a phrase in four books, two from Promethean and two from Mage.<br /> <br /> It first appears in Mage 1e in the corebook as a wild theory.<br /> <br /> The first Promethean book it shows up in is the corebook, where it's still explicitly-theoretical and maybe the abode of the qashmallim in yet more wild theories.<br /> <br /> It next shows up as an incidental mention in Pandora's Book alongside all the other &quot;what do [potent specimens of the Big Three supernaturals] see when they [finally disappear into legend]?&quot; tidbits preceding the section on What The Principle Might Be.<br /> <br /> The last book it shows up in is Left-Hand Path, where it's postulated to be symbolized by the Elder Diadem.<br /> <br /> The only relevant places the phrase &quot;lesson in humility&quot; shows up are in Saturnine Night, where it's part of the writeup of Fredrich Hagen the clone-maker, and in Night Horrors: The Unbidden, where it's part of a sidebar about the False Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-04-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T17:22:04-07:00","id":963459,"title":"","content":"I think that, combined with Wood Ingham's &quot;New World of Gods and Monsters&quot; article in <b>Strange Alchemies</b> (&quot;<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">A Promethean is a new challenge for the mystic. The mages think that they have access to all things, but <u>the workings of the Pyros are completely alien to them</u>. Try as they might, their spells won\u2019t duplicate the feat. The power that drives the Created <u>resists the mages\u2019 efforts to steal and harness it.</u></span>&quot;) and a handful of references to &quot;scions of the Lone Watchtower&quot; in connection to <i>qashmallim</i>, might be what I'm remembering. In particular, <b>Tome of the Mysteries</b> singles out Pyros as &quot;<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">a curious exception to the array of forces, Essence or Mana-based energies cataloged by mages.</span>&quot; It's completely alien to them; their efforts to harness it are thwarted; the difficulty in scrutinizing it sets it apart from the other mystical energies mages have encountered. Yeah; I think that's how I got the impression that Pyros is beyond the scope of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> This was further reinforced years later by the curious exception in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> that provided the Arcana needed to create and modify templates for every major gameline <i>except</i> Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-04-2016, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T18:14:16-07:00","id":963475,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, I am more interested in expanding how the auras of the different kinds of supernaturals all interact and mix. For instnace - setting off a changeling Embracing the Wyrd versus the Uratha's Hunter Aspect, or the like. Vampire disciplines can be negated by Lashing Out - can this also happen from Hunter Aspects and a Nimbus? Should mage spells in general cause a comflict with Auras, given the close relationship of Nimbus and spellcraft? Should the same philosphy apply to other powers?<br /> <br /> I personally think this is some rather rich area to mine for stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:36:58-07:00","id":964279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963475#post963475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, I am more interested in expanding how the auras of the different kinds of supernaturals all interact and mix. For instnace - setting off a changeling Embracing the Wyrd versus the Uratha's Hunter Aspect, or the like. Vampire disciplines can be negated by Lashing Out - can this also happen from Hunter Aspects and a Nimbus? Should mage spells in general cause a comflict with Auras, given the close relationship of Nimbus and spellcraft? Should the same philosphy apply to other powers?<br /> <br /> I personally think this is some rather rich area to mine for stories.</div> </div> </div> </div> Those are interesting questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:40:10-07:00","id":964280,"title":"","content":"Mage actually says that mages flaring their nimbus works like lashing out in such crossover situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:42:43-07:00","id":964284,"title":"","content":"I had a realization in another thread, that a great unifying theme is being caught in the clash of competing shadowy organizations, each witb they're own strange agendas, all thristy for power, and all bearing dark &amp; damgerous secrets, coming from different gamelines. Its a nice over arching theme, that can easily tie the various themes from the other game lines together.<br /> <br /> I'd also like a settings chapters kike the core books of game lines get, preferably ones that already appear in various core books, like Toronto, Tokyo, Montreal, Tuscan, LA, Budapest, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:29:18-07:00","id":964310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=964284#post964284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a realization in another thread, that a great unifying theme is being caught in the clash of competing shadowy organizations, each witb they're own strange agendas, all thristy for power, and all bearing dark &amp; damgerous secrets, coming from different gamelines. Its a nice over arching theme, that can easily tie the various themes from the other game lines together.<br /> <br /> I'd also like a settings chapters kike the core books of game lines get, preferably ones that already appear in various core books, like Toronto, Tokyo, Montreal, Tuscan, LA, Budapest, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny that you mention that... *looks at my own chronicle* *coughs*<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's almost like someone looked at my game when they came up with this book. It's eerie. I mean, I know that's not the case, and I'm relatively unimportant in the grand scheme of things, but it's crazy similar, because the idea of this book is exactly how I run all my games, which all take place in the same Chronicle/continuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:48:04-07:00","id":964345,"title":"","content":"David Hill just revealed more details on Changeling Japan, and it seems like its largely designed for Crossover Chronicles, the Envoys connect the massive Freehold to all of the other Supernatural Creatures with tons of hooks. Combine it with the Toyko sections in the othet books and you have a really cool and complex, interacting setting, filled with all kinds of weirdness and mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T05:27:03-07:00","id":964904,"title":"","content":"Can fallen magic affect Pyros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:29:23-07:00","id":965004,"title":"","content":"What about places of power? Almost every splat has its places of power (&quot;dragon nests&quot;, loci, hallows...) and all these places gives the &quot;supernatural fuel&quot; most of these splats uses (essence, mana, plasm...). What about if a group of Mages are interested in the Dragon Nest of an Ordo Dracul group because they say it is a Hallow and must be theirs, or a pack of werewolves and a group of thyrsus mages are defending a Locus from the machinations of a greedy human villain that wants to expropiate the land to build a skycraper for his corporation?<br /> <br /> It is common to see Mage vs Mage or Wolf vs Wolf fighting for Hallows and Loci, but what about stealing it from other splats (or sharing it? or defending it?). Could a place, say a graveyard, give Essense with death resonation and also Plasm? Or a peacefull forest give Mana and Essence resonating with calm spirits?<br /> <br /> Thinking about all the different types of places and fuels makes my head ache, and I am thinking of giving the world the same fuel but named different and taken on different manner depending on the splat, and not &quot;fueling&quot; equally everyone depending on the resonance of that fuel, each splat feeling comfortable with one place or another. It is only an idea, but since I read the concept of &quot;resonance&quot; I fell in love with it.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see this treated in the new book, and also the conflicts for places of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 09-07-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:53:37-07:00","id":965018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965004#post965004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a pack of werewolves and a group of thyrsus mages are defending a Locus from the machinations of a greedy human villain that wants to expropiate the land to build a skycraper for his corporation?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a lot more pat than anything I'd hope for. Especially when the solution is a fairly obvious one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:03:21-07:00","id":965078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965018#post965018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems a lot more pat than anything I'd hope for. Especially when the solution is a fairly obvious one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eat the greedy human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:08:35-07:00","id":965087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965078#post965078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eat the greedy human?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dude calm down. I swear you should have that Obsession of yours checked. Back to planning the possession of Mr.Mayor by our totem, we need to focus.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:19:31-07:00","id":965102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965087#post965087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dude calm down. I swear you should have that Obsession of yours checked. Back to planning the possession of Mr.Mayor by our totem, we need to focus.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Thyrsus did spawn the Devourers of the Flesh and the Hunter's Flesh legacies.<br /> <br /> But yes, when the situation is 'one evil human' a lethal solution from monsters that aren't paladins isn't unreasonable to expect, and the situation is rather cut and dry. If you really want it could be a matter of 'make them change their mind' using magic and other manipulations.<br /> <br /> A better option might be something like, how would the storyteller bring together a pack and cabal that share the same 'feeding ground,' when a pylon of Seers or pack of Pure move in. Which still puts it into an easy problem of 'good versus bad,' so you can just have the newcomers be another cabal or Forsaken pack. Or what do the predatory vampires and werewolves who share the area around the spot do when a cabal moves in?<br /> <br /> Just glancing at it it doesn't seem like Hallows and loci have overlap, though given their importance I could see some being created. And a vampire feeding ground might create its own locus. So it seems like it might come down to territory more than resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:24:16-07:00","id":965106,"title":"","content":"What does a vampire do when their Touchstone has been &quot;replaced&quot; by a Demon (via Soul Pact)? Are they still a Touchstone? Do you just go raiding questionable office buildings on the weekends now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:36:14-07:00","id":965124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965106#post965106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does a vampire do when their Touchstone has been &quot;replaced&quot; by a Demon (via Soul Pact)? Are they still a Touchstone? Do you just go raiding questionable office buildings on the weekends now?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an amazing story hook. &quot;Man, ever since you won the lottery, you've also been spending a lot of time staking out that Deva Corp. Warehouse Manager's house. What's the deal?&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's another weird idea: what if your Touchstone made a Pact and traded their relationship with you to a Demon? Your character wouldn't know anything had changed, but maybe your coterie would?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:40:08-07:00","id":965128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965106#post965106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does a vampire do when their Touchstone has been &quot;replaced&quot; by a Demon (via Soul Pact)? Are they still a Touchstone? Do you just go raiding questionable office buildings on the weekends now?</div> </div> </div> </div>If one of the Unchained is doing their job properly then yeah all that happens is the touchstone individual would act a little weird here and there nothing to worry about. From what I understand a touchstone isn't a mystical thing its just the connection with the individual, so this probably wouldn't be affected by the Unchained taking the person's place. Especially as a soul pact would just have the Demon wearing the person's life as a suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:40:27-07:00","id":965130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965124#post965124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like an amazing story hook. &quot;Man, ever since you won the lottery, you've also been spending a lot of time staking out that Deva Corp. Warehouse Manager's house. What's the deal?&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's another weird idea: what if your Touchstone made a Pact and traded their relationship with you to a Demon? Your character wouldn't know anything had changed, but maybe your coterie would?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Alright, why have you been spending so much time with that weirdo?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean, I've always spent my early Friday mornings chatting with Phil.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...No. You haven't.&quot;<br /> <hr /><br /> Here's another one.<br /> <br /> The Demon uses the Vampire as a reference for their Cover (Just ask my good friend Vlad where I was that weekend. I'm just another regular human doing regular human things.)<br /> <br /> ...Which puts the investigators onto the Vampire (who may have problems with interviews during daylight hours).<br /> <br /> ...Which has the Demon and/or investigators looked into as a Masquerade risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:38:26-07:00","id":965238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965087#post965087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Dude calm down. I swear you should have that Obsession of yours checked. Back to planning the possession of Mr.Mayor by our totem, we need to focus.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hahahaha good one!<br /> <br /> And if the Mr. Mayor is a puppet of an Invictus high rank vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:46:15-07:00","id":965243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965238#post965238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hahahaha good one!<br /> <br /> And if the Mr. Mayor is a puppet of an Invictus high rank vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>What if he is only pretending he is, while secretly being the high priest of a Deceived cult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T14:24:19-07:00","id":965266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965243#post965243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if he is only pretending he is, while secretly being the high priest of a Deceived cult?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the CofD, are there really many humans left in local government that aren't controlled, possessed, magically cowed, simply replaced or far, far worse by the innumerable mages, vampires, werewolves, demons, or other supernatural groups and individuals, various and sundry?<br /> <br /> I want to know what it's like for the rare independent, free-willed &quot;real&quot; human in the county clerk's office or local zoning board. <br /> <br /> I shall assume they're quickly recruited by TFV or some other hunter group or join a cult before its too late.<br /> <br /> The real question is what groups of supernaturals treat their slaves, errr...., vassals the best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:09:11-07:00","id":965284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965266#post965266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the CofD, are there really many humans left in local government that aren't controlled, possessed, magically cowed, simply replaced or far, far worse by the innumerable mages, vampires, werewolves, demons, or other supernatural groups and individuals, various and sundry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, supernaturals don't have the numbers to deal with them all, and even if they did they're not organized enough to do so and the vast majority wouldn't care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want to know what it's like for the rare independent, free-willed &quot;real&quot; human in the county clerk's office or local zoning board. </div> </div> </div>That's what almost all the blue books depict, their fiction often goes into it, though I don't know if there's specifically a county clerk or local zoning board officer.<br /> <br /> Boiled down: It's a little weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:36:35-07:00","id":965361,"title":"","content":"On another site, within the past few days, I started a Crossover play-by-post game, since I haven't gotten to run one in 2e yet and I was inspired by this thread and the announcement itself. I have 2 Beasts, 2 Vampires, 1 Werewolf, and 1 Changeling (playtest rules with some tweaks), which, yes, means I ended up with a big group in addition to it being crossover, which is even more difficult, but I had trouble saying no to people showing interest, heh. (Mages, of course, were banned for reasons I've gone into previously, and they're very rare within the city)<br /> <br /> Anyway, a few things I've done is make it a setting conducive to it; like I've mentioned before, it's one where there's a small number of PC-type supernatural beings, but a large amount of supernatural happenstance, so it's a bit 'tier 1' in scope, with little more than a non-aggression pact spanning all supernatural groups for government.<br /> <br /> For the group itself (who have essentially come together as a bunch of professional know-it-alls i.e information traders), given the werewolf wanted a totem, beasts wanted family ties, changelings have pledges (I said Oaths work on supernaturals, but are unpredictable), and the Kindred would likely have been considering blood bonds, I made it so the combination of the different means of connection caused a sort of unifying effect that'll make things incredibly difficult if broken, but provides some unusual benefits that no given connection alone would offer. Bit of a plot device level of unity that they'll uncover more details about as things progress.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm planning to make a big deal about is how different supernaturals all have their own unique senses, and each individual similarly may have unique sensory powers as well. I try to add little side-notes for every individual, describing things only they can sense, a small part of the whole that they'll need. They all have ways to gather information, but it's the combination of all of the facets they can cover in their own unique way that'll make them so formidable in their &quot;field&quot;.<br /> <br /> No real specific reason to mention this past thought spewing in case it helps anyone else, and any conversation/idea-churning it could potentially spark to make my life easier, heh.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:46:48-07:00","id":965544,"title":"","content":"I really like what you did with all the bond-like abilities of the different splats, I may use it if I ever run a crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:51:23-07:00","id":965600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965004#post965004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about all the different types of places and fuels makes my head ache, and I am thinking of giving the world the same fuel but named different and taken on different manner depending on the splat, and not &quot;fueling&quot; equally everyone depending on the resonance of that fuel, each splat feeling comfortable with one place or another. It is only an idea, but since I read the concept of &quot;resonance&quot; I fell in love with it.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see this treated in the new book, and also the conflicts for places of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd certainly be interested in options for how the various fuels &quot;relate&quot; to one another. Like, in my headcanon, glamour can sort of be understood as dSekhem/dt, and vitae and plasm are strongly related.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:10:07-07:00","id":965652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965600#post965600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd certainly be interested in options for how the various fuels &quot;relate&quot; to one another. Like, in my headcanon, glamour can sort of be understood as dSekhem/dt, and vitae and plasm are strongly related.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I'd have thought Pyros and Sekhem would be closer, while Glamour would be nearer to Mana or Essence. And we all know Aether is a specific kind of Essence byproduct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:22:50-07:00","id":965656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965284#post965284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, supernaturals don't have the numbers to deal with them all, and even if they did they're not organized enough to do so and the vast majority wouldn't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been thinking about this theme, supernaturals and normal humans.<br /> <br /> The point is that, although the books always pay attention in that humans are dangerous because its numbers, and must not be underestimated, then after reading about all the factions there that manipulate humankind and deal with humans and are obsessive about control (Invictus, Carthian movement, Masters of Iron, Silver Ladder, Seers of the Throne...) with all their mind control powers and infiltration powers (obfuscate discipline, mage veiling practice...), as a reader I begin to see vampires, werewolves, mages, fae... everywhere, and ruling the world through their puppets.<br /> <br /> For me it has been a breaking point and I rolled an integrity check not to take the Paranoid Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the CofD, are there really many humans left in local government that aren't controlled, possessed, magically cowed, simply replaced or far, far worse by the innumerable mages, vampires, werewolves, demons, or other supernatural groups and individuals, various and sundry?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the sensation I got. No matter how much I read that humans must be taken with care. What prevents the Major of New York, for example, being Dominated by an Invictus Ventrue, then Fascinated by a Daeva, then possessed by a spirit sent by an Ithaeur, then programmed by a Seer of the Throne and after that seduced into a pledge by a beautiful fairest changeling? Or perhaps all this splats are too busy stabbing each other to pay attention to this? It got to the point that it looked ridiculous, or funny, depending on the point of view (poor Major...).<br /> <br /> So I have been thinking of this, and I remembered the essential: that the one who decides this is the Storyteller. And some Storytellers (like me, a CoD novice one), tend to forget this.<br /> <br /> Players may think the Major is a weakling (human = no superpowers = weakling), but is the Storyteller who decides it. He decides if that Major is a weakling, a ghoul, a sleeper, a wolf-blooded, a possessed human, if he knows about supernaturals or not, or if he is stubborn as stone and manipulative and emotionless to make a city Prince blush in shame...<br /> <br /> The trick, I think, is looking to the real world. Maybe humans have no &quot;superpowers&quot; compared to supernaturals, but they can be very, very dangerous, and do whatever is necessary to be done to achieve their objectives.<br /> <br /> Is good for me to allow players having fun with their &quot;supers&quot; beating and manipulating human scum, defeating the villain with their powers. Those are funny sessions that players and I enjoy a lot. But I also think it will be good to remember players how dark and dangerous humans can be from time to time, in adventures where the mood is &quot;Who is the real monster?&quot;<br /> <br /> Is a thing I would like see covered in the book ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 09-08-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:47:46-07:00","id":965672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965656#post965656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have been thinking about this theme, supernaturals and normal humans.<br /> <br /> The point is that, although the books always pay attention in that humans are dangerous because its numbers, and must not be underestimated, then after reading about all the factions there that manipulate humankind and deal with humans and are obsessive about control (Invictus, Carthian movement, Masters of Iron, Silver Ladder, Seers of the Throne...) with all their mind control powers and infiltration powers (obfuscate discipline, mage veiling practice...), as a reader I begin to see vampires, werewolves, mages, fae... everywhere, and ruling the world through their puppets.<br /> <br /> For me it has been a breaking point and I rolled an integrity check not to take the Paranoid Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is the sensation I got. No matter how much I read that humans must be taken with care. What prevents the Major of New York, for example, being Dominated by an Invictus Ventrue, then Fascinated by a Daeva, then possessed by a spirit sent by an Ithaeur, then programmed by a Seer of the Throne and after that seduced into a pledge by a beautiful fairest changeling? Or perhaps all this splats are too busy stabbing each other to pay attention to this? It got to the point that it looked ridiculous, or funny, depending on the point of view (poor Major...).<br /> <br /> So I have been thinking of this, and I remembered the essential: that the one who decides this is the Storyteller. And some Storytellers (like me, a CoD novice one), tend to forget this.<br /> <br /> Players may think the Major is a weakling (human = no superpowers = weakling), but is the Storyteller who decides it. He decides if that Major is a weakling, a ghoul, a sleeper, a wolf-blooded, a possessed human, if he knows about supernaturals or not, or if he is stubborn as stone and manipulative and emotionless to make a city Prince blush in shame...<br /> <br /> The trick, I think, is looking to the real world. Maybe humans have no &quot;superpowers&quot; compared to supernaturals, but they can be very, very dangerous, and do whatever is necessary to be done to achieve their objectives.<br /> <br /> Is good for me to allow players having fun with their &quot;supers&quot; beating and manipulating human scum, defeating the villain with their powers. Those are funny sessions that players and I enjoy a lot. But I also think it will be good to remember players how dark and dangerous humans can be from time to time, in adventures where the mood is &quot;Who is the real monster?&quot;<br /> <br /> Is a thing I would like see covered in the book ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that people sufficiently high up in political (or other) hierarchies, such a mayors, police commissioners, generals, CEO's of major companies, etc., are not generally controlled or directly influenced by the supernatural factions because they are too high profile and any problems could backfire spectacularly. When seeking to control governments and other entities, supernaturals target key advisers, middle managers and other who actually implement policy on a practical level or themselves have significant influence over the primary decision-makers.<br /> <br /> For instance, controlling the head of the zoning board, the mayor's chief of staff or a few police precinct captains can be far easier, more efficient and productive, and far less risky than trying to control the mayor himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:59:47-07:00","id":965681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965672#post965672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the impression that people sufficiently high up in political (or other) hierarchies, such a mayors, police commissioners, generals, CEO's of major companies, etc., are not generally controlled or directly influenced by the supernatural factions because they are too high profile and any problems could backfire spectacularly. When seeking to control governments and other entities, supernaturals target key advisers, middle managers and other who actually implement policy on a practical level or themselves have significant influence over the primary decision-makers.<br /> <br /> For instance, controlling the head of the zoning board, the mayor's chief of staff or a few police precinct captains can be far easier, more efficient and productive, and far less risky than trying to control the mayor himself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good point of view. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:08:37-07:00","id":965727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965672#post965672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, controlling the head of the zoning board, the mayor's chief of staff or a few police precinct captains can be far easier, more efficient and productive, and far less risky than trying to control the mayor himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That also creates one of my favorite situations: opposing characters in an corporate setting. <br /> <br /> Think <i>The Office</i>, but with subtle supernatural powers engaged in a cold war where no-one wants to rock the boat too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:38:05-07:00","id":965739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965656#post965656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been thinking about this theme, supernaturals and normal humans.<br /> <br /> The point is that, although the books always pay attention in that humans are dangerous because its numbers, and must not be underestimated, then after reading about all the factions there that manipulate humankind and deal with humans and are obsessive about control (Invictus, Carthian movement, Masters of Iron, Silver Ladder, Seers of the Throne...) with all their mind control powers and infiltration powers (obfuscate discipline, mage veiling practice...), as a reader I begin to see vampires, werewolves, mages, fae... everywhere, and ruling the world through their puppets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is you seem to be taking 'control' as in humans as some sort of slave who kneels before an enthroned supernatural. It can be as subtle as someone just being rich and being able to donate to the right groups. It can be much more subtle than that, if it happens at all.<br /> <br /> For one thing if you've read about these groups you know that Seers are rare, the Silver Ladder focuses on mystery cults, the Invictus and Carthians are not global or interested in micromanaging the world, and the Iron Masters don't have any reason to work from the shadows. An Invictus Prince might have an 'in' with the mayor or governor, but they're just another one of dozens of rich and powerful people who do. The Seers aren't everywhere, but the Exarchs already rule the world, their system is in place. Silver Ladder isn't about enslaving humanity but uplifting them through the mysteries of their cults. A werewolf-run company was detailed pretty well in the Pack book, they're good at what they do and surely use supernatural abilities to help but outwardly they're just a good, fairly well known if insular company.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is the sensation I got. No matter how much I read that humans must be taken with care. What prevents the Major of New York, for example, being Dominated by an Invictus Ventrue, then Fascinated by a Daeva, then possessed by a spirit sent by an Ithaeur, then programmed by a Seer of the Throne and after that seduced into a pledge by a beautiful fairest changeling? Or perhaps all this splats are too busy stabbing each other to pay attention to this? It got to the point that it looked ridiculous, or funny, depending on the point of view (poor Major...). </div> </div> </div>The fact that the mayor of New York doesn't have that much power and it's not worth the effort it would take to control him. That politics in your own group are complicated enough without worrying about the details of an actual political campaign for an elected official you could only conceivably interact with at night time. That a possessed being isn't going to be programmed or seduced into a pledge. This is the kind of thing that works great in a feudal era or time when there was a single ruler who could say all, but there's entire systems of checks and balances to ensure that a mayor doesn't control every aspect of the city. Even the leader of the free world, the president of the United States can't have the army go from house to house and confiscate your guns and silver bullets if he wanted to. He might be able to write up a law to outlaw silver bullets and private ownership of them, but that law has to pass through the houses to be put into effect, and while he can make an executive order over it, that can be overturned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Players may think the Major is a weakling (human = no superpowers = weakling), but is the Storyteller who decides it. He decides if that Major is a weakling, a ghoul, a sleeper, a wolf-blooded, a possessed human, if he knows about supernaturals or not, or if he is stubborn as stone and manipulative and emotionless to make a city Prince blush in shame... </div> </div> </div>It's a given in the Chronicles that people know about the supernatural. It would be strange for someone with at least a modicum of influence and access to information about an area to not at least have a hint of what actually lives there. I believe this has been explicitly stated, with world leaders all at least knowing what's out there, but I couldn't be sure.<br /> <br /> It's in the fiction, though. Prince Maxwell has influence because he knows people, and he's wealthy. Solomon Birch and Norris because they've got their hooks into the right people. They don't need to dominate the mayor because that doesn't really get them anything they can't get easier and without risking the Masquerade through some other means.<br /> <br /> Considering books like a Thousand Years of Night portray the 'end level' supernaturals like vampires as part-conspiracy, I'd expect some more of this in books like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2016, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:21:15-07:00","id":965790,"title":"","content":"I believe that the governments being aware of supernatural was stated in Dave's Premeditation story in the Beast Anthology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:30:47-07:00","id":965797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965790#post965790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that the governments being aware of supernatural was stated in Dave's Premeditation story in the Beast Anthology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. Although it really felt more like a setting update than something that was always the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-08-2016, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:43:40-07:00","id":965805,"title":"","content":"'Every government knows monsters exist.' Which is in line with the Chronicles of Darkness. It's not as if Task Force Valkyrie isn't a thing.<br /> <br /> But lets also keep in mind this doesn't mean once you get a government job you're sent copies of Vampire the Requiem Second Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:44:43-07:00","id":965806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965797#post965797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Indeed. Although it really felt more like a setting update than something that was always the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, TASKFORCE VALKYRIE and other Conspiracies should have been proof that knowledge of the supernatural exists at high organizational levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:07:42-07:00","id":965859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=965806#post965806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, TASKFORCE VALKYRIE and other Conspiracies should have been proof that knowledge of the supernatural exists at high organizational levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least <i>some part</i> of the organization knows. TF:V existing doesn't necessarily mean everyone is briefed on them, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:14:52-07:00","id":965864,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> for your comments. You helped me a lot, really <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T19:53:11-07:00","id":966544,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong, but doesn't HtV says that the president doesn't even know what TFV does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T05:04:52-07:00","id":966713,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but there's an adventure which makes it clear that both the Vice President and President know about the supernatural.<br /> <br /> In the woundgate setting, it's mentioned that the US government is aware of the Occult states of america, and that all national governments are aware of the shatterlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:27:31-07:00","id":966769,"title":"","content":"I guess it depends on which president the books talked about. Also isn't the woundgate non-canon as a part of Mirrors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:02:35-07:00","id":966779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=966713#post966713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe, but there's an adventure which makes it clear that both the Vice President and President know about the supernatural.<br /> <br /> In the woundgate setting, it's mentioned that the US government is aware of the Occult states of america, and that all national governments are aware of the shatterlands.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Woundgate is an alternative setting, no cannon CofD.<br /> <br /> I was under the impression that limited elements of various governments know that the supernatural exists and can be quite threatening. The vast majority of the governments' bureaucracy doesn't know about the supernatural (any more than everyone in the CofD has some vague sense about it), and what they do know is often incomplete, piecemeal or even wrong.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that some of the people in the know in government are supernatural themselves or servants of supernaturals. Why strike directly at your enemies when the taxpayers and ignorant government drones will do it for you (e.g., Division 6)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-10-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:18:59-07:00","id":966808,"title":"","content":"Knowing about the supernatural and knowing about Task Force Valkyrie are two separate things. Everyone knows about the supernatural, the vast majority of people don't know about the extent of it, with multiple alternate worlds and entire nations of people that aren't people.<br /> <br /> All that said, there's no reason to believe the mage from Premeditation is accurate. Mages are capable of being wrong and believing in conspiracy theories as easy as Sleepers. People know about the supernatural, and people make up the government, that does not mean that the governments of the world are more fully aware of things than the average human.<br /> <br /> That said, the president is an elected official who may be in and out of the government in 4 or 8 years, or even less. Sharing all the secrets of the world with someone who will effectively be out of the government in that time may not be something they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:44:18-07:00","id":966826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=966808#post966808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing about the supernatural and knowing about Task Force Valkyrie are two separate things. Everyone knows about the supernatural, the vast majority of people don't know about the extent of it, with multiple alternate worlds and entire nations of people that aren't people.<br /> <br /> All that said, there's no reason to believe the mage from Premeditation is accurate. Mages are capable of being wrong and believing in conspiracy theories as easy as Sleepers. People know about the supernatural, and people make up the government, that does not mean that the governments of the world are more fully aware of things than the average human.<br /> <br /> That said, the president is an elected official who may be in and out of the government in 4 or 8 years, or even less. Sharing all the secrets of the world with someone who will effectively be out of the government in that time may not be something they do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DaveB commented about the issue on 4chan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#117743\"><b>Anonymous</b></span> Sat 23 Apr 2016 08:14:00 <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46838856/#46853478\" target=\"_blank\">No.</a><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46838856/#q46853478\" target=\"_blank\">46853478</a> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/report/46853478/\" target=\"_blank\">Report</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#888888\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Quoted By: <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46838856/#46853527\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;46853527</a> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46838856/#46853659\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;46853659</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#364041\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Has anyone read DaveB's story &quot;Premeditation&quot; from the Beast Fiction Anthology?<br /> <br /> Among other things, I was amused by one interesting bit on p. 140, where Hal, the smug and knowledgeable mage, confidently states that every government knows about the supernatural, and some even kidnap or disappear certain members.<br /> <br /> Was this a Hunter reference, some new canon part of the setting in 2e, or was Dave just fucking around?</span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#117743\"><b>DaveB</b></span> <span style=\"color:#117743\">!!kn3vuELOelB</span> Sat 23 Apr 2016 08:37:33 <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46838856/#46853659\" target=\"_blank\">No.</a><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46838856/#q46853659\" target=\"_blank\">46853659</a> <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/46838856/#46853659\" target=\"_blank\">View</a><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/report/46853659/\" target=\"_blank\">Report</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#364041\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#789922\"><a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/post/46853478/\" target=\"_blank\">&gt;&gt;46853478</a></span><br /> <br /> A little of column A and a little of column B.<br /> <br /> Morocco really does have secret prisons, and the government disappears people - in the 90s, it was anyone who the King thought was a risk to him, while nowadays, it does so with the support of the US, who use them for kidnapping people under the War on Terror.<br /> <br /> Najat's dad was the kind of person to get vanished even without being a shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> But yes, I assume everyone in the CofD setting knows about the supernatural, but only a few want to think about it and even fewer do something about it. TFV probably has equivalents all over the world.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:08:30-07:00","id":967109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=966826#post966826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> DaveB commented about the issue on 4chan.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I recall a piece from Vampire about a vampire who has a night guard as a Touchstone. The night guard all but said that she knew what the vampire was, and had once had misgivings, but is willing to let the vampire be as long as her or she only preys on people who are a threat to the innocent people of the neighborhood- all through an extended metaphor about coyotes.<br /> <br /> One of the big things with CofD is that most people have had some sort of brush with the supernatural. Maybe not enough to blow the lid off of the whole thing, but enough to make people stay away from dark allies, the whole &quot;there but for the grace of God&quot; shtick. But nobody is willing to talk about it, because to do so is to draw people's attention to the Things that Go Bump, and nobody wants to think about how vulnerable they are. So off to the loony house with anybody who mentions that time they saw somebody drinking blood from another person's neck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 09-11-2016, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:24:15-07:00","id":967199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=966779#post966779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woundgate is an alternative setting, no cannon CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure Woundgate has plenty of cannons, actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, there's no such thing as canon in CofD. One uses what they like and discards the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:32:40-07:00","id":967200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967199#post967199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure Woundgate has plenty of cannons, actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, there's no such thing as canon in CofD. One uses what they like and discards the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Typo aside, there is most certainly a default <i>canon</i> setting in the CofD. You may choose to include or exclude whatever you wish, and most us change something in our own games, but there is indeed a defined and intended setting. Moreover, most of Mirrors, including Woundgate was explicitly alternative setting material. That was the whole point of the book. Using to prove or disprove anything about the CofD is unproductive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T04:20:25-07:00","id":967258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967200#post967200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Typo aside, there is most certainly a default <i>canon</i> setting in the CofD. You may choose to include or exclude whatever you wish, and most us change something in our own games, but there is indeed a defined and intended setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as the developers made sure that there are incomatible elements between the different splat's cosmologies on purpose I'd say there is less a &quot;defined and intended setting&quot;. More like a continuum of intended yet sometime mutually exclusive setting elements, parts of which you can combine to form a full setting without big internal inconsistencies and which fits OPP's vision of how the CofD looks and feels like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:56:15-07:00","id":967405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967258#post967258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as the developers made sure that there are incomatible elements between the different splat's cosmologies on purpose I'd say there is less a &quot;defined and intended setting&quot;. More like a continuum of intended yet sometime mutually exclusive setting elements, parts of which you can combine to form a full setting without big internal inconsistencies and which fits OPP's vision of how the CofD looks and feels like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Purportedly inconsistent cosmologies among certain splats does not change the fact that there's an intended setting in the CofD. In fact, these alleged inconsistencies are part and parcel of the setting and intended to convey the mystery and horror of the game world (and permit new material to be added over time). Moreover, the cosmologies are largely about myth, history and purpose, that may inform and motivate characters, but they still exist withing the same defined setting. For instance, the contemporary setting remains the same regardless of whether a character believes in the Dark Mother, Atlantis or the God Machine. I agree that OPP intentionally made it easy to remove or change parts of the setting to suit players needs and preferences, particularly, in 2e, such as whether to include the God Machine in a particular chronicle, but the ability to add or excise setting elements has nothing to do with whether there is a intended and defined setting, rather it's evidence of good rpg game design.<br /> <br /> In any event, Woundgate still was explicitly presented as an alternative setting in a book expressly about alternative material. While some may like Woundgate, including myself, it offers little guidance or meaning about the &quot;default&quot; CofD, regardless of whether one considers the CofD as a single defined setting or a set toolbox consisting of individual gameline settings designed to be compatible.<br /> <br /> These issues, however, do demonstrate how difficult a true crossover chronicle book (or gameline) will be to produce without aggravating many fans, rewriting large setting elements, or requiring the word count of a large encyclopedia set.<br /> <br /> While I'm very anxious to see the final product, and will almost certainly buy the first book, I do not envy the developer and writers on this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:24:51-07:00","id":967559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967258#post967258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as the developers made sure that there are incomatible elements between the different splat's cosmologies on purpose I'd say there is less a &quot;defined and intended setting&quot;. More like a continuum of intended yet sometime mutually exclusive setting elements, parts of which you can combine to form a full setting without big internal inconsistencies and which fits OPP's vision of how the CofD looks and feels like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please describe some of these incompatible elements. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:55:36-07:00","id":967834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967200#post967200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typo aside, there is most certainly a default <i>canon</i> setting in the CofD. You may choose to include or exclude whatever you wish, and most us change something in our own games, but there is indeed a defined and intended setting. Moreover, most of Mirrors, including Woundgate was explicitly alternative setting material. That was the whole point of the book. Using to prove or disprove anything about the CofD is unproductive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's play then.<br /> <br /> Let's take Second Sight.<br /> <br /> Are psychic powers abilities innate human potential, the result of genetic mutation, the result of scientific enhancement, or the gift of angelic or other such entities? The book give all of them as options, which one(s) are canon?<br /> <br /> Is thaumaturge the result of certain rituals just having innate power, the result of human belief, blessings by angels/spirits/other such entities, all of the above, or the result of partial awakenings into pseudo-mages? The book gives all of them as options, which one(s) are canon?<br /> <br /> In second edition in which psychic powers (and presumably one day thaumaturge) are supernatural merits, which of the above ways to gain them are canon options and which aren't? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 09-12-2016, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:37:51-07:00","id":967870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967834#post967834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are psychic powers abilities innate human potential, the result of genetic mutation, the result of scientific enhancement, or the gift of angelic or other such entities? The book give all of them as options, which one(s) are canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason why &quot;all of the above, and more besides&quot; isn't a valid answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967834#post967834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is thaumaturge the result of certain rituals just having innate power, the result of human belief, blessings by angels/spirits/other such entities, all of the above, or the result of partial awakenings into pseudo-mages? The book gives all of them as options, which one(s) are canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say &quot;all of the above&quot; or even &quot;there is no actual distinction&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967834#post967834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In second edition in which psychic powers (and presumably one day thaumaturge) are supernatural merits, which of the above ways to gain them are canon options and which aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of them? Learn occult ritual? Supernatural Merit! Rare genetic quirk? Supernatural Merit! Scientific augmentation? Supernatural Merit (see Lost Boys in Hurt Locker preview)! Gift of other being? Well, Demons can inflict Stigmata, and I doubt Spirits and many other such powers can't do the same, so Supernatural Merit!<br /> <br /> None of these options invalidate the others. They just mean there is more than one way to telekinetically skin a cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:41:36-07:00","id":968613,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping we get a few crossover subsplats, but I understand that other people aren't really that interested in that side of things. Maybe as a stretch goal? I think this is a big enough project to warrant a Companion and maybe even a follow up. Oh, is there going to be a fiction anthology?<br /> <br /> I've mentioned thinking this would be a great chance for ChroD Kiasyd before, and that's honestly mostly why I want crossover z-splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:06:01-07:00","id":971107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=967870#post967870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see no reason why &amp;quot;all of the above, and more besides&amp;quot; isn't a valid answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd say &amp;quot;all of the above&amp;quot; or even &amp;quot;there is no actual distinction&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All of them? Learn occult ritual? Supernatural Merit! Rare genetic quirk? Supernatural Merit! Scientific augmentation? Supernatural Merit (see Lost Boys in Hurt Locker preview)! Gift of other being? Well, Demons can inflict Stigmata, and I doubt Spirits and many other such powers can't do the same, so Supernatural Merit!<br /> <br /> None of these options invalidate the others. They just mean there is more than one way to telekinetically skin a cat.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Fate Arcana at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 has a spell that can grant Supernatural merits and the MCI which can and often is centred around Supernatural beings can also grant Supernatural Merits. There maybe other ways too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:39:36-07:00","id":971601,"title":"","content":"I hope we get some new and updated z-splats in this, focused on crossover. <i>Ancient Bloodlines</i> gives us the Usiri, a Nosferatu bloodline out of Ancient Egypt tasked with borrowing the memories of sleeping elders for safekeeping in order to recite them once they rise from torpor and must contend with the Fog of Ages; with the Fog gone in 2e, they're left more or less pointless... unless there happened to be a convenient group of immortal amnesiacs running around Egypt that may well need help with their faulty Memory!<br /> <br /> Now the tough part is whether I cross my fingers for this to make it into the book or do it myself now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T15:18:28-08:00","id":1006878,"title":"","content":"So does anyone here think a changeling promethean mage and god-machine crossover would work well for a invasion of the body snatchers type chronicle or do think i should add a forth splat for humanity? because i'm thinking of run a body snatchers parody game next year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:27:59-08:00","id":1010493,"title":"","content":"So I asked Rich about the Crossover Chronicles in the comments on last Monday Meetings and he said that he's not sure if CC will be Kickstarted this coming year (2017) or the next. So maybeeeeeee we get everything to 2e or at least in production for 2e before Crossover Chronicles drops?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T16:52:28-08:00","id":1014515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=1010493#post1010493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I asked Rich about the Crossover Chronicles in the comments on last Monday Meetings and he said that he's not sure if CC will be Kickstarted this coming year (2017) or the next. So maybeeeeeee we get everything to 2e or at least in production for 2e before Crossover Chronicles drops?</div> </div> </div> </div> Lets see what settings are done and what are left.<br /> <br /> Prommy, werewolf, vampire, mage, beast, demon, are done, Changeling should be in a matter of months. <br /> <br /> The leaves Giest the Sin Eater and Mummy. Giest has already started, so we'll see how that goes.<br /> <br /> Mummy feels too soon to get a whole new edition, I mean I'm still getting stuff from the kickstarter! So I'd suggest Crossover Chronicles just include a mechanics update for Mummy, done.<br /> <br /> So that would mean very thing would depend on Geist getting finished in time for a Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T16:59:34-08:00","id":1014518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=1014515#post1014515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lets see what settings are done and what are left.<br /> <br /> Prommy, werewolf, vampire, mage, beast, demon, are done, Changeling should be in a matter of months.<br /> <br /> The leaves Giest the Sin Eater and Mummy. Giest has already started, so we'll see how that goes.<br /> <br /> Mummy feels too soon to get a whole new edition, I mean I'm still getting stuff from the kickstarter! So I'd suggest Crossover Chronicles just include a mechanics update for Mummy, done.<br /> <br /> So that would mean very thing would depend on Geist getting finished in time for a Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Deviant should also be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T17:56:03-08:00","id":1014548,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Hunter. Also, that seems like a pretty optimistic prediction re: Changeling and Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:08:23-08:00","id":1014556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=1014515#post1014515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lets see what settings are done and what are left.<br /> <br /> Prommy, werewolf, vampire, mage, beast, demon, are done, Changeling should be in a matter of months. <br /> <br /> The leaves Giest the Sin Eater and Mummy. Giest has already started, so we'll see how that goes.<br /> <br /> Mummy feels too soon to get a whole new edition, I mean I'm still getting stuff from the kickstarter! So I'd suggest Crossover Chronicles just include a mechanics update for Mummy, done.<br /> <br /> So that would mean very thing would depend on Geist getting finished in time for a Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the timeline holds, I'd expect Mummy 2e announced in 2017 and released in 2019 or 2020.<br /> <br /> That hurt to write out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T08:38:17-07:00","id":1130283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=1014556#post1014556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming the timeline holds, I'd expect Mummy 2e announced in 2017 and released in 2019 or 2020.<br /> <br /> That hurt to write out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you were right on the first part. Anyone's guess when it gets released, but I'm holding out for late 2018, early 2019. <br /> <br /> Anywho... I'm guessing that the Crossover Chronicle is now the Contagen Chronicle based off of this year's <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/217030/Onyx-Path-Publishing-Brochure-2017?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">brochure</a>. I dig it. Supernatural diseases are always fun. I wonder if it will make use of the Infected from Hurt Locker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T08:56:02-07:00","id":1130290,"title":"","content":"'The Contagion Chronicle is an overarching Chronicle consisting of chronicle hooks,riveting settings, and Storyteller aids to help present all the Chronicles of Darkness game lines into one consistent story. In the chronicle, the Contagion acts as a motivational force and inspires the formation of factions where vampires, werewolves, mages, mummies, etc. come together in new and unique ways.<br /> Once joined together to deal with the Contagion, these factions will never see their world (or each other) the same way, and will be forever changed. Each time the Contagion emerges to threaten the fabric of our world, the only beings capable of manipulating, slowing, weaponizing, or halting it, are the unnatural denizens from across the Chronicles of Darkness. The Contagion permeates Infrastructure and warps the known antagonists and supporting blocks present in the lives of every inhuman being.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:51:22-07:00","id":1130322,"title":"","content":"Interesting. The first part consisting of chronicle hooks, settings, and storytelling advice to play games with multiple lines, is what I expected to find in a crossover book. But I didn't think it would also include a full chronicle tying all the games into a single story and event/threat prompting their vastly different characters to work together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:53:03-07:00","id":1130325,"title":"","content":"Having an example is a good way to handle it. We had theorized about it by hoping they did a single locale, like Chicago. A plague does it without locking you in a specific area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2017, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:59:28-07:00","id":1130332,"title":"","content":"It is. I hadn't considered it because it seemed more important to address the many many points of intersection between all the lines in specific settings and smaller examples as well as storytelling advice. But having a unified big show of how to handle a mass crossover chronicle should be helpful, and even more so if it's a fun adventure in its own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}